window.FWN_PRODIGIOUSLY_AMAZING_WEAPONSMITH_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_PRODIGIOUSLY_AMAZING_WEAPONSMITH_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2901,"title":"Chapter 2901 - Drift Apart (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Based on Young Master Moying’s protective and overbearing manner, how could he possibly not be angry at all? He even... even asked them not to find trouble with the Sacred Phoenix Race?","Li Moying didn’t bother to explain.","If it was anyone else who dared to hoot in front of him, he naturally would not let that person off so easily.","But Huang Sanbai and the others were Huang Yueli’s clansmen after all. Moreover, if she wanted to soar to the peak of the cultivation path, she definitely could not leave her clan totally.","Since that was so, he could only show his wife’s family mercy.","Li Moying pursed his lips slightly and lifted his right hand.","“Since Huang Yueli isn’t here, let’s leave!”","He finished talking and walked towards the door.","Since she wasn’t here, he wasn’t intending to waste any more time at this place.","The most important thing was to quickly search for her elsewhere!","Li’er was in such a dangerous situation so the sooner he found her, perhaps he might be able to save her!","Cloudy Qilin clan practitioners looked at one another in dismay. But none of them dare to defy his commands hence all of them followed after him.","Seeing their departing figures, Sacred Phoenix Race practitioners were all stunned.","They originally assumed that they would not escape being humiliated by the Cloudy Qilin clan! But whoever knew that these people only struck them down and turned to leave?","Moreover, from that Cloudy Qilin clan’s god grade genius’s intention, he wasn’t intending to pick on Sacred Phoenix Race? Why did he do that? Was there something wrong with him?","Huang Sanbai totally didn’t hear what Li Moying said before he left.","At this very moment, he was consumed by humiliation and rage. All he wanted was to dig a hole and hide into it, like an ostrich!","He... a Dao Profound Realm mid-phase practitioner, defeated at the hands of a twenty over year old junior! Moreover, it was right in front of so many clansmen!","That junior had subdued a Qilin and caught him unaware. There were a lot of chances but this wasn’t the most humiliating part!","Huang Sanbai flushed with anger and his gaze was exceptionally cold. “Cloudy Qilin clan’s brat... how dare you! Since you insulted me in such a manner, don’t blame me for being rude to you! I will definitely crush you, the so-called god grade genius, and ensure that you will never be able to rise in power!”","He didn’t think that he was the one who maligned Li Moying first. That was why he met with the other party’s counterattack. Instead, he pushed all the blame onto Li Moying.","It also became reasonable for him to malign Li Moying for attempting to murder Huang Yueli.","That brat was disrespectful to him first, so he had no choice but to do this!","...","Whereas for Li Moying, he had already left the mayor’s manor. Leading the guards, they left Serene Rain Town.","“Young Master Moying, we... where are we heading to now?” The leader of the guards chased after Li Moying quickly and asked cautiously.","Li Moying’s speed was simply too fast. Even though they were well-trained, they couldn’t catch up to him at all!","Li Moying’s anxious and frustrated emotions were totally unconcealable, which was different from his usual cold, aloof, and emotionless image.","He stopped in his tracks and spat out two words, “Find her!”","“Find her?” The guards were stunned and asked, “Find who? That Sacred Phoenix Race’s god grade genius?”","Li Moying didn’t reply, but his speed became even faster!","The guards started to display their body movement Profound Skills and barely managed to chase up to him."]},{"number":2902,"title":"Chapter 2902 - Drift Apart (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Serene Rain Town had several exits and there were guards stationed there to interrogate all the crowds who were entering or leaving the town.","But Li Moying and the others were wearing the Cloudy Qilin clan’s totem. When they saw the high and mighty ancient God clan, the guards wouldn’t dare to stop them, even if they were bold enough.","The group of them left the city gates without a hitch and Li Moying finally stopped. He turned around and instructed, “Even the Sacred Phoenix Race people don’t know where Huang Yueli had gone to. The possibility of her meeting with a fatal danger is extremely high...”","Huang Sanbai claimed that she was attacked by the Cloudy Qilin clan hence she went missing. Although Li Moying doubted his words, it didn’t come across his mind that Huang Sanbai was guilty.","He was making a wild guess and wondered which mysterious force in God Realm had intentionally chosen this moment to strike, just so to incite the feud between the two clans.","But Sacred Phoenix Race’s practitioners had a deep prejudice against the Cloudy Qilin clan. So even if he wanted to explain, the other party wasn’t interested to listen at all.","Hence, they could only depend on themselves to search for her and analyze all the clues that they had got.","He muttered irresolutely to himself for some time, then he spoke up. “Since the Sacred Phoenix Race had been searching in Serene Rain Town, that meant that the location where Huang Yueli had gone missing was not far from Serene Rain Town. Moreover, this town is a necessary path from Soul Connection Ocean to Sacred Phoenix Continent. Even if she wanted to go to the neighboring small towns, it is necessary to pass through this place. Since we can’t find her in this small town, the biggest possibility is that Huang Yueli had gone missing in between the Soul Connection Ocean and Serene Rain Town...”","It wasn’t difficult to come to this conclusion.","Li Moying had come to God Realm for a year and he understood God Realm’s comprehensive topography.","Soul Connection Ocean was a terrain on the verge of God Realm and in between this place to Serene Rain Town, there was an extremely vast barren land. There was only one narrow channel that allowed the practitioners to pass through.","Whereas in this vast barren land, there were very few traces of humans and the topography was extremely complex. There was also a huge quantity of Spirit Beasts prowling around. Even Dao Profound Realm practitioners wouldn’t dare to enter that place so easily, not to mention Lower Realm practitioners who had just ascended.","But if one were to leave the channel and enter into the barren land, that practically meant that it was impossible to leave that place alive!","If that mysterious force wanted to deal with Sacred Phoenix Race’s god grade genius, luring them into the barren land was the easiest choice to make...","Li Moying thought over this briefly and quickly made the arrangements. “There isn’t any time to waste. All of you will split up into two teams and interrogate those small towns by the side. You cannot miss out on any towns which are near Soul Connection Ocean! Tian Yi, Tian Er, you two will follow me to the barren lands to search for her!”","The guards originally stood respectfully beside Li Moying and listened to his instructions.","But upon hearing the fact that he was preparing to enter the barren land, everyone lifted their heads in shock.","Even Tian Yi and Tian Er, who was leading the team, couldn’t help but speak out to stop him!","“Young Master Moying, you... you really... must you go into the barren land? But the barren land is simply too dangerous. Even the Elders in the clan don’t dare to enter it easily. Please reconsider your decision!”","“That’s right, Young Master. The Sacred Phoenix Race’s god grade genius is missing but they don’t even dare to go into the barren land to search for her. Why must you go on their behalf? Frankly speaking, their affairs have nothing to do with you! Even if that god grade genius died accidentally, it has nothing to do with the Cloudy Qilin clan. Perhaps, it might even be a great thing...”","“Shut up!”","Tian Er was speaking non-stop when he heard his Young Lord bark sharply!","He shivered and hurriedly shut his mouth."]},{"number":2903,"title":"Chapter 2903 - Drift Apart (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Lifting his head, he saw a bitter, cold glint in Li Moying’s profound peach-blossomed eyes!","That eerie cold glint was like a dagger that stabbed deep into his body.","Li Tian Er’s knees went weak and he immediately knelt on the ground. “Young... Young Master... This Subordinate...”","He had never seen such a terrifying expression on Li Moying and instantly shivered with fright. But he didn’t understand what he said wrongly at all.","Every single time the Sacred Phoenix Race was to run into bad luck, the clansmen would gloat over their misfortunes and no one felt that there was anything wrong about this.","Li Moying swept a glance at him and his thin lips moved slightly. “The Sacred Phoenix Race’s missing god grade genius... is This Young Lord’s wife in the Lower Realm!”","“Wh... What??”","His sentence was much more terrifying than the heavenly thunder.","All the guards seemed as though they had been struck by lightning. They looked at him in a daze, and couldn’t recollect their senses for a long time.","Li Moying’s expression was still icy cold. “Li’er is Your Lady so don’t let me hear anyone speaking ill of her one more time! If we can’t find her, I will not return to Cloudy Qilin Continent!”","By now, Li Tian Yi had already calmed down a little. He stammered and said, “Young... Young Master, are you... you’re not joking right?”","“Y...Yes, this matter... you can’t make a joke out of it casually!”","“Really... I was almost scared to death! So it’s just a joke? I say...”","Quivering voices started to ring.","However, Li Moying merely said coldly, “Does This Young Master look as if I’m joking with you? This is as real as it can be! But no one is allowed to spread the word at all! Otherwise... This Young Master will make that person’s life into a living hell!”","The guards trembled and hurriedly said that they wouldn’t dare to!","In reality, they indeed didn’t dare to defy Li Moying’s orders. They were assigned to be his subordinate and even if someone was initially not convinced, it had been over a year. So everyone had witnessed Li Moying’s shocking innate talent, courage, and insight. So all of them were won over by him!","Now, they had truly served their allegiance to Li Moying and not to Cloudy Qilin clan!","No one dared to betray him, nor would they possibly do so!","But, they still felt that this was extremely unrealistic. No matter how they thought about it, it seemed as though they were still dreaming!","What joke was this?","In the past ten thousand years in God Realm, the first two god grade genius that had ascended from the Lower Realm were actually a couple??","Moreover, their Cloudy Qilin clan’s pride, Young Master Moying who had swept many women off their feet, was married at such a tender age?? He even married a young lady from their mortal enemy, the Sacred Phoenix Race??","Even those storytellers on the streets wouldn’t dare to make up a story like this!","Just as everyone was still in a daze, Li Moying had already repeated his arrangements. Lastly, he added, “We’ll do this for the next two months. If we’re still unable to find her by then, all of us will gather at Sacred Phoenix Continent two months later. By then, we’ll try to find other ways to look for her! Alright, grab hold of time, and let’s move out!”","“Yes, This Subordinate understands!”","The guards cried out in unison and split up.","But everyone still felt as though they were in a dream.","Sacred Phoenix Race’s god grade genius was their Young Master Moying’s wife...","Today’s dream was too shocking and too frightening... how they wished that they could wake up from this quickly...","Li Moying utilized his body movements Profound Skill and led Li Tian Yi and Li Tian Er towards the perilous barren land."]},{"number":2904,"title":"Chapter 2904 - Drift Apart (4)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Li Moying had never imagined that by doing so, he would be drifting further and further away from Huang Yueli!","For close to a month, Huang Yueli had been in disguise. She passed through all the small and large channels in God Realm and made her way hastily towards Sacred Phoenix Continent. She had passed through dozens of towns.","In the first two weeks, her journey had been extremely smooth sailing. She didn’t meet with a single Sacred Phoenix Race practitioner at all.","But after some time, Huang Yueli realized that Sacred Phoenix Race practitioners started to appear in the streets and alleys.","Originally, she thought that it was because she was coming nearer to the Sacred Phoenix Continent.","But once, she passed by a large town and saw her picture posted on the city wall.","This made Huang Yueli instantly realize what was going on!","It seemed that everything was not a coincidence. Huang Sanbai realized that he could not find her in Serene Rain Town, so he had no choice but to report her disappearance to the clan...","“But, this is still a little strange! Isn’t Huang Sanbai afraid of being punished by the clan leader if he reported this? Or was it because Huang Sanbai’s forces in Sacred Phoenix Race had already reached this extent?” Huang Yueli frowned with puzzlement.","She naturally hadn’t imagined that Huang Sanbai had already turned Li Moying into his scapegoat.","But because of this, Huang Yueli had overestimated Huang Sanbai’s position in the clan. So all the more she didn’t dare to return to Ice Moon Summit.","After a month of her tough journey, Huang Yueli finally arrived at the Sacred Phoenix Continent, one of the twelve Continents where the Sacred Phoenix Race reigned power in!","Standing underneath the city gate, she lifted her head and took a look. Any newly ascended Lower Realm practitioners would be awed by this majestic city!","The Sacred Phoenix Continent was surrounded by mountains and had the most dangerous topography among all the continents. The surrounding walls were extremely solid.","Underneath the city walls were numerous God Realm practitioners holding Spirit Armaments, surrounding and protecting the Sacred Phoenix Continent.","Those practitioners who were entering and leaving the city gate instantly felt how insignificant they were. They didn’t even dare to speak loudly and formed into a line. They queued up to pay the entrance fees into the city.","“Ten medium grade crystal jades!”","Huang Yueli obediently retrieved ten medium grade crystal jades from her interspatial ring and was just about to hand it over.","Suddenly, a voice rang from the side. “Wait! This person seems to be an ascender from the Lower Realm! Let me take a look!”","A Sacred Phoenix Race practitioner held a painting in his hand and looked at Huang Yueli.","She stood there emotionlessly and allowed him to check her out.","“He doesn’t look quite like... Lad, what’s your name? Which Continent did you come from?” The Sacred Phoenix Race practitioner asked after he looked at her.","Huang Yueli had already memorized her fake identity and casually replied a few words. Then she passed through the checkpoint with flying colors.","After she ventured into the Sacred Phoenix Continent, the first thing Huang Yueli did was to find a teahouse to have a rest.","Previously when she was in the small towns, the practitioners’ ability wasn’t considered as ridiculously strong. There were even a few commoners who had fourth or fifth stage realm cultivation.","But after she entered into a huge continent like the Sacred Phoenix Continent, the situation was completely different.","Every single person that Huang Yueli laid her eyes on, were practically a practitioner in ninth stage realm and above. There were occasionally a few whose cultivations weren’t very high. But they were mostly young people under thirty years old and were from the ordinary human race.","Huang Yueli was now in Dream Profound realm mid-phase cultivation.. If one didn’t look at her age, she really couldn’t be considered as a top exponent at this place."]},{"number":2905,"title":"Chapter 2905 - Sky Gem Glass Chamber (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","“Sir, this is your tea and snacks. Please enjoy!”","The waiter placed the teapot, teacup, and a few plates on the table. Then he nodded to Huang Yueli and left.","Huang Yueli hurriedly called out to him. “Wait! Young brother, can I ask you something?”","As she spoke, she took out a few medium grade crystal jades from her interspatial ring and passed it to the waiter.","The waiter originally felt that she was a Lower Realm ascender so he wasn’t very willing to talk to her. In the end, when he saw her so shrewd and offered some tips, a broad smile immediately appeared on his face.","“Sir, what do you wish to know? Feel free to ask! Although my cultivation isn’t very high, I’m born in Sacred Phoenix Continent and grew up around here. So I know almost everything in Sacred Phoenix Continent!”","Huang Yueli nodded her head. “That’s great! Let me ask you, how many teleportation arrays does Sacred Phoenix Continent have? Which continents do they lead to? If I want to go to Cloudy Qilin Continent, which way should I take?”","When the waiter heard that, he instantly grew anxious and kept looking around to the left and right. After he verified that there wasn’t anyone in the surroundings, he heaved a sigh of relief.","“I say, Sir, you’ve just ascended from the Lower Realm. No wonder you don’t know that you shouldn’t be saying this so carelessly here! We Sacred Phoenix Continent are on Sacred Phoenix Race’s turf. Sacred Phoenix Race had always been on loggerheads with Cloudy Qilin clan. If anyone were to hear you talking about Cloudy Qilin clan here, you might get into trouble! Moreover, a Lower Realm ascender like you doesn’t look like an ancient God clan, isn’t it? Why are you going so far away for? Are you intending to join one of the big forces?”","Huang Yueli blinked and looked at the waiter’s anxious look. She felt rather speechless about this.","She didn’t expect that even mentioning Cloudy Qilin clan’s name was not allowed on Sacred Phoenix Race’s turf!","Would it be the same over at Cloudy Qilin clan’s side?","In that case, when she reached Cloudy Qilin Continent, she had to conceal her identity very well. Otherwise, there would be big trouble...","Her thoughts raced past swiftly, and an enlightened expression appeared on her face. “I see, thank you, Young brother, for your pointer! Actually, I don’t have to join Cloudy... that whatever clan. I just happened to hear of them when I was in the Lower Realm so I thought of going over to take a look... Speaking of this, a Lower Realm practitioner like me doesn’t have any power or status. My ability is also so ordinary, so it should be very difficult to join a large force, right?”","The waiter took a look at her and rubbed his chin. “Speaking of this, you don’t look very old. But since you’re able to ascend to God Realm, your innate talent is much stronger than mine! Why don’t you find a place in Sacred Phoenix Continent to settle down instead? It probably wouldn’t be possible to join the Sacred Phoenix Race but there is plenty of second-rate or third-rate forces in Sacred Phoenix Continent. They also hold a considerable amount of resources. At least, it’s something beyond your imagination for people like you from the Lower Realm!”","In order to conceal her identity, Huang Yueli intentionally disguised herself to be slightly older. She even stuck a mustache on her upper lips.","The current her looked like a slim and comely young man around thirty years old.","Adding on to the fact that she intentionally suppressed her cultivation to look as though she had just broken through to the tenth stage realm, most ordinary practitioners would feel that she was a human race practitioner with human grade innate talent.","Among the Lower Realm ascenders, that innate talent was not too eye-catching.","Hearing what the waiter said, Huang Yueli nodded her head.. “I also think so! But I’ve just arrived in God Realm, so I was thinking of traveling around first to find out about the situation, then decide on which force to join. So, Young brother, can you tell me the situation about the teleportation array in the city...”"]},{"number":2906,"title":"Chapter 2906 - Sky Gem Glass Chamber (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Huang Yueli brought the topic up again.","The waiter frowned and was slightly surprised. “What? You’re still thinking about that teleportation array?”","He leaned a little closer and spoke softly, “To tell you the truth, the position of the teleportation array isn’t hard to find because every block of teleportation array is extravagantly built. Even from afar, you will be able to see it, and would not mistake it for something else!”","Huang Yueli smiled. “That’s great!”","“Great? Great my foot!” The waiter stared at her. “Did you think that that teleportation array belongs to your family? Can you stop dreaming? Do you know how much it costs to activate the teleportation array each time? At least ten thousand high grade crystal jades! Moreover, no matter how much money ordinary people have, don’t assume that Sacred Phoenix Race will definitely activate it for them. One has to verify that they are of a certain status first! Otherwise, why would they show you this face to do this service for you? Huh?”","The waiter suddenly got agitated and blurted out endlessly, his saliva splattering everywhere!","However, when he turned back to take a look, he realized that she wasn’t looking at him at all. Instead, her head tilted to one side and she was looking downstairs from the second floor of the teahouse.","The waiter coughed in displeasure. “Hey, are you listening to me or not? I’m telling you so much out of good intentions! If you don’t listen to my advice, don’t blame me for not reminding you when you get thrown out by them!”","But Huang Yueli was still looking downstairs attentively so she didn’t say a word.","The waiter found it a little strange and leaned closer. “What are you looking at?”","He walked to the railing, took a look downstairs, and said, “Oh!”","“So you’re looking at this... that’s true. Sky Gem Glass Chamber’s Grandmaster Xiao actually passed by this place. This isn’t something that happens every day...”","Downstairs the teahouse on the streets, a luxurious carriage slowly steered by.","The pedestrians on the streets saw the carriage and everyone shot a revered look in the carriage’s direction.","Several guests were secretly discussing this. One could tell from their conversation that it was full of envy and admiration.","“Why has Grandmaster Xiao come over to our district today?”","“Who knows? But I’m guessing that it should be a Dao Profound Realm top exponent who could invite Grandmaster Xiao over? Perhaps, it might be a large force from Sacred Phoenix Continent!”","“Sigh, I envy Grandmaster Xiao so much. He is so sought after, no matter where he goes...”","“There’s nothing to envy about! If you want to become a Spiritual Armament Master, you have to be extremely strict on yourself. Moreover, Grandmaster Xiao is Sacred Phoenix Continent’s top rated Sky Gem Grandmaster! As for you, it’s better to stop dreaming...”","Huang Yueli heard the noise and suddenly thought of something. Then she turned around and asked the waiter, “Young brother, the carriage downstairs... is he a Sky Gem Grandmaster?”","The waiter retracted his gaze and turned to look at Huang Yueli. He said disdainfully, “I didn’t expect a Lower Realm ascender to know about the Sky Gem Grandmaster as well?”","Huang Yueli didn’t bother about his tone. In her memories, she recalled the things that Huang Zixiao told her when she was undergoing the refinement in the inheritance tower. She muttered to herself, “An Armament Master who can refine Treasure Armaments are known as Sky Gem Grandmasters in God Realm. Their statuses are extremely revered... then what is the Sky Gem Glass Chamber?”","The waiter snorted and explained gleefully, “I thought you know everything! But in the end, don’t you still have to ask me? This Sky Gem Glass Chamber is an organization formed by God Realm’s Armament Masters. It’s equivalent to... your Lower Realm’s so-called Guild?”"]},{"number":2907,"title":"Chapter 2907 - Sky Gem Glass Chamber (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","“But Sky Gem Glass Chamber is a major force that is independent of the Twelve Continents. No matter if it is in terms of inheritance, it’s status in history, it does not pale in comparison to the ancient God clans. Although they can’t compete in terms of power, all the large clans still fight to fawn over the Sky Gem Glass Chamber!”","Hearing the waiter’s explanation, Huang Yueli nodded her head pensively.","In the past, Huang Zixiao also told her that God Realm’s top tier Holy Armament was something that only Life Profound Realm practitioners could refine. One’s inherent fated blood essence was one of the materials, and that Armament Master could only refine one piece in their entire lives.","This thing was something that ordinary practitioners could forget about going. Even if it was Dao Profound Realm’s top exponents, it was impossible to obtain one as well.","So all the large forces scrambled to fawn on Sky Gem Grandmasters.","The waiter coughed again. “What do you think? Now, do you know what kind of status does a Sky Gem Grandmaster holds?”","Huang Yueli nodded to show that she had gained some insight and hurriedly asked, “Then, for a Sky Gem Grandmaster like Grandmaster Xiao, is his status high enough? Does he have the right to use Sacred Phoenix Continent’s teleportation array?”","The waiter scoffed, “Isn’t that obvious? Sky Gem Grandmaster! What kind of status do you think that is? Even the Castellan of our Flame Square City has to bow down to him!”","“I see...” Huang Yueli muttered to herself irresolutely.","She roughly understood God Realm’s situation from reading the <<Overview of God Realm>>.","She knew that in each Continent, it would generally be demarcated into more than ten different cities, and those would be managed by various God clans’ higher management.","Taking the Flame Square City that she was in right now, the Castellan was an important branch family lord among the Sacred Phoenix Race’s descendants. In the clan, his status was on par with ordinary Elders. But if compared with Huang Sanbai, he was on a lower level.","For someone like this, he would be considered as a big shot in God Realm. However, a Sky Gem Grandmaster’s status was actually on par with the Castellan...","The waiter added, “Let’s stop talking about the Sky Gem Grandmaster. As long as a Spiritual Armament Master can refine a Spirit Armament, that person would be able to join the Sky Gem Glass Chamber as a junior member. He will also be entitled to use the teleportation array! Moreover, a Spiritual Armament Master’s income is also an imaginable amount. Ten thousand high grade crystal jades are nothing to them!”","Hearing that, Huang Yueli’s lips couldn’t help but curl upwards!","Originally she was still worried about how to earn enough money to go to Cloudy Qilin Continent.","Now, the waiter had supplied her with a good train of thought...","If she could join the Sky Gem Glass Chamber and become a Spiritual Armament Master, then the problems that she faced now would all be resolved!","Huang Yueli quickly made a decision and turned around to ask, “Young brother, do you know where is the branch office of the Sky Gem Glass Chamber in Sacred Phoenix Continent? Which way should I go?”","“What? What did you just say?”","The surroundings were rather noisy and the waiter thought that he had heard wrongly!","Huang Yueli could only repeat her question one more time.","The waiter’s eyes widened as he looked at her in astonishment. He thought that he was developing hallucinations!","“What? Are you alright? You’re asking me how to go to the Sky Gem Glass Chamber? What do you want to do?”","He thought of the things that Huang Yueli said and an astonishing conclusion surfaced in his mind.","“Wait, don’t tell me that you’re intending to join the Sky Gem Glass Chamber, and later use that identity to request to use the teleportation array?? Haven’t you woken up from your dream yet!”"]},{"number":2908,"title":"Chapter 2908 - Sky Gem Glass Chamber (4)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Huang Yueli frowned slightly, feeling displeased in her heart.","No one in Soaring Heavens Continent dared to talk to her in this way.","But now in God Realm, she had to conceal her identity and had to do everything in a low-key fashion. So she could only endure with this.","Huang Yueli took out another two pieces of medium grade crystal jades and placed them on the table.","“Are you going to tell me the way to Sky Gem Glass Chamber or not? If you don’t wish to do so, I’m going to ask someone else! I believe that there are plenty of people who know the way around here!”","It wasn’t just plenty!","Other than newbies like Huang Yueli, who was here for the first time, who wouldn’t know the way to such an iconic place?","When the waiter saw the crystal jades, he kept staring at it and hurriedly laughed it off. “Sir, why are you so impatient? I didn’t say that I don’t know! Sky Gem Glass Chamber’s branch can be found in the bigger city-states and there’s one here in Flame Square City as well. It’s located in the southeast part of the city. Just walk straight along this street to the end and you will reach that place...”","After Huang Yueli heard that, she tossed the two medium grade crystal jades to the waiter, then turned around and left.","The waiter held the crystal jades in his hand and looked at her departing figure. Then he sneered disdainfully.","“These Lower Realm ascenders are so amusing! Did they think that they had refined a few broken Profound Armaments in the Lower Realm and they can become out God Realm’s Spiritual Armament Masters? How dare he even have the cheek to ask the way to the Sky Gem Glass Chamber? Simply overestimating his abilities! He even dares to throw his temper?”","“Forget it, if he wants to go, just go! The people in the Sky Gem Glass Chamber are not easy-going people. When they see such a dumba*s who is so arrogant, they would absolutely show him some colors! By then, it’d be too late for him to cry! Anyway, it has nothing to do with me!”","The waiter picked up the crystal jades and hummed a tune as he walked into the teahouse.","As for Huang Yueli, she followed the waiter’s direction and walked along the street in front. Shortly after, she saw a special eye-catching building.","It was indeed like what the waiter said. Anyone could recognize it from far away.","There weren’t any guards stationed at the entrance of the Sky Gem Glass Chamber but no one dared to barge in.","Huang Yueli had some knowledge of God Realm’s arrays and knew that it was because there were many special arrays set up at the entrance. For those who couldn’t see through this, all they could see was the walls around the Sky Gem Glass Chamber, even if they went an entire round. They wouldn’t be able to find the main entrance at all.","Huang Yueli observed from the side for a little while and had already understood the way for her to enter.","She started to walk, preparing to head over.","Suddenly, she heard a sharp series of horseshoe sounds and there was even someone shouting in a high-pitch voice, “Move aside, move aside! All of you, get out of the way! A respectable Spiritual Armament Maser is going to Sky Gem Glass Chamber. All the outsiders should quickly get out of the way!”","Immediately following that, a horse carriage raced swiftly on the streets!","That person who spoke was very impolite, but the pedestrians on the streets didn’t show any dissatisfaction at all. Everyone hurriedly moved to the side.","The person in the carriage was a Spiritual Armament Master!","Even if it was just a junior Spiritual Armament Master, that person was someone that ordinary people could not afford to offend!","The carriage stopped right in front of the Sky Gem Glass Chamber. The curtains were lifted, and a young lady walked down slowly from the carriage.","She wore a hat, and a long muslin cloth dropped down and covered the top half of her face.. The faintly discernible look was very unclear, but just based on her sharp chin, fair complexion, and that curvy side view, one could tell that she was an extremely attractive and beautiful woman."]},{"number":2909,"title":"Chapter 2909 - Sky Gem Glass Chamber (5)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","A burst of praises was heard among the bystanders.","A respectable and beautiful female Spiritual Armament Master was rarely seen in Flame Square City.","The female Spiritual Armament Master didn’t turn back but walked right into the Sky Gem Glass Chamber.","Huang Yueli followed behind closely and walked into the main door.","The Sky Gem Glass Chamber’s interior was luxuriously decorated. There were various large and small mechanisms and arrays that were set up everywhere, which made the entire building shine in splendor.","When she walked in, the female Spiritual Armament Master had already taken down the hat which she wore, revealing her face. As expected, she was indeed a gorgeous beauty.","This round, everyone in the main hall was excited and all of them crowded around her to fawn on her.","“Young Miss, are you a Spiritual Armament Master? Such an outstanding person like you came to visit our Flame Square City’s Sky Gem Glass Chamber, we are honored by your presence!”","“This Young Miss, are you here at the Sky Gem Glass Chamber to look for armament refining materials, or do you have any incomprehensible queries? Feel free to look for me! I am rather famous among the Spiritual Armament Masters in Flame Square City. No one knows the situation here better than me!”","“Move aside! I’m the one who is the most outstanding Spiritual Armament Master in Flame Square City...”","To fight for the beauty’s attention, all the young Spiritual Armament Masters were about to exchange blows!","She raised her hand and showed a badge in her hands.","When they saw the badge, those originally noisy Spiritual Armament Masters instantly clammed their mouths shut.","Because the badge that this beautiful woman brought out reflected the status of a high ranking Spiritual Armament Master!","Her armament refining standard was even higher than most male Spiritual Armament Masters present! They even claimed that they would help her solve her difficulties...","The beautiful woman didn’t even need to say a word to subdue all the people present.","They went silent for a moment and quickly crowded around her and started to laud her accomplishments.","But these had nothing much to do with Huang Yueli at all.","She swept a glance at the beautiful woman and shifted her eyes away.","Since no one was paying any attention to her, she could take this chance to check out the Sky Gem Glass Chamber’s interior.","The main hall was closest to the main door and it should be a reception area. Although there weren’t many people entering or leaving the building, every single person was luxuriously dressed. Their expressions were haughty and they wore special badges on their clothes. She believed that they were members of the Sky Gem Glass Chamber.","There were several doors behind the back of the main hall. Some doors were tightly shut and she couldn’t see what was behind them.","Two doors were open wide. One room was filled with various kinds of big or small armament furnaces and armament refining materials while the other room was filled with books. It looked like a book depository.","Huang Yueli pondered for a moment and was just about to walk into the Book Depository when someone suddenly called her.","“Wait! That lad over there!”","Huang Yueli was stunned and turned around.","The Spiritual Armament Masters who were crowded around the beauty suddenly noticed Huang Yueli’s presence. He immediately walked over and interrogated her loudly.","“Who are you? How did you come in? Do you know what place is the Sky Gem Glass Chamber? How dare you wander about on your own?”","Huang Yueli wasn’t nervous as she replied in neither overbearing nor servile manner.. “I walked in front through the main door. Why? Is there a problem with that? The Sky Gem Glass Chamber’s door is wide open, and it didn’t say that no one is allowed to come in, isn’t it?”"]},{"number":2910,"title":"Chapter 2910 - Quit While You’re Ahead (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","The young Spiritual Armament Master who questioned her was speechless.","Sky Gem Glass Chamber indeed did not stop outsiders from entering the place. However, outsiders usually didn’t have the ability to come in at all!","After Huang Yueli said that, he didn’t know how to retort at all.","After a while later, he came back to his senses and hurriedly said, “Then... then surely you can’t just barge into the other places recklessly in this manner right? After you entered the place, don’t you know how to find someone to ask? Where are your manners?”","Huang Yueli merely swept him a glance. “I wanted to find someone to ask but weren’t all of you busy? None of you were free to entertain me. So I thought I shouldn’t bother you guys!”","“Don’t spout rubbish, we...” The Spiritual Armament Master wanted to rebuke but he saw the beautiful Spiritual Armament Master from the corner of his eye and his anger immediately subsided.","He was the admission staff on duty today but because of a beautiful woman, he had neglected his duties. If the Branch President saw this, he would definitely be scolded.","Thinking of this, he gave a hurried cough and said, “Ughh, right, we were a little busy earlier! Why didn’t you come over to remind me about this? Alright, come over here to proceed with the registration!”","He quickly went back to his seat and indicated for Huang Yueli to go over.","It so happened that she also had some questions to ask, hence she walked over directly.","“What’s your name? You’re not someone from our Flame Square City, right?”","Huang Yueli nodded and said, “That’s right, I am...” She registered herself using that fake identity once again.","The admission staff instantly revealed a shocked expression. “What? You’re a Lower Realm ascender!! Right, from your dressing, you indeed do look like one. But... but since you’re just ascended, how could you... how could you possibly enter our Sky Gem Glass Chamber? Has someone taught you the way before this?”","Huang Yueli replied calmly, “The mechanism and array at the entrance aren’t very difficult, so why do you think I can’t come in?”","“Not... not considered difficult? Are you joking?” The Spiritual Armament Master’s eyes widened in shock, as he looked at Huang Yueli in disbelief. “To a genuine Spiritual Armament Master, that array is the basics for starters! But you’re not a Spiritual Armament Master, right?”","Huang Yueli replied nonchalantly, “although I am not God Realm’s Spiritual Armament Master, we do have Armament Masters in our Golden Ray Continent. In the past when I was in the Lower Realm, I was well versed in this, so the array and mechanisms at the entrance isn’t a problem for me!”","“But...” The Spiritual Armament Master frowned, as his mind was full of puzzlement.","There were indeed Armament Masters in the Lower Realm but refining ordinary Profound Armaments and refining Spirit or Treasure Armaments were completely two different matters!","The principle of armament refining was different, not to mention that to become a Spiritual Armament Master, the requirement for the practitioner’s innate talent was very high. It wasn’t something that ordinary Armament Masters could compare with!","For so many years, there had been so many ascended Armament Masters who wanted to learn the art of refining Spirit Armaments. But in the end, only a handful of them succeeded.","This was the first time he came across someone like Huang Yueli, who came alone to the Sky Gem Glass Chamber, without anyone’s help.","If what this lad said was true, wouldn’t that mean that his innate talent in armament refining was ridiculously high?","The admission Spiritual Armament Master was stunned, not daring to believe that such a thing would happen.","However, Huang Yueli got a little impatient. When she saw him keeping quiet, she opened her mouth and asked, “I came to the Sky Gem Glass Chamber to find out if there’s any way which can allow me to become a Spiritual Armament Master as soon as possible?”"]},{"number":2911,"title":"Chapter 2911 - Quit While You’re Ahead (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","The Spiritual Armament Master came back to his senses and said, “I knew you were going to ask about this! Most practitioners who want to become Spiritual Armament Masters would bring their Masters along. Otherwise, they wouldn’t even be able to enter the Sky Gem Glass Chamber! You’re pretty lucky. As a Lower Realm ascender, you came in on your own without any Master! This is the first time I came across something like this...”","When Huang Yueli heard that, she frowned. “What? If I don’t have a Master, that means I can’t become a Spiritual Armament Master?”","“That’s not necessarily so as well,” the admission Spiritual Armament Master thought for a moment and said, “Even if you don’t have a Master, you can still take part in the simple assessments in the Sky Gem Glass Chamber first. As long as we have confirmed your Spiritual Armament Master innate talent, you will be able to become a Spiritual Armament apprentice. The apprentice has a total of nine grades and that will allow you to learn all the basic knowledge systemically. After you have become a ninth grade apprentice, you must refine a low grade Spirit Armament before you can officially become a Spiritual Armament Master.”","Hearing this, Huang Yueli instantly felt that something was amiss.","“Are there nine grades to an apprentice grade? How much time is required to pass through all the assessments?”","The admission officer said, “This... the time depends on each person’s innate talent! Seeing that you can enter Sky Gem Glass Chamber on your own, I believe that your comprehension isn’t too bad. You should be able to pass one grade every year. In this case, you’d probably take around ten years to become a ninth grade apprentice!”","Huang Yueli’s lips twitched uncontrollably. “Ten... ten years?”","Where would she find so much time to take part in the assessments!","She couldn’t wait to immediately become a Spiritual Armament Master and fly over to look for Li Moying!","However, the admission officer wasn’t done talking yet.","“That’s right. But don’t be too happy first. Although passing the apprentice assessments isn’t difficult, the crux to becoming a Spiritual Armament Master means you will have to refine a genuine Spirit Armament. Not a standard grade Spirit Armament, but a low grade Spirit Armament! Many people would spend more than ten years just at this step.”","Hearing that, Huang Yueli suddenly thought of something as a ray of hope suddenly arose in her heart.","“Then in this case, if I can refine a low grade Spirit Armament immediately, wouldn’t that mean that I can directly become a Spiritual Armament Master? So I wouldn’t need to attend those apprentice assessments?”","The admission officer was still talking non-stop because it was rare that a Lower Realm ascender who didn’t know anything would head over. Hence he could show off his eloquence.","Whoever knew that in the middle of his explanation, Huang Yueli interrupted him in this way so he was completely dazed.","“You... what did you just say??” He thought that he had heard her wrongly!","Huang Yueli repeated what she just said and the admission officer’s gaze seemed as though he was looking at an idiot!","“You can’t even pass the apprentice assessments, so how are you going to refine a Spirit Armament? Did you really think that you are a peerless genius? Looks like you must be a famous Armament Master in your Lower Realm! But if you think that it’s the same in God Realm, you must be daydreaming! You simply don’t know how high the heavens are!”","To think that it was a waste of his time telling her so much, he did not expect her to be a lunatic who overestimated herself!","The admission officer looked at Huang Yueli disdainfully.","She didn’t bother about what he said, but only wanted to find out the answer. “So, can it be done or not?”","The admission officer almost spat out a mouthful of blood!","After such a long time, this fellow wasn’t even listening to what he said!"]},{"number":2912,"title":"Chapter 2912 - Quit While You’re Ahead (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","The admission officer sneered. “Yes, of course, you can! If you have the ability to refine a Spirit Armament directly! In our line of work, there are so many principles that haven’t been used. So if someone can refine a Spirit Armament, that means that person has the fundamentals! If you have such capability, who wouldn’t acknowledge it?”","Huang Yueli nodded her head satisfactorily when she heard the answer and heaved a sigh of relief.","Luckily, the Sky Gem Glass Chamber’s rules weren’t a stick in the mud!","If they insisted for one to pass through all ninth grade apprentice assessments before proceeding with the Spiritual Armament Master certification, then she could only give up on this.","After all, the reason why she wanted to become a Spiritual Armament Master was mainly that she wanted to obtain a sufficiently high status to mobilize various Continent’s teleportation arrays.","Otherwise, she didn’t place too much emphasis on this meaningless title.","If she really had to spend eight or ten years, she might save even more time if she traveled by foot to Cloudy Qilin Continent!","She thought about it and asked again, “Then where can I find books related to refining Spirit Armaments? I’ve visited a few book stores but I couldn’t find any at all.”","The admission officer stared at her and he was totally at a loss for words!","This fellow didn’t even know where to find the Spirit Armament refining books meant that she didn’t even know the basics of Spirit Armament refining! Did he thought that he could skip over the apprentice assessments and directly refine a Spirit Armament?","He gave a cold harrumph and said, “It’s obvious that Spirit Armament refining books can’t be found in ordinary book stores! Since you don’t have a Master, then you can only purchase from the Sky Gem Glass Chamber! High grade manuals are exchanged with contribution points. But since you’re only looking at entry-level books, you just need to be a Spiritual Armament apprentice to purchase it!”","Huang Yueli’s eyes lit up upon hearing that. “That’s great! How can I become an apprentice?”","The admission officer shot a glance at her. “As long as your innate talent is high enough, you can be one. Follow me!”","Huang Yueli followed him into a small room and there was an elderly man with silvery-white hair. His head was bent down as he was carefully handling the materials in his hands.","“Senior Bai, there’s a newbie here who wants to assess his innate talent.”","Hearing the admission officer’s voice, he barely lifted his head and said, “Alright, go over there for assessment!”","The Spiritual Armament apprentice innate testing was extremely simple.","The admission officer brought Huang Yueli over to the corner where a crystal machine was and indicated for her to place her hand on it.","Huang Yueli could tell that this was a standard innate talent assessment, which was the same as what she saw in the inheritance tower in the past.","But the one in the inheritance tower was solely testing innate talent whereas the one in front tested fire and metal dual attributes.","Huang Yueli intentionally restrained the Profound Energy in her body and slowly released fire and metal attributed Profound Energies while observing the admin officer’s expression.","Fire and metal attributed energies slowly ascended in the crystal columns.","Initially, the admission officer’s face had a slight hint of disdain. He was still upset over what Huang Yueli had said earlier.","But as the column raised to a certain standard, his expression slowly turned solemn. In the end, he even revealed a slight hint of astonishment.","When Huang Yueli saw this, she immediately quit while she was ahead and retracted the remaining Profound Energy.","She didn’t want to expose her true ability, but yet didn’t want him to look down on her.","So the most suitable time to stop was when the Spiritual Armament Masters looked a little surprised, but not at the rate where they would be shocked."]},{"number":2913,"title":"Chapter 2913 - Quit While You’re Ahead (4)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","As expected, the admission officer’s surprised look only lasted for a second and he immediately walked up.","“I didn’t expect an ordinary-looking lad like you to have such innate talent! Metal and fire dual attributes are both at earth grade genius level. As long as you can find a good Master, you will be able to become a high ranking Spiritual Armament Master. If you’re lucky enough, you might be able to become a Sky Gem Grandmaster!”","Hearing that, Huang Yueli’s vision swept past the innate talent assessment apparatus.",".... Earth grade lower level genius standard!","This kind of innate talent was considered pretty good in God Realm. Other than disciples from large forces, it was difficult for most ordinary practitioners to reach this level.","It was even rarer for both metal and fire dual attributes to reach earth grade. So no wonder the admission Spiritual Armament Master sounded a little sour as if he was jealous.","Huang Yueli courteously asked, “Oh no, I wouldn’t dare think so far. So in this case, am I considered as an official Spiritual Armament apprentice now?”","The admission officer said, “There’s still the power of comprehension and memory assessments. Come over here!”","The second assessment was to make Huang Yueli read a paragraph of the Armament Refining Encyclopedia, then distribute the materials according to the description she had read.","To Huang Yueli, this was a piece of cake, and she completed it with ease.","When the admission officer saw Huang Yueli’s hands swiftly moving and completed the distribution swiftly, his eyeballs almost dropped on the ground!","A Lower Realm ascender might not even have heard of these materials, but she was able to grasp the method of distribution so quickly!","This power of comprehension... she had simply crushed all the young Spiritual Armament Masters in their Flame Square City branch office.","Huang Yueli put down the materials in her hand and turned to the admission officer. “Alright, what do I have to do next?”","He came to his senses and hurriedly said, “Alright, you’ve done well in these two assessments. After I report this to the Elder, you will become Sky Gem Glass Chamber’s junior Spiritual Armament apprentice!”","The admission officer returned to the room where the elderly man was sitting quietly. He bent down and whispered into the Elder’s ear.","The elderly man originally wasn’t paying any attention but after he heard that, his eyes lit up.","Raiding his head, he beckoned to Huang Yueli. “Lad, come over here!”","Huang Yueli’s brows rose and she listened and walked over.","The elderly man sized Huang Yueli up and down, then said, “You really are a Lower Realm ascender! I didn’t expect you to have such high innate talent, so you are a rough diamond! I appreciate your talent, so you can stay with me from now on!”","The admission officer’s eyes revealed a hint of jealousy when he heard what the elderly man said!","Evidently, from what the elderly man meant, he was intending to take Huang Yueli as his disciple!","This Grandmaster Bai looked very normal but he was one of the Sky Gem Grandmasters in Flame Square City! So many people wished that he would take interest in them!","Whoever knew, he took fancy to a country bumpkin who ascended from the Lower Realm!","Thinking of this, the admission officer started to regret bringing her over, and the gaze he cast on her was rather unfriendly.","Grandmaster Bai squinted his eyes and waited for Huang Yueli to kneel in ecstasy to pay her greetings to him.","However, she merely went into a blank and waved her hand decisively, “This... this Grandmaster, thank you for your offer, but I’m just passing by Flame Square City.. I have no intention to stay for long, so I won’t be able to learn how to refine Spirit Armaments from you.”"]},{"number":2914,"title":"Chapter 2914 - Replace That Woman (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Grandmaster Bai didn’t expect himself to be rejected. His eyes widened with disbelief.","After a while, the Spiritual Armament Master standing next to him recollected his senses and jumped up in indignance. “You... you lad, how dare you! Do you know who Grandmaster Bai is? He’s a respectable and esteemed Sky Gem Grandmaster! He’s willing to take you, a Lower Realm ascender, who knows nothing as a disciple so it’s your good fortune! Yet you rejected this chance??”","Huang Yueli frowned slightly as her piercing gaze swept past the admission officer!","This God Realm’s Spiritual Armament Master had flaunted all the superiority of God Realm practitioners to the max today, trying to belittle and suppress her with various kinds of remarks.","The Spiritual Armament Master wanted to add on when he abruptly met with Huang Yueli’s gaze. His heart pounded wildly! He couldn’t continue with the rest of his sentence at all!","Not knowing why, Huang Yueli’s gaze made him turn icy cold, as though he was facing a peerless top exponent who was much stronger than him by several times! That kind who could crush him with just one finger!","But wasn’t this fellow just a Lower Realm ascender?","How could he possibly... be so strong?","Just as the Spiritual Armament Master went stiff from fright, Huang Yueli had already retracted his gaze. Then she cupped her fists towards Grandmaster Bai. “Grandmaster Bai, I really can’t stay in Flame Square City for long, so I can only offer my apologies. May I ask... may I receive the badge for Spiritual Armament apprentice now?”","“Huh? Oh, oh... right, this is your badge.”","Grandmaster Bai also sensed that Huang Yueli seemed to have changed into another person, which made a knowledgeable and experienced man like him feel chilly.","But that was just something that flashed past in an instance. It only took a blink of an eye and Huang Yueli resumed back to her normal self. Hence Grandmaster Bai thought he had developed a hallucination.","Hearing Huang Yueli’s words, he regained his senses and picked up a badge from the table. Then he passed it to her.","“That’s such a pity. Based on your innate talent, if you learn the methods of refining a Spiritual Armament properly, there is a sliver of hope for you to become a Sky Gem Grandmaster! Since you are so sure that this isn’t your calling, I will not force you. Here, this is your badge. Keep it properly!”","Huang Yueli took the badge, gave her thanks, and prepared to leave. Just then she heard a knock from the door.","“What’s the matter?” Grandmaster Bai asked.","The person who knocked was a mid grade Spiritual Armament Master who was dressed in a white robe. He came in and spoke in a low voice, “Grandmaster Bai, there’s a foreign Spiritual Armament Master who’d like to meet with Grandmaster Xiao. We’ve tried to explain several times that Grandmaster Xiao isn’t here but she refuses to leave. What do you think...”","“Oh? Really?”","Grandmaster Bai frowned. He pondered for a moment then stood up and left the room.","Huang Yueli followed behind him and silently walked out.","The beautiful Spiritual Armament Master at the reception hall was still there, and there were many young Spiritual Armament Masters and apprentices around her.","On seeing Grandmaster Bai coming out, the beautiful Spiritual Armament Master turned around and casually cupped her fists at him. “I believe you are Grandmaster Bai. I’ve heard of your name! I am Leyun and happened to pass by this place during my experience learning. I heard that Grandmaster Xiao is currently in Flame Square City as a guest and I’d like to ask him for some pointers. So will Grandmaster Bai please help to link us up?”","Hearing her speak, Huang Yueli’s brows lifted slightly.","All the Spiritual Armament Masters in Flame Square City’s Sky Gem Glass Chamber spoke to Grandmaster Bai respectfully.","But that beautiful woman’s attitude was very stuck up.. Apparently, she didn’t show any respect to Grandmaster Bai at all."]},{"number":2915,"title":"Chapter 2915 - Replace That Woman (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","It seemed that this beautiful Spiritual Armament Master’s identity was not ordinary, otherwise, she wouldn’t be so disrespectful to an honorable Sky Gem Grandmaster.","But this beautiful woman thought highly of that Grandmaster Xiao.","She wondered what kind of standard was this Grandmaster Xiao at. He should be a very famous Armament Grandmaster in God Realm, right?","Just as she was pondering over this, she heard Grandmaster Bai saying something.","“I didn’t expect Grandmaster Xiao’s arrival at Flame Square City to spread this fast! Quite a number of Spiritual Armaments Masters have come to visit him. Unfortunately, Grandmaster Xiao had already reminded me that I cannot reveal his whereabouts. Hence... I’m sorry that I can’t tell you anything!”","Hearing that, the beautiful woman’s brows creased together and her lips pursed slightly. She didn’t expect to be rejected!","The guard next to her couldn’t help but say, “Grandmaster Bai, do you know what identity my Lady here holds? She is different from those ordinary Spiritual Armament Masters! You’d best help to convey the message to Grandmaster Xiao. As long as my Lady can meet Grandmaster Xiao, we will offer a handsome reward for that! Otherwise...”","He said condescendingly, using both the carrot and stick approach.","But in the ears of a haughty Sky Gem Grandmaster like Grandmaster Bai, it was no different from being insulted!","Grandmaster Bai originally was rather patient but now, he was extremely furious!","He gave a loud harrumph and his mustache was blown away. “I can’t afford to take your reward! Our Sky Gem Glass Chamber’s rules have always been so. No matter what your Lady’s identity is, since she’s just a Spiritual Armament Master, she doesn’t have the right to order me around! Men, send them off!”","Saying that, Grandmaster Bai flicked his sleeves and returned to his room.","Everyone looked at one another in dismay.","The beautiful lady’s face turned pale as she looked at Grandmaster Bai’s departing figure. A glint of gloominess flashed past her eyes.","Those Spiritual Armament Masters, who were smitten with her, secretly advised, “Young Miss Le, don’t be upset. Grandmaster Bai’s temper is like this and we can’t do anything about it. There’s a chance for you to meet Grandmaster Xiao. One month later from today, Grandmaster Xiao will be giving a lecture at our Sky Gem Glass Chamber. He will also be giving a lecture on the attendees’ refined Spiritual Armaments. Just come over by then!”","Actually, this was exactly how Grandmaster Bai would reply to every Spiritual Armament Master who asked to meet Grandmaster Xiao.","Today, it was because he didn’t see eye-to-eye with Leyun, hence he didn’t tell her. Instead, he directly asked her to leave.","When Leyun heard this news, her expression turned slightly better, and left with her guards.","Even until she left, the main hall was still talking about her.","“That Spiritual Armament Master is so beautiful! Moreover, from her elegant actions, she should have been from some major force?”","“That’s right. Moreover, she looks like she’s under thirty but is already a mid rank Spiritual Armament Master. I heard that she can refine several kinds of mid grade Spirit Armaments. She’s incredible!”","“Perhaps Grandmaster Xiao would notice such an outstanding person like her!”","These people did not know what this elegant beauty with outstanding innate talent did after she walked out of Sky Gem Glass Chamber and returned to her carriage.","Once she got on the carriage, she immediately threw a cup on the floor and said ferociously, I can’t stand it. The Sky Gem Glass Chamber in Flame Square City is full of lowly humans! Moreover, those lowly fellows even dared to show me a face! How dare they stop me from meeting Grandmaster Xiao!”"]},{"number":2916,"title":"Chapter 2916 - Replace That Woman (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","The female attendant on the carriage hurriedly persuaded, “Young Miss, don’t be angry. You’re the ancient God clan, Cloudy Qilin clan Clan Leader’s niece, and your status is extremely noble. Don’t spoil your mood because of a few lowly humans! How dare they offend you, do you... want This Servant to teach them a lesson?”","The beautiful Spiritual Armament Master was Cloudy Qilin clan’s heaven grade genius, the Clan Leader’s niece, Li Leyun!","In order to hide her identity, she casually registered with a fake name when she was at the Sky Gem Glass Chamber earlier.","Li Leyun shook her head. “Forget it, this is Sacred Phoenix Race’s turf and if things blow up, there might be trouble... just let them off!”","Seeing Li Leyun’s expression still gloomy, the female attendant carefully said, “Young Miss, since these human races don’t know what’s good for them, then you shouldn’t bother to talk to them any longer. The Cloudy Qilin clan also has plenty of Sky Gem Grandmasters. If you want to learn how to refine Spirit Armaments, there are plenty of masters who want to teach you. Why do you insist on looking for that Grandmaster Xiao?”","Li Leyun swept a glance at her and said angrily, “Did you think that I like to beg others in such a meek manner? Isn’t it because that Grandmaster Xiao is a Sky Gem Grandmaster who specializes in refining long swords and the swords that he refines have attack powers which are higher than same tiered Spirit Armaments!”","The female attendant couldn’t understand why so she asked again, “Last time Brother Moying mentioned that when he was in the Lower Realm, a girl that he liked had personally refined a long sword for him and he had always carried it by his side. However, it broke during one of his battles! So, I also want to refine a long sword for him!”","When Li Leyun heard that Li Moying had liked someone, she was devastated.","After thinking for a moment, she had a change of mind. Li Moying’s past lover was probably still in the Lower Realm. Nobody knew how many years it would take for her to ascend. Perhaps she might have died in the Lower Realm whereas the person Li Moying liked was the Armament Master who could refine Profound Armaments for him. In that case, wouldn’t she, the Spiritual Armament Master be able to replace her?","Li Leyun felt that she had a chance and instantly made up her mind. She had to refine an even better long sword for him.","No matter how good the Lower Realm’s Profound Weapon was, how could it be compared with God Realm’s Spirit Armament?","It was the same for people.","No matter how beautiful the Lower Realm human race girl was, she couldn’t be compared to the beautiful ladies in God clans!","As long as the Profound Weapon she refined could replace the Profound Weapon that Li Moying’s past lover had refined, then she might be able to replace that woman’s status in Li Moying’s heart.","This was exactly why Li Leyun put her pride aside and went to look for Grandmaster Xiao, the top rated Sky Gem Grandmaster whose expertise was in refining Profound Weapons.","When the female attendant heard that Le Leyun was doing it for Li Moying, she instantly kept silent.","Practically all of Cloudy Qilin clan’s unmarried young ladies were smitten with Li Moying. So she didn’t find it strange that Li Leyun was thinking of so many ways to please him.","Li Leyun leaned against the chair and muttered to herself, “One month... the timing is just nice. Brother Moying’s guard said that they will be coming to Sacred Phoenix Continent one month later, so I’ll just wait here for one month! Perhaps, I might even be able to meet with Brother Moying!”","...","The Spiritual Armament Masters were still talking about her in the Sky Gem Glass Chamber.","Huang Yueli took another look at Li Leyun walking away. Somehow, she felt that Li Leyun gave her an uncomfortable feeling.","But since it was just a chance encounter, she didn’t think too much about it.","She pinned the Spiritual Armament apprentice badge on her chest and walked to the Books Depository to purchase some books.","Every manual related to Spirit Armaments was extremely expensive. So when Huang Yueli walked in and saw the prices, she had a huge fright!"]},{"number":2917,"title":"Chapter 2917 - Overthinking (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Luckily she had already made preparations and sold off some treasures in the Sky Phoenix Ring, to accumulate a large sum of crystal jades.","She looked around, picked a few entry-level books on theory, and paid for them.","The admission Spiritual Armament Master had been following beside her. Originally, he wanted to upsell his Armament refining ability and tried to recommend a few books to Huang Yueli.","In the end, after she stepped in, she refused to look at him at all. Instead, her gaze swept past the books on the shelf. Then she took a few books and proceeded to make payment.","“Hey, wait! Don’t choose so recklessly! There are so many books here, how do you know which books are suitable for you? It’s better to listen to me...”","The admission officer propped his head to take a look as he said.","After he took a clear look at the books which Huang Yueli was carrying, he instantly couldn’t say a word more.","Those books that Huang Yueli picked were coincidentally the most suitable for beginners. Moreover, the contents of the theory and practicals were in sequence. It was extremely suitable for one to make steady progress with these!","“You... you...” The admission officer was tongue-tied.","Huang Yueli swept a glance at him and asked, “Why? Is there a problem? I should be able to purchase these books, right?”","“Yes, of course... you can...”","The admission officer couldn’t understand why this lad’s insight was so precise?","Could it be that he actually had a Master, but intentionally didn’t report to the Sky Gem Glass Chamber?","Huang Yueli wasn’t free to bother about what he was thinking of. She had been computing how to use the least amount of crystal jades to purchase the most important items.","She had a lot of crystal jades with her after she sold off all the treasures. She wasn’t considered as a poor folk as compared with the ordinary God Realm practitioners.","But money flowed just like water in the process of refining!","So a large number of high ranking Armament Masters were nurtured by large forces. If one wanted to become a high ranking Armament Master based on their own abilities, unless that person was a peerless genius, otherwise, their family would have a huge amount of fortune!","Now, she was learning the art of refining Spirit Armaments in God Realm so that was considered as starting from scratch. Hence the amount of money she had to spend was terrifying.","Initially, Huang Yueli saw many books that she was interested in. The manuals here, to a Lower Realm ascender, were all very novel. If it was in the past, she would definitely purchase everything and slowly read through it when she had the time!","But now...","Feeling the almost empty pouch, her heart was tearing up.","She finally understood what poverty meant!","How heart-rendering! How melancholic!","She could only choose the most useful books as she had no other choice. As for the remaining crystal jades, she had to purchase materials for refining!","After Huang Yueli paid the bill, she turned and walked to the room which was selling materials.","The admission officer originally thought that she would leave after purchasing the books. He didn’t expect her to purchase the materials immediately. He went into a short blank and hurriedly chased after her.","“Hey, you... what are you going to buy now? You should finish reading those books, prepare yourself first, and take some entry-level apprentice examinations first! It’s just a waste to purchase those materials. If you can’t even pass the apprentice examinations, you can’t possibly refine any Spirit Armaments at all!”","Huang Yueli shrugged and said indifferently, “It’s fine. I’ll just purchase some to have some fun. It’s alright even if I can’t refine anything out of them!”","She didn’t want to explain so much, and there wasn’t any way to explain it anyway.","As long as she could refine Spirit Armaments in the future, action would speak louder than her words.","The admission officer’s eyes widened and said, “What the, you’re really a tycoon!”"]},{"number":2918,"title":"Chapter 2918 - Overthinking (2)","paragraphs":["Purchasing Spirit Armament materials was a terrifying expense to those genuine Spiritual Armament Masters.","It was because the success rate of refining Spirit Armaments was very low.","To refine a Spirit Armament, they had to purchase several sets of materials.","As for a beginner like Huang Yueli, she might have to spend more than ten sets of materials in order to refine a complete Spirit Armament.","Moreover, she hadn’t even passed those Spiritual Armament apprentice examinations yet.","Did she have too much money, so she was squandering it to practice at home?","The look that the admission officer had towards Huang Yueli was totally different now!","A Lower Realm ascender had so much money. Did this person have some strong backing?","However, it only took a quarter of an hour before he realized that he had overthought things!","Huang Yueli indeed walked into the Spirit Armament materials room and indeed purchased some materials. But... the way she picked the items and the way she made the payment was different from a tycoon!","“This buddy, you’re here to purchase Spirit Armament materials, right? You seem to be an apprentice, is this your first time refining armaments? Then you have to buy a Spirit Armament furnace! Look at the ones we have here. These are standard models and it’s one size fits all! It is manufactured according to the standards given by Sky Gem Glass Chamber. The only difference is the materials which are used are different, and so are the pricing.”","“Buddy, you should know that the lower the rank of the Spiritual Armament Master, the lower the success rate of the Spirit Armament. It’s even more needless to say for an apprentice like you! If you buy a higher grade Spirit Armament furnace, it will greatly increase the success rate of your armament refining! Take this for example...”","The steward responsible for sales saw the hint in the admission officer’s eyes and instantly realized that this apprentice was a tycoon. The moment she walked in, he quickly promoted the items to Huang Yueli excitedly.","Whoever knew that she wasn’t even listening to him at all. Her eyes swept past the racks and pointed casually.","“I want that one!”","“Oh, alright. Little buddy, you’re so clear-cut! Then I’ll help you... eh? Are you certain you want to buy this one?”","The steward’s eyes opened wide when he followed the direction of Huang Yueli’s finger.","That was the cheapest Spirit Armament furnace on the entire rack! It was practically useless for Spirit Armament refining!","Not to mention a tycoon, even a poor Spirit Master apprentice would clench their teeth to purchase a higher grade Spirit Armament furnace. Otherwise, the probability of relying on one’s ability to control the fire and temperature was just too low! There would be no chance to officially convert into a genuine Spiritual Armament Master in this entire lifetime!","Huang Yueli nodded and said, “Yes, I’m certain. Please help me pack this up!”","The steward looked at her in astonishment. Then he turned to the admission officer, as though he was trying to speak with his eyes. “Are you teasing me? Tycoon? Buying this?”","The admission officer couldn’t understand her actions at all. Wasn’t she very rich, and had too much money to squander? Otherwise, why was she able to purchase materials without even looking at the books?","Actually, when Huang Yueli bought the books earlier, she had already flipped through the contents in the book.","To others, that speed might not even allow them to take a clear look at the pictures. But to Huang Yueli who had a photographic memory, she had already grasped the important contents inside. At least she could remember what the basic low grade Spirit Armaments’ materials were required.","She walked to the materials rack and said the names of the materials that she needed. “Dark Bolt Thread, Sky Poison Crystal, Wild Volcanic Rock...”","She said out a long list of materials.."]},{"number":2919,"title":"Chapter 2919 - Overthinking (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","The steward and admission officer were dazed to hear that, and suspicions arose in their hearts again.","Why was she purchasing so many materials at one go?","Could it be that it was just a coincidence that she didn’t know and chose the lousiest Spirit Armament, but in actual fact, she was still a tycoon?","However, after Huang Yueli asked for the long list of materials, she added on to say, “Alright, I’ll just need these. Please give me... two sets of each material! Please wrap everything up!”","When she said the words “two sets”, she couldn’t help but grit her teeth and cringe!","After buying so many materials, she didn’t have much money left on her! It would probably be enough for her to buy some street food. But it would be difficult to fork out any money for her lodging at the inn.","After living for two lifetimes, she finally experienced what was as poor as a church mouse...","Hearing Huang Yueli’s last sentence, the steward and admission officer made an expression as though they were going to throw up blood.","The steward quickly stared at Huang Yueli and said, “I say, young buddy, are you fooling around with me? You’re only buying two sets of each material? Can’t you tell that other people would buy at least five sets? A Spiritual Armament apprentice like you would need to buy at least ten sets at one go. Otherwise, how are you going to refine a finished product??”","Two sets? Was it a lot?","If possible, Huang Yueli wanted to buy an additional set so that she could save a huge sum of money.","Actually, she had done extensive research on God Realm’s Spirit Armaments.","Before her ascension, Huang Zixiao had once given her a high grade Spirit Armament to help her pass through the heavenly tribulation.","After the heavenly tribulation, that Profound Armor was greatly damaged. After Huang Yueli ascended, she was still contemplating on how to restore it to its original state.","Hence, while she was traveling on the carriage, she had been researching this high grade Spirit Armament during her free time.","After a long time of research, Huang Yueli had finally found a gateway and came up with a plan.","Today, she bought so many books back with her, mainly because she wanted to verify if her guess was the same as what she thought.","After all, if she really wanted to refine Spirit Armaments, just relying on her deduction wasn’t enough. It was necessary to get some basic knowledge and she had to verify her guesses.","After all, just relying on deduction wasn’t enough to refine Spirit Armaments. It was essential to have the basic knowledge. So she had to make up for this missing part before she could master the subject.","But she was worried if she could succeed in refining the Spirit Armament.","But this was, after all, her first time. So she purchased another extra set of materials, just in case.","Huang Yueli didn’t bother to explain and said lightly, “Why? Does the Sky Gem Glass Chamber have such a rule that we must buy a total of five sets of materials?”","“Erm... no, we don’t have such a rule.” The steward didn’t expect her to ask this, so he gave an honest reply.","Huang Yueli nodded and said, “Since that’s the case, then I’ll have to trouble you.”","Hearing her say that, the steward couldn’t ask anything else, even though he was full of queries. If she wanted to buy the items, surely he couldn’t say that he didn’t want to sell, wasn’t it!","But as he packed the items, he kept thinking about it.","Was this country bumpkin Lower Realm ascender rich or poor?","If she didn’t have any money, why did she purchase the Spirit Armament materials for? Wasn’t it equivalent to throwing money into the water!","If she had, why was she acting so petty? She only purchased two sets of each material, and even showed a distressed expression...","No matter if it was the steward or the admission officer, none of them considered the fact that Huang Yueli was preparing to refine a Spirit Armament out of these materials!"]},{"number":2920,"title":"Chapter 2920 - Overthinking (4)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","In their hearts, they were thinking that this was something that would absolutely not happen!","After Huang Yueli was done purchasing the materials, she found that she didn’t lack anything and just left.","Walking out of the Sky Gem Glass Chamber, the first thing Huang Yueli did was to head towards the largest Inn in Flame Square City to look for a room.","When the innkeeper saw that she was a Lower Realm ascender dressed in simple clothes, he instantly looked at her with disdain.","“Our Double Prosperity Inn is the best in the entire Flame Square City. The prices here are naturally not cheap. Sir, if you’re intending to stay here, you’ll have to pre-pay one hundred medium grade crystal jades as a deposit!”","One hundred medium grade crystal jades to ordinary God realm folks was not a small sum.","If it was this morning, Huang Yueli would still be able to afford it.","But now, she only had a few miserable low grade crystal jades in her pocket. She was so poor that she almost could not afford to eat, not to mention paying such a huge amount of deposit.","Seeing Huang Yueli hesitating, the arrogant expression on the innkeeper’s face grew even more obvious. “Why? Don’t tell me that you can’t afford the deposit? This is just the deposit for ten days. Didn’t you say that you’re going to stay for a month? You can’t even afford this bit of money, are you messing around with me?”","The innkeeper had just finished talking when Huang Yueli’s wrist flipped. She took out a badge from her interspatial ring and placed it right in front of him.","“I’m a Spiritual Armament apprentice, did you think that I will renege on my debt? Innkeeper, if you’re really worried, I’ll leave my apprentice badge here with you first. In case I can’t afford to pay, you can go to the Sky Gem Glass Chamber to ask for payment. What do you think?”","The innkeeper was stunned when he saw the Spiritual Armament apprentice’s badge!","There was a huge disparity between an apprentice and a genuine Spiritual Armament Master. But in ordinary folks’ minds, an apprentice’s status was already very high.","Obtaining an apprentice badge meant that the person in front of him at least had a human grade and above innate talent in both metal and fire dual attributes!","For someone with this kind of innate talent, even if one could not become a Spiritual Armament Master, if it was used in cultivation alone, one would become a Heart Profound Realm practitioner sooner or later. For a place like Flame Square City, that person was basically considered as a top exponent.","Moreover, most Spiritual Armament apprentices were under the tutelage of a Master. Just based on Huang Yueli passing the assessment based on her ability was extremely scarce.","The innkeeper felt that she had a Spiritual Armament Master behind her.","Spiritual Armament Master... that was a very rich tycoon!","How would he possibly allow his disciple to renege on a debt at the inn?","With this thinking in mind, the innkeeper immediately changed his mindset and his attitude became extremely courteous. “Oh my, you’re a Spiritual Armament apprentice from the Sky Gem Glass Chamber! No wonder I feel that this young lad here looks so extraordinary. You’re even radiating with a stylish temperament! Please, come in! The superior room that you want is on the second floor, all the way inside. It’s absolutely the quietest and spacious room!”","Huang Yueli played with the apprentice badge in her right hand and asked slowly, ”","Then... the deposit...”","“Let’s forget about the deposit! You can stay as long as you want. Just settle the bill before you leave!” The innkeeper immediately said.","Huang Yueli nodded her head satisfactorily, kept her badge, and followed the waiter to the superior room.","When she walked into the room, she silently smiled when no one was around.","“I didn’t know that a Spiritual Armament apprentice’s status is so useful! Sky Gem Glass Chamber’s status has exceeded my expectations...”","She sighed for a moment and perked herself up.","“Although it has helped me do away with the deposit, I’ll still have to pay for the room when I leave. So I have to grab hold of time and quickly refine some Spirit Armaments to sell!”"]},{"number":2921,"title":"Chapter 2921 - Integrated Into One (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Huang Yueli ignored the surroundings and revealed a satisfied smile.","“Indeed the largest inn in Sacred Phoenix Continent. The superior room’s environment is indeed much better than the other inns! Moreover, the most important thing is that this room is spacious enough. It’s enough for me to go into closed door cultivation and refine Spirit Armaments...”","While she thought, she retrieved a variety of materials and magical beast cores which she had prepared earlier.","First, she used some simple methods to set an invisibility array around the walls.","This array was something that she decoded with her father when she sneaked into Snow Phoenix Palace previously. It should be an array that was exclusive in God Realm.","Although she didn’t know what level was it in God Realm, Snow Phoenix Palace was, after all, one of the bases left behind by the ancient God clans in the Lower Realm. So the arrays inside should not be some cheap stuff.","Huang Yueli set up the array based on her memories.","Then she took out the spirit armament furnace which she bought from the Sky Gem Glass Chamber earlier.","Taking a look at this black and heavy furnace, Huang Yueli frowned slightly. “Isn’t this furnace a little too coarsely manufactured? The array patterns engraved on the exterior are so crudely done. I wonder if it is actually of any use? Moreover, the left and the right sides aren’t even at all! How do they even have the cheek to say that this is a standard spirit armament furnace? It’s even worse than the Amethyst Gold Gem Cauldron that I brought from the Lower Realm!”","Actually, spirit armament furnaces were all handmade, so it was normal to have some slight unevenness.","But Huang Yueli was used to using fine quality goods. So towards these kinds of coarsely made products, she simply could not stand it at all.","The Amethyst Gold Gem Cauldron was the furnace that she used in Soaring Heavens Continent. It was something that she and Li Moying found together. Back then, the Amethyst Light Sword was sealed within and the sword spirit acknowledged Li Moying as its Master. As for the Amethyst Gold Gem Cauldron, it was taken by Huang Yueli.","The Amethyst Gold Gem Cauldon was one of Soaring Heavens Continent’s finest armament furnaces. Each complicated array pattern on the exterior helped greatly in refining.","Moreover, the amethyst gold rays that spread out on the furnace’s entire body had different patterns. All of those were exquisite.","Alas, the Amethyst Gold Gem Cauldron was manufactured using Lower Realm’s materials. So when she brought it to God Realm, Huang Yueli felt that it was not solid enough to refine even higher grade Spirit Armaments.","The Sky Gem Glass Chamber’s most inferior spirit armament furnace didn’t have much functionality. But at least it was manufactured using God Realm’s metal materials. It was able to take on the impact of the deviant flame and a large amount of Profound Energy!","“I must refine the weapons properly. After I earn enough money, I will change this ugly-looking thing!”","Huang Yueli grumbled softly and took out the books which she had purchased in the afternoon. Then she swiftly read through it.","Her speed of reading was so fast that describing it as reading ten sentences at one time wasn’t even apt.","As she read, she mumbled to herself, “...oh, so it’s like this... no wonder I couldn’t find a solution... in this way, these fine details can be done in this way...”","Huang Yueli propped up her little cheeks and flipped through the books. It only took her less than four hours to finish reading that thick pile of books.","Raising her arms above her head, she stretched her arms.","“God Realm’s Spirit Armament refining skills are indeed much deeper than ours in Soaring Heavens Continent.. No wonder the Spirit Armaments’ power is much stronger than ordinary Profound Weapons! But if we were to use such complicated and profound skills to refine weapons, the requirement for the Armament Master’s innate talent and endurance is much higher by several times! There aren’t many with such innate talent in the Lower Realm. That’s why only God Realm can nurture so many Spiritual Armament Masters!”"]},{"number":2922,"title":"Chapter 2922 - Integrated Into One (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Combining all the comprehension that Huang Yueli had in the past with the contents that she read from the manual today, she roughly had a conclusion.","In Soaring Heavens Continent, the main element that determined the grade of the Profound Armament was based on the materials that were used to refine the Profound Armament.","An Armament Master’s innate talent might be important, but the fire and metal attributed to Profound Energies were mainly used to smelt materials, control the flame’s temperature and also help the Profound Armament to form its shape.","But refining Spirit Armaments was another thing.","The thing that decided the Spirit Armament’s grade was not the materials, but the Spiritual Armament Master’s innate talent, ability, and the control of one’s Profound Energy.","Spirit Armament materials were just a retainer that was used to contain the Spiritual Armament Master’s Profound Energy.","Using the Spiritual Armament Master’s Profound Energy to construct into an energy field was the real reason why a Spirit Armament wielded so much power.","The energy field was being sealed by the Spiritual Armament Master with special materials and when it was stimulated by a practitioner’s Profound Energy, it would release an astonishing amount of energy!","So, the method of refining a Spirit Armament and Profound Armament was totally different, and the might of the Spirit Armament was much stronger.","Of course, this didn’t mean that the Spirit Armament’s materials weren’t important.","The stability of the energy field, the degree of difficulty to activate the energy field, and the ultimate power of the energy field were closely related to the superiority and inferiority of the Spirit Armament materials.","Even for a high ranking Sky Gem Grandmaster, if he didn’t have suitable materials, it would be impossible to satisfactorily refine Spirit or Treasure Armaments.","Huang Yueli already had this guess in mind before she went to the Sky Gem Glass Chamber.","After she read the books that she purchased, her guess was more or less verified.","This kind of exclusive refining method for Spirit Armaments was doomed to be a tragedy for ordinary Lower Realm ascenders because all the refining methods that they had learned in the past could not be used at all!","But, to Huang Yueli, this was a good thing.","As one of the two God Realm’s god grade geniuses, whose innate talent could be higher than hers? Her control towards Profound Energy was something that she was born with. No matter how ordinary people try to waste their energy working hard, it was impossible for them to reach her standard!","“Now that I’ve already understood the principle, next, I’m going to give it a try...”","Huang Yueli took out an illustrated book and flipped it open. Then she left it beside the spirit armament furnace.","“Ooh, this Disheartened Dagger’s structure should be the simplest. I will start to refine from this!”","She raised her hand and struck out a hand gesture. Then a flame flew out from her palm and landed on the fire entrance underneath the spirit armament furnace.","The flame shrank a little and following that, it started to burn steadily.","The spirit armament furnace was lit almost instantly. The surroundings were enveloped by a ray of light and those roughly engraved array patterns on the furnace’s exterior were instantly lit up.","Huang Yueli’s expression was solemn as her eyes were focused. The hand gestures that she saw on the book earlier surfaced in her mind. One after another, she swiftly struck out those hand gestures.","The spirit armament furnace’s temperature soared.","When refining Spirit Armaments, the impact of the flame would be even bigger than refining Profound Armaments. But luckily, Huang Yueli used the True Phoenix Fire which was a top rate powerful flame in God Realm. So it was most suitable for use in refining armaments.","Huang Yueli followed the instructions and smoothly pre-heated up the spirit armament furnace.","“It seems rather easy...” This thought flashed past Huang Yueli’s mind.","She didn’t know that to Spiritual Armament apprentices with ordinary innate talents, completing this step required them to practice at least more than a thousand times!"]},{"number":2923,"title":"Chapter 2923 - Integrated Into One (3)","paragraphs":["It was impossible for them to succeed on their first try, just like her!","Huang Yueli heaved a silent sigh of relief but she didn’t dare to slack off. Her concentration was still maintained in a taut state.","She threw the materials that were piled next to her into the spirit armament furnace in sequence.","The process of smelting materials was the same as Soaring Heavens Continent’s method, so it was a piece of cake for Huang Yueli.","Not too long after, all the materials had been fused.","Her expression abruptly turned grave as she stared at the melted materials in the spirit armament furnace without blinking.","“The next step is the most difficult part. This is also the biggest difference between refining Profound Armaments...”","After the spirit armament materials had been fused, she had to slowly decrease the furnace’s flame. During this process of decreasing the temperature, the materials in the furnace would slowly set into shape.","Huang Yueli had to draw out the energy field structure using her Profound Energy within the shortest amount of time she had, and encase the energy field into the materials. Moreover, to display the full force of the energy field, the materials must be molded into a certain shape.","That meant to say that Huang Yueli had to split up her concentration, work on the structure of the energy field while ensuring the exterior shape of the materials, and fuse the two perfectly...","This complicated process, to a Spiritual Armament Master’s Profound Energy, endurance, and soul trace, was a huge test.","As long as she was slightly careless, it would fail...","Huang Yueli perked her concentration and carefully controlled the release of her Profound Energy.","The energy field was slowly drafted out. At the same time, the materials that were in the cooling process were being pulled into a curvy arc by her.","She was at her last step, to encase the energy field into the dagger’s interior...","“BOOM—!!”","A loud explosion rang beside Huang Yueli’s ears!","The spirit armament furnace’s flame exploded and a fiery flame shot right through the roof!","“Oh no!” Huang Yeuli’s expression changed and she hurriedly retracted the True Phoenix Fire.","Luckily her reaction was swift and she had struck out timely. Although the roof of the guest room was scorched by the raging fire, it didn’t burn through it and hence, it didn’t lead to a fire.","But...","Huang Yueli shifted her glance towards the half-molded long sword in the spirit armament furnace. She gloomily discovered that the Spirit Armament that she was still refining had already turned into a bundle of ash.","This time’s refinement ended in failure!","She sat down on the chair and lifted her hand to wipe off the sweat on her forehead.","It was impossible to say that she wasn’t feeling frustrated after failing the refinement of a Spirit Armament.","She had already deduced the process several times in her mind before she started refining, and after she was certain that every single detail had no problem, then she started the process. Moreover, her Profound Energy and soul trace were extremely strong. Every single hand gesture that she struck out was extremely accurate, and the plan was executed well.","According to this trend, she should have successfully refined the Disheartened Dagger...","But now, she failed. It meant that there was a problem with her deduction! This had turned her plans around!","“What’s going on? Why did this happen? What on earth had gone wrong?” Huang Yueli frowned, and her mind swiftly raced past all the possibilities.","In the process of refining Spirit Armaments, the energy field that she drew shouldn’t be a problem. The most difficult points that the manuals had indicated to take special note of, were easily overcome by her powerful control.","Molding the materials into shape was a simple matter. Anyone with slight metal attributed innate talent would be able to do it well.."]},{"number":2924,"title":"Chapter 2924 - Integrated Into One (4)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","So, the biggest problem should still be related to the encasement of the energy field into the Spirit Armament materials...","Huang Yueli flipped through the books and tapped her hand on the table as she was engrossed in her thoughts, trying hard to find out the crux of the problem.","After a while, she muttered to herself, “Could it be that during the fusing process, the sequence of the amount of Profound Energy that I added wasn’t correct? Indeed, before the explosion happened, I had already sensed the repulsion of the energy field from the Spirit Armament. But because I don’t have any experience and assumed that it was normal... Looks like I need to decrease my speed and use my soul trace to check on the Spirit Armament’s situation first before injecting my Profound Energy based on the situation...”","Huang Yueli pondered over this for a moment more and finally decided that she had to act according to the situation. Too many situations could happen during the refinement of Spirit Armaments. No matter how much sufficient preparation she had made, it would be difficult for her to handle it.","Having thought through this, Huang Yueli perked herself up again. “It’s indeed not simple to refine Spirit Armaments! Luckily I bought two sets of materials each so I still have another chance to try. This time, I cannot make the same mistake again!”","Huang Yueli walked to the furnace and checked on it. This furnace might look run-down, but the quality was not that bad after all. At least it was solid enough.","That small explosion did not make the furnace explode. In fact, there wasn’t even any scratch on the furnace at all.","Huang Yueli wiped the spirit armament slightly and lit up the fire again.","The smelting process was much faster than before and it only took less than an hour before she entered the drawing of the energy field.","This time, Huang Yueli didn’t dare to slack off. She adjusted all the Profound Energy in her body, and her concentration was also fully unleashed. She tried all her means to feel the Spirit Armament’s refining process, as well as all the series of changes.","Following the Spirit Armament materials giving off a sizzling sound, Huang Yueli’s senses seemed to have entered another world.","In this subjective world, the Profound Energy in the energy field seemed to have turned into rays of glaring light that floated past her eyes. She didn’t need to put in much effort to see it clearly.","Huang Yueli subconsciously controlled the energy field and slowly fused it with the materials.","Every thread and every ounce were encased perfectly without a single flaw...","The Spirit Armament slowly set into shape, and Huang Yueli started to relax.","It seemed that she had found the correct direction this time around!","Huang Yueli hadn’t seen any other Spiritual Masters refine Spirit Armaments, so she didn’t realize that something was wrong with the refining method that she had come out with.","It was her first time refining Spirit Armaments, so the reason for her failure was not because there was something wrong with her plan. But the reason was that God Realm’s Spiritual Armament Master’s energy field fusion method could not be written down on the books. Instead, it was all passed down verbally from the Master to disciple.","Huang Yueli didn’t have a Master, and no one told her the method, so it was reasonable for her to fail.","If it was anyone else, that person would definitely have thought of a way to find a Master.","But Huang Yueli didn’t think of this at all. She insisted on using her heaven-defying innate talent and power of comprehension to think of a solution.","But her method was different from the standard method used in God Realm.","Moreover, as she refined one after another piece of Spirit Armament, her method was slowly formed, and the disparity between it and the standard method was becoming further and further..."]},{"number":2925,"title":"Chapter 2925 - One Month Later (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","One month later.","An intense battle was happening on the barren lands in between the Soul Connection Ocean and Serene Rain Town.","A huge Fissure Plume Blonde Condor swooped down from the sky fiercely. Its power wings flapped, and bursts of powerful wind attack waves caused the trees in the surroundings to be uprooted!","“Young Master Moying, be careful!!” Li Tian Yi and Li Tian Er cried out in horror.","The Fissure Plume Blonde Condor was a high tiered spirit beast Moreover, it had metal and wind dual attributes so its speed was extremely fast with a high level of attack power. In God Realm, even practitioners in Heart Profound Realm end-phase were not willing to provoke it, what more for their group. The one with the highest cultivation among them was Li Moying, who was in Heart Profound Realm early-phase.","The guards were several hundred meters away from the Blonde Condor and they were made to retreat by its power, being thrown back by the wind.","Facing the Fissure Plume Blonde Condor, it was imaginable to think how much pressure Li Moying was under right now!","Li Tian Yi and the others turned cold from shock. They wanted to dash forward to save him, but none of them could resist the wind and couldn’t move at all.","They could only watch the Fissure Plume Blonde Condor give a loud shrill and swooped down towards Li Moying’s head.","“Young Master Moying!!!”","Li Tian Yi and Li Tian Er cried out in alarm as they shut their eyes, not daring to see what was about to happen.","They were under the Clan Leader’s orders to risk everything they had to protect the only god grade genius in their clan. Even if all of them had to die, they could not allow Li Moying to lose his life here!","If something were to happen to him here, they... they would not be able to pay the consequences, even if they had to die ten thousand times!","After a round of horrifying explosive shouts, the Fissure Plume Blonde Condor’s roar became even sharper like a sharp blade that passed through everyone’s ears. In an instant, everyone lost their hearing.","The guards’ complexion turned pale and they covered their ears. But all they could hear were buzzing sounds. They felt light-headed and dizzy, trying their best to stop themselves from throwing up.","After some time later, they finally recovered a bit of consciousness.","Li Tian Yi opened his eyes and looked at the center of the storm. He only took a look and cried out in astonishment, “Young Master Moying, this... this is...”","Li Tian Er also looked in the direction of his gaze.","On one look, he found that the mighty Fissure Plume Blonde Condor had already sprawled on the ground. Its eye-catching wings drooped by its side and the surface on the ground was covered in red. Blood kept spilling out from the side.","From the looks of this, it seemed that it had already died from its serious injury.","The body resembled a small hill. Even if it laid limp on the ground, it was still four to five meters tall.","But the Fissure Plume Blonde Condor’s head was facing upwards. Its eyes widened like full moons, as though it couldn’t believe that it was so easily defeated by a god clan practitioner with such weak cultivation!","“Heavens! The Fissure Plume Blonde Condor is dead! It actually died in this way!”","“Could it be that Young Master Moying had killed it? But... but how is this possible? The last time I came out on experience learning with Elder Qing and met with a Fissure Plume Blonde Condor. But we spent a great deal of effort to kill it!”","“But other than Young Master Moying, who else is here??”","“This is simply a miracle... Young Master is too strong...”","Li Tian Yi and Li Tian Er looked at the Fissure Plume Blonde Condor’s corpse in astonishment, and their hearts were filled with worship for Li Moying.","As for Li Moying, he stood next to the condor with a placid and calm look on his face."]},{"number":2926,"title":"Chapter 2926 - One Month Later (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","As though the person who killed a high tiered spirit beast wasn’t him at all.","Hearing the guards gasping in surprise, he swept a glance at the Blonde Condor’s dead body and instructed, “Settle the corpse!”","“Yes, Young Master!”","Actually, Li Tian Yi and the others had already started to work on it before he instructed.","Every single part of the high tiered Spirit Beast like the Fissure Plume Blonde Condor was precious. A piece of tail feather or a bottle of blood was all high tiered materials that were hard to come by. It could be used for refining armaments or medicinal pills.","The guards started to work on it while Li Moying lowered his head. Looking at the weapon in his hand, he frowned slightly.","The long sword in his hand had already broken into two when he fought against the Fissure Plume Blonde Condor earlier!","As the only god grade genius in the clan, Cloudy Qilin clan wasn’t stingy to him at all. The long sword in his hand was a genuine mid grade Treasure Armament.","This was something that the Elders were allowed to use in ancient god clans. It was difficult for ordinary forces’ Dao Profound Realm practitioners to get one, not to mention Heart Profound Realm practitioners. As for the other people, even if they sold everything they had, they wouldn’t be able to afford a single kill the Fissure Plume Blonde Condor successfully.","Seeing Li Moying go into a trance, Li Tian Yi thought that he was feeling the heartache to damage the Treasure Armament So he quickly advised, “Young Master Moying, it’s just a mid grade Treasure Armament. It might be valuable but to a large clan like us, the Cloudy Qilin clan, it’s not worth mentioning at all! Instead, you are Cloudy Qilin clan’s greatest fortune. Damaging one Treasure Armament is nothing, as long as it can save your life. Even if it takes one hundred or one thousand pieces, it’s all worth it!”","What Li Tian Yi said was not exaggerated at all.","Li Moying represented Cloudy Qilin clan’s fortune for the next few thousand years. If he was hurt, even slightly, it would make the entire clan uptight.","However, Li Moying’s frown didn’t ease when he heard this.","He remained silent for a moment and suddenly sighed. “I didn’t expect this. Although God Realm’s Treasure Armament power is very big, it was damaged so quickly. Back then when I was in the Lower Realm, I used my long sword for several decades and nothing happened to it at all”","Li Moying wasn’t feeling the heartache for some mid grade Treasure Armament. But when he saw the broken sword in his hands, he suddenly recalled the past. The Profound Weapon that Huang Yueli refined for him.","In his past life, he had always used the ninth tiered Profound Weapon that was refined by Huang Yueli. But it broke during the process of his split soul.","In this lifetime, Huang Yueli gifted him with the Amethyst Light Sword and it had also broken into half during the heavenly tribulation.","It seemed like a prediction, as though each time the weapons she gave him broke, it would mean that they would be separated...","In the past, when they split up, he would keep the weapon that she gave him by his side. It seemed as though his Liter was still accompanying him and fighting alongside him.","But now, what he could use was the weapon that the clan had assigned to him.","So what if the power was strong or the weapon grade was high?","Only his Li’er understood him the best. She knew what weapon was most suitable for him, and how it would be able to display his full power to the max!","Li Tian Yi didn’t know what Li Moying was thinking about. Seeing him go into a trance, he could only come out with some gibberish advice.","“Young Master, if you feel that the clan’s weapons aren’t suitable, you can ask the clan’s Sky Gem Grandmasters to refine one for you. The Fissure Plume Blonde Condor’s tail feather and spine are very important Treasure Armament materials. It’s just nice, we can bring this back!”"]},{"number":2927,"title":"Chapter 2927 - One Month Later (3)","paragraphs":["Translator Misty Cloud Translations | Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Speaking of this, no matter which Sky Gem Grandmaster it was, they had respectable and esteemed statuses. Moreover, all of them were haughty so it r than climbing to heaven to ask them to refine a Treasure Amament.","Even if it was the Elders from the Cloudy Qjlin clan, they might not do it. It would depend on how close they were.","But if it was Li Moying, not only would the Sky Gem Grandmasters not reject, they would fight to refine for him instead.","After all, a god grade genius could possibly become a Life Profound Realm peerless exponent.","By then, the Sky Gem Grandmaster who refined the ‘Treasure Amament for him would be able to boast about it!","It was the utmost glory to a Dao Profound Realm top exponent to use the Treasure Armament that a Sky Gem Grandmaster had refined!","When Li Moying heard that, he shook his head slightly and didn’t say anything at all.","No matter which Sky Gem Grandmaster it was, that person couldn’t be compared with his Li’er. But where did she go to?","At this moment, Li Tian Er, who was injured during the battle with the Fissure Plume Blonde Condor earlier, had already treated his wounds and walked over again.","“Young Master, you you’re not injured, are you?” Li Tian Er asked.","Li Moying shook his head.","The two guards exchange a glance and Li Tian Yi stepped forward. He asked cautiously, “Then. Young Master, what should we do next? Should we continue heading into the barren lands? There are very few people here and no one knows what we will meet with if we venture further. But we’ve already met with the Fissure Plume Blonde Condor here. If we go in further, we might meet with stronger Spirit Beasts..","Li Tian Yi stopped speaking at this point.","But his meaning was already very clear.","After all, Li Moying was still in Heart Profound Realm. Although he killed the Fissure Plume Blonde Condor, he had to pay a price for it. Even his mid grade Treasure Armament was destroyed.","If they were to meet with even more powerful Spirit Beasts, the result would be dire.","Hearing this, Li Moying’s gaze congealed slightly and he turned silent. After a while, he finally opened his mouth, “The deadline of two months is almost up.","We’ll set off to Sacred Phoenix Continent tomorrow and meet up with the others!","Li Tian Yi and Li Tian Er heaveda sigh of relief. “Yes, Young Master!”","They were extremely worried that ILi Moying would insist on doing it his way, to continue searching for her in the barren lands.","If he really died or suffered a serious injury there, they wouldn’t be able to answer for it.","But unfortunately, Li Moying’s character was overbearing. If he decided on something, no one could change his mind!","Now, he had finally decided to go back.","Li Moying swept a faint glance at them and knew what they were thinking of.","But he didn’t bother to explain.","He was willing to give up searching and head to Sacred Phoenix Continent because he had roughly confirmed that Huang Yueli didn’t go into the barren lands.","Otherwise, just based on their meticulous search, they would be able to find some clues of her appearance. However, there was nothing at all.","Adding on the fact that his little fox had always been cautious. As long as she found the barren land to be extremely dangerous, she would realize that she had gone in the wrong direction and wouldn’t possibly continue to venture in.","In this way, there was only one possibility.","His Li’er did not take this barren lands path at all. Instead, she had entered Serene Rain Town.","But no matter what the reason was, as long as Huang Yueli did not die in the barren lands, then she would definitely appear in the Sacred Phoenix Continent."]},{"number":2928,"title":"Chapter 2928 - One Month Later (4)","paragraphs":["Transtator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Sacred Phoenix Continent, Flame Square City.","In Double Prosperity’s superior room, Huang Yueli’s eyes were tightly shut as","she was fully focused on refining Spirit Armaments.","The current her looked rather disheveled. Her clothes were crumpled and her","face was smeared with dust and ash.","Ever since she started to research on the refining method for Spirit Armaments","in the superior room, she didn’t step out nor take a shower.","In reality, her thoughts were totally on armament refining and she had no time","to bother about the other matters.","A loud “boom” was heard, followed by a fiery tongue sticking out of the spirit","armament furnace. The bright light shone and gradually extinguished.","“It’s done, it’s done! This Moon Frost Hook Sword is finally refined","successfully! This is one of the most complicated kinds that Ive refined among","the low grade Spirit Armaments. Luckily I have enough patience..”","Huang Yueli looked at that unique and sharp weapon in the furnace as her","heart leaped with joy.","During this closed door cultivation, she had successfully refined several low","grade Spirit Armaments, which were extremely popular weapons in God","Realm.","Among them, the most simple few kinds were equivalent to testing her","endurance and control towards Profound Energy. Initially, she hadn’t grasped","the knack and failed during the first time, succeeding only on the second time.","Towards this, Huang Yueli felt a little frustrated over this.","“Refining Spirit Armaments is much more difficult than what I had imagined!","Luckily I bought two sets of ingredients in advance. Otherwise, it would be a","waste of my effort if I didn’t manage to refine anything at al!”","Huang Yueli was grumbling silently in her mind. But she didn’t expect that her","success rate already was very shocking!","If the news of this leaked out, she would be worshipped by all the Spiritual","Armament Masters.","At this point, all the Spirit Armament materials that Huang Yueli bought from","the Sky Gem Glass Chamber were all used up.","She had nothing else to do, so she could only extinguish the True Phoenix Fire","in the spirit armament furnace. Stretching herself, she stood up.","“T haven’t been outdoors for such a long time. I feel that I’m about to turn","moldy. I think it’s time to go out for a walk”","She took a bath and redid her disguise, then walked out of the room.","When she came downstairs, she was stopped by the innkeeper.","This guest, you’ve stayed at our inn for an entire time. Are you intending to","continue staying here? Or will you be checking out? Our shop is currently","having some financial difficulties so we’d like to ask you to settle the bill for","this month’s stay..”","Huang Yueli’s smile instantly disappeared when she heard that.","What? What did you say? One month had passed! Time passed this quickly!","Huang Yueli’s eyes widened.","The innkeeper nodded and said, “Isn’t that so?","Huang Yueli jumped up. “Oh no, one month has already passed! Luckily I came","out of my closed door cultivation on time, otherwise, Id miss Grandmaster","Xiao’s lecture!”","She saw the sky was still bright and discovered that it was still morning. So she","immediately started to run out and sped towards the Sky Gem Glass Chamber.","“Wait, guest, the payment for your room","The innkeeper wanted to stop her but her cultivation was much higher than","his, so she disappeared without a trace within a few seconds. Only the","innkeeper was left standing there with a terrible look on his face.","What’s going on with this person? When he came, he wasn’t even willing to","pay the deposit. I gave him some leeway on account that he is a Spirit","Armament apprentice. But he stayed for an entire month and didn’t even step","out at all. Now he’s even run away! Surely he’s not here to con me, right?"]},{"number":2929,"title":"Chapter 2929 - Free Show (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Huang Yueli ran very quickly and arrived at the Sky’ Gem Glass Chamber","shortly after.","Today, there were a lot of people in the reception hall. Practically everyone had","pinned the Spiritual Armament Masters badge on their chests.","The beautiful Spiritual Armament Master that she met one month ago was also","in the crowd. She i,vore an elaborate long robe and her make-up was delicate.","She gave off a haughty aura and one could tell that she had an extraordinary","background.","Many Spiritual Armament Masters crowded, wanting to strike up a","conversation with her. But she kept showing that cold look on her face, totally","ignoring everyone.","There were so many Spiritual Armament Masters around so an apprentice like","Huang Yueli was very insignificant. No one even noticed her at all.","She was happy with the peace and walked in by herself.","But she looked around everywhere and didn’t see the legendary Grandmaster","Xiao, “ho was supposed to give the lecture today.","She was just about to ask someone when she suddenly heard a rather familiar","voice from behind. “Ihere’re so many attendees here today! It’s almost time for","the lecture so we have to grab hold of time quickly. Grandmaster Bai is having","a chat with Grandmaster Xiao, so theyd be coming out very soon!”","Huang Yueli recognized the voice. Wasn’t that person the same Spiritual","Armament Master who admitted her the last time?","She turned her head around and indeed saw that young Spiritual Armament","Master talking to someone.","She turned her head back and coincidentally met with that person,","recognized her at one glance.","“You.. aren’t you that person from that time... what’s your name again? Right,","you’re called Li Yuehuang right? Your name is really strange!” His impression","of Huang Yueli was very deep because this Lower Realm ascender was just too","strange. He had never seen anyone with so much self-confidence before.","Alas, no matter how confident she was, a Spirit Armament wasn’t that easy to","be refined!","The admission officer said, “Why? It’s just been a month and you’ve come to","the Sky Gem Glass Chamber again? Have you finished using those materials","that you purchased the other time?”","Huang Yueli nodded. “I’ve indeed finished using it all...”","“l knew it!” Hearing her say those words, the admission officer slapped his","thigh and interrupted her. “Do you know how difficult it is to refine Spirit","Armaments now? I’m sure you know how difficult it is to finish reading those","manuals now! Young man, it’s better not to be too ambitious! Just treat the","money that you spent on purchasing those materials as throwing it into the","drain and learn a lesson from it! You’d better take part in the apprentice","assessments and not daydream!”","Huang Yueli was speechless, and she wanted to explain for herself.","Other than coming to attend Grandmaster Xiao’s lecture today, she also wanted","to submit her Spirit Armament and apply to become an official Spiritual","Armament Master.","But before she could say a word, that Spiritual Armament Master jumped up.","“Ah, Grandmaster Xiao and Grandmaster Bai are out!!! ‘me lecture’s about to","start! I have to hurry over. You can go into the Books Depository to take a look","on your ov?vn. I don’t have time to entertain you today!”","Huang Yueli lifted her head and saw two elderly men slowly walking along the","rear courtyard’s corridor from a distance away.","One of them was Grandmaster Bai, whom she had met previously. other","looked rather scholarly. From the looks of this, he should be the legendary top","rated Sky Gem Grandmaster, Grandmaster Xiao.","The admission officer immediately rushed over.","Seeing him leave , Huang Yueli called out to him hurriedly. “Wait, this senior,","I’m also here to attend Grandmaster Xiao’s lecture. I don’t Imow where the","lecture hall is, bring me along!”","The admission officer’s footsteps took a halt, and he frowned.. “What did you","say? You are here to attend the lecture too? You’re not even a Spiritual","Armament Master, so can you even understand the lecture?”"]},{"number":2930,"title":"Chapter 2930 - Free Show (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 2930 : Free Show (2)","Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Huang Yueli knew that he didn’t believe in her ability so she didn’t bother to spend too much effort to explain. She only said, “Grandmaster Xiao is so famous. I’m sure I will be able to learn a lot of things from listening to his lecture.","The admission officer cast a glance at her as his eyes reflected unconcealable contempt.","“I say, can you know where you stand? Those who can attend Grandmaster","Xiao’s lecture are all genuine Spiritual Armament Masters bearing the Sky Gem Glass Chambers badges! The contents in Grandmaster Xiao’s lecture are extremely profound and you apprentices will not be able to understand it. Moreover speaking, there are so many apprentices in the entire Flame Square","City. If everyone were to attend it, there wouldn’t be enough seats at all. Flame Square City’s branch President had already passed down the instructions that only Spiritual Armament Masters will be able to enter the venue. You can stop dreaming about this and go back earlier!”","The admission office bore a haughty look on his face. But he wasn’t picking on","Huang Yueli. It was a kind of arrogance that came naturally from a Spiritual Armament Master!","A Spiritual Armament apprentice required a very high innate talent and there might only be one or two in every ten thousand people. Because when ordinary practitioners saw Spiritual Armament apprentices, they felt that these people were extremely incredible.","But it was an extremely difficult task to be promoted to a genuine Spiritual Armament Master from an apprentice.","In every one hundred apprentices, there would only be four or five people who could obtain the Spiritual Armament Master’s badge, which was even less than","10% of the passing rate.","Hence, to a Spiritual Armament Master, they wouldn’t bother about an entry-level apprentice at all.","Huang Yueli knew this clearly so she wasn’t very upset over this.","She thought for a moment and opened her mouth to ask, “Then now, if I were to....” take part in the Spiritual Armament Master’s assessment, would that be","alright?","However, before she could finish her sentence, she heard a familiar voice coming from afar. “Eh? Aren’t you that day’s... you’re called Li Yuehuang, am I right?”","Huang Yueli and the Spiritual Armament Master beside her turned around in astonishment and saw Grandmaster Bai walking towards them.","She had a favorable impression of Grandmaster Bai and when she saw that he recognized her, she immediately cupped her fists and bowed, “Grandmaster Bai.’","When he saw her, he nodded his head satisfactorily. But instantly thought of something and frowned. Then he asked in a displeased voice, “Why? Why have you come to the Sky Gem Glass Chamber again? Didn’t you say that you won’t be staying long in Flame Square City that day?”","“Ughh, this...”","Huang Yueli was stunned and immediately recalled that she had once used this excuse to reject Grandmaster Bai’s request to take her as his disciple.","Her eyeballs rolled and she said, “Grandmaster Bai, originally I was about to leave. But I heard that Grandmaster Xiao is going to conduct a lecture here today. So I intentionally stayed behind to attend this lecture. But it seems that I’ve made a wasted trip. I didn’t expect an apprentice like me to not have the right to attend the lecture...”","Grandmaster Bai’s brows rose when he heard that.","To tell the truth, he lamented silently for a long time after Huang Yueli left that day!","An armament refining genius with such outstanding innate talent and power of comprehension was so hard to come across! Alas, she wasn’t willing to stay in Flame Square City to learn armament refining skills!","Now that he met her once again, it was simply a joyful surprise!","This young man knew to come to listen to Grandmaster Xiao’s lecture. This meant that he had developed an interest in armament refining skills!","Since she had the interest, it was very good because she might change her mind to acknowledge him as her Master!","Thinking of this, Grandmaster Bai felt that he should give her a helping hand and also let her know the advantage of having a Master.","“Since you’re here, it’s alright to come to attend the lecture. Anyway, it’s just one extra seat. We have enough seats for you...’"]},{"number":2931,"title":"Chapter 2931 - Free Show (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Huang Yueli cried out in surprise, “Really? Then I’ll have to thank Grandmaster Bai for this!”","She intentionally mentioned this to him but it was out of her expectations for him to agree so readily.","On seeing that Grandmaster Bai had agreed, the Spiritual Armament Master beside her couldn’t say anything about it. He gave a harrumph and led Huang Yueli to the rear courtyard.","There was a stage in the courtyard. Grandmaster Bai and Grandmaster Xiao were already walking towards it.","The place below the stage was filled with tables and chairs, and quite a number of Spiritual Armament Masters had already taken their seats.","Huang Yueli found a place in the corner and sat down.","When the admission officer saw that, he snorted softly. “It’s good that this fellow knows his limits!” He didn’t bother about Huang Yueli and looked for other Spiritual Armament Masters who he was familiar with to sit with them.","After a while later, Li Leyun also walked in from the other corridor.","When she appeared, all the other Spiritual Armament Masters’ eyes lit up!","“It’s Young Miss Leyun! Young Miss Leyun is here!”","“Young Miss Leyun, look here. I’ve saved the best seat for you. You can hear the lecture from here the clearest!”","“Stop dreaming. Why would Young Miss Leyun want to sit with you? Didn’t you see that President Gao had accompanied her here personally?”","Huang Yueli looked over curiously and saw a middle-aged man standing next to the beautiful Spiritual Armament Master. A Sky Gem Grandmaster badge was pinned on his chest and it seemed that he was the presiding officer in charge of Flame Square City’s Sky Gem Glass Chamber.","President Gao brought Li Leyun over to meet Grandmaster Xiao.","After they exchanged conventional greetings, President Gao pointed to the young lady next to him and introduced her. “Grandmaster Xiao, this is Spiritual Armament Master Leyun who came to Flame Square city on an experience learning trip. Young Miss Leyun isn’t even thirty years old yet but she’s already a mid rank Spiritual Armament Master. Her innate talent is really outstanding! She worships Grandmaster Xiao, you, a lot!”","President Gao was a humble man and he was especially glad to help the younger generation with outstanding innate talent. Hence he naturally had high expectations for Li Leyun.","On the contrary, Grandmaster Xiao’s response was much colder.","A mid rank Spiritual Armament Master under thirty years old might sound impressive to ordinary people, but Grandmaster Xiao had met plenty of them!","He nodded slightly. “Her innate talent is not bad, indeed a talent. She should be nurtured well!”","Although he said it politely, he didn’t even look at Li Leyun in the eyes at all. Apparently, he didn’t think much of her.","When Li Leyun saw his look, she felt her anger rising!","She was Cloudy Qilin Clan Leader’s niece. Usually, who wouldn’t fawn on her and praise about her armament refining innate talent! This old man looked as though he wasn’t interested in her at all!","She didn’t even despise this old man for being a lowly human race!","Luckily, Li Leyun remembered that Flame Square City was the Sacred Phoenix Race’s turf, so she forced herself to swallow this anger and went down the stage to take her seat.","The Spiritual Armament Masters below the stage all swarmed around her, envious that she had the chance to get so close to Grandmaster Xiao.","Li Leyun sneered silently and ignored those human race Spiritual Armament Masters.","Huang Yueli hid in the corner and saw everything.","“Tsk tsk, this kind of person hangs around everywhere! I got to watch a free show again!” Huang Yueli shook her head.","Grandmaster Xiao got up on the stage and shortly after, she officially started his lecture.","Huang Yueli cast Li Leyun behind her mind and started to listen attentively.","The lecture had just started for a moment and Huang Yueli realized that Grandmaster Xiao lived up to his name for being God Realm’s first rated Sky Gem Grandmaster!","He had in-depth research in the refining of Spirit Armaments.."]},{"number":2932,"title":"Chapter 2932 - Free Show (4)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","The only thought that Huang Yueli had in mind was to refine the strongest weapon for Li Moying, so she listened extremely attentively.","She learned a lot of things from Grandmaster Xiao’s analysis.","All the questions that she had when she read the books were all resolved.","Huang Yueli was very engrossed, and she felt that Grandmaster Xiao’s lecture was truly great.","But to many of the Spiritual Armament Masters here, they were not feeling the same.","In reality, a majority of them totally couldn’t understand what Grandmaster Xiao was talking about!","Although many of them had passed various assessments and became genuine Spiritual Armament Masters, most of them had scraped past the courses through memorization. They were not clear of the underlying principle at all.","Moreover, when they were refining armaments, they had to strictly follow according to the indications in the blueprint. So they only knew very few kinds of Spirit Armaments.","Once the materials in their hands had some slight changes or if the external conditions were different, their refinement would definitely fail!","But Grandmaster Xiao’s lecture was all related to the most basic principles of armament refining. In these people’s ears, it was no different from reading a hieroglyphic!","When the lecture started, a majority of the Spirit Armament Masters below the stage were dazed because they couldn’t understand the contents at all!","Although they didn’t dare to talk in front of Grandmaster Xiao, their minds were already wandering and all of them had already gone into a trance!","It was the same for the Spiritual Armament Master who admitted Huang Yueli. He sat upright and still while sneaking glances around.","Li Leyun was seated right in front of him, and she was listening attentively.","He couldn’t help but think silently, “As expected from Young Miss Leyun, her innate talent is much stronger than us by so much! She’s probably the only one who can understand Grandmaster Xiao’s lecture in this entire place!”","The admission officer sighed and turned his gaze elsewhere.","When he looked in Huang Yueli’s direction, he was stunned.","Huang Yueli propped her chin with one hand and her eyes were glued to the stage without blinking. She was extremely focused in listening to the lecture and she would nod occasionally, as though she was echoing in agreement to what Grandmaster Xiao said.","The admission officer went into a blank and sneered, “He’s so good at pretending! Grandmaster Xiao’s lecture is so profound so how could an apprentice like him possibly understand this? He even showed such an expression, he’s really good at pretending!”","However, Huang Yueli didn’t notice that someone was looking at her.","She placed all her attention on Grandmaster Xiao. She was listening to him analyze the armaments far away and also watching him display the method on stage.","At the same time, she compared her refining process against Grandmaster Xiao’s method.","‘Oh, so it’s supposed to be treated in this way. Mmm, yes, it’s logical. In this way, the blade will be even sharper... Hmm, if a few more reflection points are added to the energy field, it would indeed double up the power! Grandmaster Xiao is so incredible!”","“But...” After a moment later, she frowned puzzledly. “It seems a little strange on the way of handling this here. Grandmaster Xiao says that adding this array pattern would increase a total of 30% power. But there’s a pattern array that can increase up to 40%. I’ve already verified it for myself! Why didn’t Grandmaster Xiao use it? Could there be other problems? Later I’ll need to clarify my doubts!”","By the time Grandmaster Xiao was done with his lecture, Huang Yueli had already discovered about four to five similar doubts.","Finally, Grandmaster Xiao stopped and drank some water.","“Alright, I shall stop my lecture here today. Now, we’ll be going into the next segment..’"]},{"number":2933,"title":"Chapter 2933 - Free Show (5)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","President Gao hurriedly took over when he heard that. “Grandmaster Xiao had said that he would personally comment on the Spirit Armaments that everyone brought. It’s a rare chance for such an outstanding Sky Gem Grandmaster like Grandmaster Xiao to give you some pointers, so please don’t miss it!”","Hearing that, all the Spiritual Armament Masters began to stir with excitement!","Although everyone did not understand the lecture, they did not leave because they had been waiting for this moment!","Even Huang Yueli could not sit still!","She had a lot of questions and was hoping that she could have an in-depth discussion with Grandmaster Xiao!","The city walls soared high into the clouds at the Sacred Phoenix Continent.","Li Moymg brought along his guards and was about to enter the city via carnage.","“Wait, the three of you, stop there. What are your identities and where did you come from?” The trio was stopped when they had just arrived at the city gates.","Li Moymg frowned slightly, not expecting Sacred Phoenix Race’s men to conduct such strict checking. Everyone, who was entering the city, had to line up and be checked.","In this way, that meant that Sacred Phoenix Race’s men hadn’t found his Li’er as well...","Actually, Cloudy Qilin clan’s practitioners had always been rejected by the Sacred Phoenix Race. Luckily, Li Moying was already prepared and made some slight changes to his clothes. He removed all the items which bore the Cloudy Qilin clan’s markings on him.","Li Tian Yi walked up and after a period of socializing with the Sacred Phoenix Race’s guards, they entered the city successfully.","After they entered, Li Moying hurriedly went to the gathering point in Flame Square City where he was supposed to meet with up the others.","The guards had arrived earlier than him and when they saw Li Moyingwalking in, all of them swarmed up and bowed to him respectfully.","Li Moymg waved his hand impatiently and said, “Alright, dispense with the formalities. I asked you to search for Li’er’s traces in the neighboring towns. Has anyone found any clues?","Hearing that, everyone turned silent.","“Young Master Moying, this..","“This Subordinate has failed to complete the mission. Will Young Master please mete out my punishment!”","“We’ve already checked with the neighboring towns and cities but no one had seen that young lady that you described...”","The guards started to speak cautiously. The more they spoke, the more apprehensive they got.","Speaking of that, the person whom Li Moying made them search for was very special.","From Li Moying’s description, Sacred Phoenix Race’s peerless genius was extremely beautiful. For a young lady of this caliber, no matter where she went to, she would easily attract everyone’s attention so it was impossible that they couldn’t find her at all.","But under such a large-scale search, there was still no news of her so the chances of survival were not high.","Everyone was thinking of the same thing but yet no one dared to say it out!","Li Moymg had already said that the young lady was his Lower Realm’s wife.","They had deep feelings for each other. If she really died when she just arrived","in God Realm... no one knew if their Young Master would be able to take this blow!","If it wasn’t for the fact that they saw Sacred Phoenix Race’s men also searching high and low for her, they might think that this was Sacred Phoenix Race’s plot to deal with their Young Master a blow!","Li Moymg’s expression sank gradually and his hands were clenched tightly into fists. His fingers etched deeply into his palms.","Li’er... his Li’er..","What danger did she meet with? Why was there still no news of her until today?","At this moment, Li Moying was feeling extremely regretful. Why didn’t he manage to reach Soul Connection Ocean earlier, and take her away right before the Sacred Phoenix Race’s men had found her!","After a round of discussion, one of them stood out and passed a letter to Li Moymg.","“Young Master, we’ve received Clan Leader’s letter, urgmg you to return to","Amethyst Paramount Palace as soon as possible...”"]},{"number":2934,"title":"Chapter 2934 - Free Show (6)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","The guard submitted the letter, took a few steps back, bowed, and stood still feeling terrified.","Actually, ever since Li Moying left Cloudy Qilin Continent, the clan had sent numerous letters urgmg him to return.","However, Li Moying had turned a deaf ear to it, and the guards didn’t dare to use this matter to disturb him.","But this time, the Clan Leader had personally sent the letter telling him that if he still didn’t return, he would come personally to capture him back!","That was why the guards didn’t dare to hide this any longer, passing the letter to him.","Whoever knew, Li Moying didn’t bother to take a look at it. He simply threw the letter on the ground!","“That’s enough. Didn’t I already tell you that you can ignore whoever tries to urge me! If I can’t find Huang Yueli, I will never go back! Do you disregard my instructions? If you want me to return, why don’t you spend more effort and try to find her!”","The guards looked at the letter which had landed in the mud, and they were crying bitterly in their hearts.","Since when did they not put in any effort at all? But she had vanished in thin air so there was nothing they could do about it!","Seeing that Li Moying was on the verge of an explosion, Li Tian Yi suddenly had an idea. He walked up and persuaded, “Young Master, don’t be anxious. Today, there’s still one more guard who hasn’t come back to meet up with us. That person is Tian Wu, who you sent to Ice Moon Summit to find out more news! Perhaps Sacred Phoenix Race had already found some clues, so let’s wait for his return before we take the next step!”","Li Moying heard that and calmed down.","Indeed, Sacred Phoenix Race had sent a lot more people than his subordinates.","Moreover, only Sacred Phoenix Race was most clear about Huang Yueli’s","situation .","“Alright, let’s wait for Tian Wu here for a couple of days. The rest of you, continue to search around the cities and towns nearby. Be careful, don’t let the Sacred Phoenix Race’s men discover us!”","The guards hurriedly responded to him and were about to leave when someone suddenly seemed to recall something and stopped.","“Young Master, there’s one more thing...”","“What is it?” Li Moying’s patience was almost worn out.","The guard hurriedly said, “Young Miss Leyun had also arrived in Flame Square City one month ago and she had been waiting for your return. What do you","“Li Leyun? What’s she doing here?” Li Moying frowned angrily.","“This... I heard that a famous Sky Gem Grandmaster is giving a lecture in Flame Square City and she specially came to attend it. She’s currently in the Sky Gem Glass Chamber...","“What do Li Leyun’s whereabouts have to do with This Young Master? Is this matter even worth wasting time over? In the future, there’s no need to tell me about it! Hurry up and go search for her!”","“Yes! This Subordinate will go right away!”","Seeing Li Moying getting slightly angry, the guards were extremely terrified. They didn’t dare to waste any time and hurriedly left to search for her.","Only Li Tian Yi stayed beside Li Moymg as his personal guard. He looked at Li Moymg’s cold face from the side and couldn’t help but sigh silently.","Li Leyun had specially come to Flame Square City and everyone knew that it was because she wanted to meet Li Moying and go on experience learning with him so that their feelings would grow over time.","Alas, the dropping flowers pinned for love but the heartless brook babbled on. Li Moymg wasn’t interested in her at all...","Sky Gem Glass Chamber.","After President Gao finished his sentence, the Spiritual Armament Masters started to raise their hands, hoping to attract Grandmaster Xiao’s attention.","“Grandmaster Xiao, I have a question!”","“Grandmaster Xiao, This Junior has brought a few Spirit Armaments along. I hope that you can give me some pointers!”","The scene was extremely chaotic so President Gao coughed loudly and picked a person, “Yuankang, you go first!”","Ji Yuankang, whose name was called, was only 35 years old but was already a mid rank Spiritual Armament Master.."]},{"number":2935,"title":"Chapter 2935 - This Is The Real Genius! (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Although his innate talent was slightly weaker than Li Leyun, he was President Gao’s favorite disciple, a resident Spiritual Armament Master with the highest innate talent in Flame Square City.","As compared to an outsider Spiritual Armament Master like Li Leyun, he enjoyed some special privileges.","Everyone didn’t dare to make a sound when they saw him, and could only watch him walking up the stage delightfully.","“This Junior, Ji Yuankang, would like to ask Grandmaster Xiao for some pointers!”","Ji Yuankang bowed deeply and took out the Spirit Armaments that he had refined, leaving it on the podium.","That was an extremely sharp cutlass. Both the blade and handle were engraved with ocher-colored plume array patterns.","Huang Yueli immediately recognized it. This was one of the weapons that she had seen on the Spirit Armament Illustration Book, the Crismon Plume Cutlass.","She had to admit that Ji Yuankang’s armament refining skills weren’t too bad. This Crimson Plume Cutlass was exactly the same in the illustration book. It had been perfectly restored. From its luster, it could be considered to be one of the fine quality mid grade Spirit Armaments.","As expected, when this Crimson Plume Cutlass was brought out, it instantly attracted the Spiritual Armament Masters’ gasps, and they were praising Ji Yuankangs workmanship.","Li Leyun was the only one who sneered. Did he want to get Grandmaster Xiao’s pointers just based on this ordinary Spirit Armament? Simply overestimating himself! These lowly human races were so ill-informed!","The reality was exactly the same as what she thought.","When Grandmaster Xiao saw that Crimson Plume Cutlass, he frowned after taking a glance at it. “The Spirit Armament that you want me to see is this Crimson Plume Cutlass?”","“Yes!” Ji Yuankang replied respectfully, feeling confident.","Grandmaster Xiao sneered. “It’s just a standard weapon from the Spirit","Armament Illustration Book and so badly done! The standard of mid rank Spiritual Armament Masters is very low now!”","This was simply akin to telling Ji Yuankang in his face that he was not fit to be a mid rank Spiritual Armament Master.","All the praises and gasps suddenly stopped instantly and everyone looked awkward.","President Gao’s beloved disciple was criticized in such a manner, and he felt as though he was put on the spot. But he knew Grandmaster Xiao’s temper. He was an extremely proud man who always spoke his mind. Ji Yuankang could only blame himself for his lack of skills.","So he could only say, “Yuankang, didn’t you hear what Grandmaster Xiao said?","You need to work harder and practice even more! What are you waiting for? Aren’t you getting off the stage?","Ji Yuankang felt humiliated so he could only leave the stage dejectedly.","President Gao cleared his throat and said, “Who else wants to come up the stage to ask Grandmaster Xiao for some pointers?”","It was completely silent below the stage.","Originally, those Spiritual Armament Masters were fighting to get on the stage. But when they saw Ji Yuankang being mercilessly despised, who dared to go up on stage? Their skills were much worse than Ji Yuankang!","Just at this moment, a melodious voice rang within the crowd.","“Mid rank Spiritual Armament Master Leyun would like to ask Grandmaster Xiao for your pointers!”","The voice stopped, and Li Leyun stood up from her seat. No one was there to fight with her, and she directly walked towards the stage.","Grandmaster Xiao nodded noncommittally.","Li Leyun felt displeased on seeing his arrogant attitude!","This old man was just a human race, how dare he be so disrespectful towards the noble God clan! If it wasn’t because he had some skills, she wouldn’t even want to bear with this at all!","But all these were just temporary. Grandmaster Xiao would definitely have a change of attitude when he saw the Spirit Armament that she refined.","Li Leyun was extremely confident, and her right hand flipped around to retrieve three pieces of Spirit Armaments from her realm ring. She lined it up and placed it on the podium.."]},{"number":2936,"title":"Chapter 2936 - This Is The Real Genius! (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","“Wow, what are those?”","“Incredible, she took three mid grade Spirit Armaments out at the same time!”","“That’s not all! I’ve never seen those few Spirit Armaments that Young Miss Leyun is holding in the illustration book at all!”","Li Leyun’s Spirit Armament left everyone stunned.","Even Huang Yueli’s brows rose in surprise.","The three Spirit Armaments that Li Leyun took out were all long swords. Moreover, those were something that she had not seen in the illustration books. Apparently, they were much higher grades than those ordinary standard Spirit Armaments.","Grandmaster Xiao’s eyes also lit up. “These three long swords... This is the first time I’ve seen them! From the looks of it, these should be some special illustrations which some big forces have kept right? If I didn’t see it wrongly, these three long swords’ attacks are much higher than standard Spirit Armaments by 30%. Moreover, there should be additional Profound Skills attached to it!”","Li Leyun felt extremely delighted when she heard Grandmaster Xiao talking about her Spirit Armament’s merits. Her chin was raised high up as she looked at the crowd disdainfully.","Based on her innate talent and ability, sitting next to these human race Spiritual Armament Masters to attend the lecture was simply an insult!","“Grandmaster Xiao, you have good eyesight! These three long swords of mine are all refined based on my clan’s inherited illustrated books. The illustrations are extremely complex and I spent a great deal of effort before I managed to refine them successfully.”","Li Leyun’s words sounded calm but in reality, they carried a hint of flaunting. She was just waiting for Grandmaster Xiao to praise her.","Whoever knew that Grandmaster Xiao suddenly frowned shortly after he focused on the three weapons for a while.","“These three weapons illustrations are indeed extraordinary! But...”","“But what?” Li Leyun asked surprisedly.","“But your refining skills are apparently out of practice. Various areas of the energy field’s fine details are treated very crudely, not to mention that there are several array patterns which are wrong!”","Saying that, Grandmaster Xiao put on a regretful look and shook his head. “It’s a waste of such exquisite illustrations and so many high grade spirit armament materials, yet coming out with such disappointing Spirit Armaments! A waste, simply a huge waste!”","Hearing Grandmaster Xiao’s comments, everyone was stunned.","Li Leyun’s face flushed red. “You... how dare you say that about me! I’m just a mid rank Spiritual Armament Master. There are not many people who can refine these Spirit Armaments! I’m already considered a genius!”","When she was in the Cloudy Qilin clan, she had always been fawned on by the clan’s Sky Gem Grandmasters. Who dared to say that the Spirit Armaments that she refined weren’t good!","But now Grandmaster Xiao said this and her anger just flared up. She immediately couldn’t stand it any longer!","Grandmaster Xiao wasn’t an easy-going person as well. He immediately snorted coldly. “Why? You are not convinced when I said that about you? You’re just slightly better than that young lad earlier. But if you claim that you’re an armament refining genius, it’s really very far off! Do you know how many mistakes you committed in those few Spirit Armaments that you refined?","Everyone, look at this...”","Grandmaster Xiao originally couldn’t be bothered to bicker with Li Leyun but on hearing her rebuke him, he suddenly got inspired and started to pick out all the mistakes that she had made. He started to rant endlessly on it.","After speaking for around one hour, he felt thirsty and stopped. “Let’s stop here first. There are just so many low level mistakes! You still have the cheek to call yourself a genius?","Li Leyun’s face was extremely red, and she was furious.. But yet she couldn’t say a single word to rebuke him, so she was feeling very aggrieved!"]},{"number":2937,"title":"Chapter 2937 - This Is The Real Genius! (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Grandmaster Xiao might be sharp -tongued but what he said was not wrong at all!","Every mistake he pointed out was true.","The three Spirit Armaments that Li Leyun was so proud of were indeed inadequate. But she didn’t expect him to point it out so directly!","Seeing a genius like her, shouldn’t everyone be encouragmg and praising her instead? Why would he pick on her over a small mistake?","She felt extremely aggrieved, especially when she noticed the Spiritual Armament Master’s gazes below the stage. It made her wish that she could dig a hole and hide in the ground!","Seeing her stand at the original spot not moving, Grandmaster Xiao looked at her impatiently. “Why? Do you still have any other questions to ask?”","Li Leyun wished that she could punch Grandmaster Xiao’s face. But this was the Sacred Phoenix Race’s turf so she didn’t dare to create trouble here!","Moreover, if she continued to argue with Grandmaster Xiao, she didn’t know what other ways would he pick on her Spirit Armaments again!","No matter what, she was in the wrong for this matter!","Li Leyun was extremely furious but there was nothing she could do about it. Hence she hissed through her teeth, “Thank you Grandmaster Xiao for your pointers!”","After that, she swiftly kept away her Spirit Armaments and left the stage dejectedly.","If one was to compare how complacent she was earlier on the stage, then she would be incomparably disheveled right now!","Moreover, she was a person with a lot of pride. After being embarrassed in such a way, there was no way that she could continue to stay on in the Sky Gem Glass Chamber.","Li Leyun directly walked towards the door, preparing to leave this goddamn place!","Grandmaster Xiao saw her actions and didn’t think much of it. He had met plenty of the so-called “Genius Spiritual Armament Masters” who had slightly better innate talent!","Not to mention himself, even ordinary Sky Gem Grandmasters like President Gao or Grandmaster Bai weren’t any weaker than Li Leyun when they were young. Who did this lass think she was, who would bother to fawn on her?","President Gao felt slightly awkward but he couldn’t scold Grandmaster Xiao hence he coughed loudly again.","“Cough cough, cough cough, everyone please keep quiet! Now, are there any other people who would like to ask Grandmaster Xiao for pointers on their Spirit Armaments? The time is not early any longer so will everyone please grab hold of time quickly!” President Gao attempted to ease the commotion.","Hearing his words, the Spiritual Armament Masters looked at each other in dismay but no one dared to make a sound.","Originally, everyone wanted to ask for some comments, with the hope to gain some praise from Grandmaster Xiao to raise their status.","But now, they realized that Grandmaster Xiao wouldn’t praise anyone at all. Even a genius like Li Leyun who was on stage got criticized so badly. Who else would dare to go up? Wouldn’t they be asking for a scolding?","Seeing that the commotion had turned cold, President Gao urged once again. “Is there no one else who’d like to come up on stage? This is a rare chance! If there’s no one else, then the lecture shall end here today!”","President Gao would be very happy if no one went up.","The earlier it ended, the lesser Grandmaster Xiao would deal a blow to the younger Spiritual Armament Masters!","Right now, Li Leyun had already walked to the entrance and was just about to walk out.","Right now, Li Leyun had already walked to the entrance and was just about to walk out.","She heard President Gao’s words, and a sneer surfaced on her lips/","She had already been scolded and sent off the stage. Who else would dare to go up? Flame Square City’s Spiritual Armament Masters was a bunch of trash who couldn’t even be compared to a finger of hers! Who would dare to go on stage?","But just at this moment, she suddenly heard a voice coming from her back.","“Grandmaster Xiao, I have a few Spirit Armaments that I’d like to ask for your comments!”"]},{"number":2938,"title":"Chapter 2938 - This Is The Real Genius! (4)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","What?!","There’s someone else who wished to ask Grandmaster Xiao for pointers??","Hearing that voice, every Spiritual Armament Master present, including Grandmaster Bai and President Bai, were stunned.","Everyone had the same thought in mind. ‘Could it be that among the Spiritual Armament Masters today, there was an even more talented Spiritual Armament Master than Young Miss Leyun hidden in the audience? Otherwise, who would dare to ask for pointers after her? Wasn’t that person asking to be shamed?”","President Gao was initially prepared to announce the end of the lecture. His words were stuck at the back of his throat.","He hurriedly coughed. “Cough cough, which Spiritual Armament Master wishes to come on stage? Since there’s no queue, just come up directly!”","Everyone turned and looked around at the same time, hoping to find that “incredible genius” in the crowd.","Even Li Leyun also stopped. She turned around, wanting to see which Spiritual Armament Master had self-proclaimed himself to be even more talented than her!","A figure slowly stood up from a corner and strode towards the stage.","After everyone took a clear look, their eyes widened and their eyeballs almost dropped on the ground.","“This... this... who is this person? Why haven’t I seen him before?”","“I’ve never seen him before either!”","There’s a number of foreign Spiritual Armament Masters who came by today so it’s very normal that you haven’t seen him around. But... look at the badge on his chest. It’s a Spiritual Armament apprentice badge, right?”","“You’re right, he’s really a Spiritual Armament apprentice!”","“A fella who isn’t even a Spiritual Armament Master wants to ask Grandmaster","Xiao for pointers? Is he mad?”","“Hahahaha, things are getting interesting. A baby calf isn’t afraid of the tiger! Young Miss Leyun had already been scolded by Grandmaster Xiao that badly. I wonder if he will be thrown out of this place directly!”","Seeing such a comical fellow, the Spiritual Armament Masters all started to relax in the original gloomy atmosphere in the courtyard.","Even Li Leyun also felt that it wasn’t as embarrassing as before. She silently thought that even the heavens were helping her!","This fellow would definitely be scolded by Grandmaster Xiao so badly that he would doubt what he had been doing for his entire life. By then, she wouldn’t be the most embarrassed person!","Thinking of this, Li Leyun wasn’t in a hurry to leave any longer. She leaned against the door and waited to see how this unlucky person would embarrass himself!","Grandmaster Bai couldn’t help but frown upon seeing Huang Yueli walking out from the corner.","When she walked nearer, Grandmaster Bai hurriedly spoke out before her,","“Little Li, what are you doing? This isn’t a place where you can make trouble!","Grandmaster Xiao said earlier that he would only accept those Spiritual Armament Masters who brought along the Spirit Armaments that they have refined. So don’t join in the crowd! Quickly go down!”","Grandmaster Bai had a solemn expression and his tone was extremely fierce.","But Huang Yueli knew that this Grandmaster did that because he admired her innate talent. He was worried that she wouldn’t be able to stand the scolding by Grandmaster Xiao hence he intentionally chased her away.","So Huang Yueli didn’t think much of it and said with a smile, “Grandmaster Bai, you’re worrying too much! This Junior knows the rules. Since I’ve come to ask Grandmaster Xiao for pointers, of course, I’ve brought my own Spirit Armaments that I’ve refined!”","“You refined a Spirit Armament??” Grandmaster Bai stared at her as though he had just seen a ghost. “Little Li, stop talking rubbish! Grandmaster Xiao hates young people who overestimate themselves!”","The Spiritual Armament Masters below the stage started to burst out laughing.","A Spiritual Armament apprentice bringing out his Spirit Armament? What kind of joke was that?","If she could refine Spirit Armaments, she would have applied for the Spirit Armament Master’s badge, right?","Huang Yueli didn’t make any unnecessary explanations. Her expression was indifferent as she raised her right hand. Three Spirit Armaments then appeared on the platform.."]},{"number":2939,"title":"Chapter 2939 - This Is The Real Genius! (5)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Three Spirit Armaments appeared and everyone sucked in a breath of cold air.","Even Li Leyun’s eyes widened in disbelief.","The reason was that those three might be all Spirit Armaments, but Huang Yueli took out three different types!","One was a long sword, another was an armor while the last piece was an extremely rare jade pendant-shaped Spiritual Artifact!","It wasn’t just the exterior shape that was different, the functions were totally different as well. Hence the energy field within the Spirit Armament and fusion method were different.","Ordinary Spiritual Armament Masters were well versed in only one type. Or perhaps it could be put in this way, most Spiritual Armament Masters could only specialize in one type of Spirit Armament. For example, Spiritual Armament Masters who specialize in refining long swords would have much weaker standards if they were to refine daggers, not to mention armors.","A Sky Gem Grandmaster like Grandmaster Xiao who specialized in refining all weapons was extremely scarce!","But now, Huang Yueli took three different kinds of Spirit Armaments out at once!","Moreover, one of them was the Spiritual Artifact, which was the most difficult thing to refine!","Everyone lost their senses slightly and some of them even rubbed their eyes, not believing in what they were seeing!","Grandmaster Xiao also revealed an astonished expression. After a long pause, he said, “Are these... really something that you’ve refined on your own?","Huang Yueli nodded. “Will Grandmaster Xiao please give me some pointers, please?","This time, Grandmaster Xiao’s expression was no longer disdainful. In replacement was a solemn look.","He took out a set of gloves from his interspatial ring and put it on. Then he carefully picked up the left most long sword. Lifting it against the sunlight, he checked on it carefully.","He checked extremely carefully and turned it around, checking every single fine detail.","Not only that, he even put his gloved finger and gently rubbed against the sword blade, feeling the energy that was released from the engraved array patterns.","Grandmaster Xiao took a very long time to check. Those Spiritual Armament Masters originally stuck out their necks, hoping to hear his evaluation on these Spirit Armaments.","But as time went by, the audience became a little impatient and started to whisper.","“What’s going on? Why is Grandmaster Xiao taking such a long time to check?” “No idea! Could this be that the apprentice’s Spirit Armament is especially outstanding?”","“What joke are you cracking? He’s just an apprentice. Even if this Spirit","Armament is really refined by him, there should be a limit to his standard! Moreover speaking, everyone can recognize those few Spirit Armaments that he refined right? Aren’t those all standardized Spirit Armaments?”","“That’s right. Earlier Young Miss Leyun’s three long swords were all esoteric lore illustrations from her clan and Grandmaster Xiao didn’t even spend that long to look!”","Hearing those Spiritual Armament Masters discuss about her, Li Leyun’s lips twitched and almost flew into a rage again!","The displeasure in her heart towards Grandmaster Xiao increased again!","“Is this old fella blind or what? It’s just a few standardized Spirit Armaments.","What’s there to look at, and he’s taking so long to look! What kind of top rated Sky Gem Grandmaster is he? He can’t even tell the difference between good and bad Spirit Armaments.”","“Is this old fella blind or what? It’s just a few standardized Spirit Armaments.","What’s there to look at, and he’s taking so long to look! What kind of top rated Sky Gem Grandmaster is he? He can’t even tell the difference between good and bad Spirit Armaments.”","Amid everyone’s guesses and discussions, Grandmaster Xiao finally finished checking the Spirit Armament and slowly put down the long sword.","He didn’t check on the remaining two pieces of Spirit Armaments. Instead, he stood up from his seat and cupped his hands in obeisance.","“Your armament refining skills are indeed miraculous works.. It’s an eye-opener for me!”"]},{"number":2940,"title":"Chapter 2940 - This Is The Real Genius! (6)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Grandmaster Xiao’s reaction was simply out of everyone’s expectation.","All the Spiritual Armament Masters’ mouths were agape and they couldn’t make a single sound because their tongues were tied!","They had to be dreaming, right? This was absolutely a dream!","Grandmaster Xiao, an extremely proud Sky Gem Grandmaster famous throughout the entire God Realm, actually... he actually treated a Spiritual Armament apprentice with such respect!","Moreover, he even said that the apprentice’s armament refining skills were","“miraculous works ! ”","Did they hear him wrongly? Or had they met a fake Grandmaster Xiao?","Such a thing... how could it possibly happen?","Even though everyone was in a daze, Huang Yueli remained composed.","She was also shocked that Grandmaster Xiao treated her with such respect. But shortly after, she calmed down and returned the greeting courteously.","“Grandmaster Xiao, you’ve over-praised me! I’ve just started to learn the skill of refining Spirit Armaments and there are many areas that I still can’t grasp.","So I’d like to ask you for your pointers!”","“Just started learning?” Grandmaster Xiao’s brows rose in astonishment.","But he didn’t think too much about this. He only felt that the young man was being humble. After all, as compared to an old fellow like him who was a few hundred years old, a young man who was around thirty years old was indeed considered as “just starting to learn” even if he started when he was ten years old.","“You’re simply too humble! Your Spirit Armament refining skills are self-accomplished and there are many parts of it where it’s a new creation. It had greatly raised the Spirit Armament’s original power! There are many areas which had been improved and this is my first time seeing this. It’s such an eye-opener! I wonder which Grandmaster are you currently studying under?” Grandmaster Xiao’s first reaction was that Huang Yueli had acknowledged an incredible Master who imparted her these exclusive methods.","Huang Yueli narrowed her eyes, not knowing how to answer him.","She didn’t expect the Spirit Armaments that she had refined would gain such high evaluation from Grandmaster Xiao. Originally, she was prepared to be criticized by him.","After all, this was her first time refining Spirit Armaments, so it was understandable if there were flaws to it.","Now that Grandmaster Xiao praised her this much, Huang Yueli started to feel a little vexed.","She had intentionally laid low to conceal her identity, but accidentally gained such fame while she wasn’t paying attention!","Huang Yueli was still hesitating when Grandmaster Xiao frowned and said,","“No, no, no, that’s incorrect! I know all of the famous Spiritual Armament Masters in God Realm and I’m very familiar with their style. None of them are like you... could it be that you created these methods on your own??","Huang Yueli hurriedly said, “Grandmaster Xiao, please stop guessing. My Master had gone into seclusion many years ago! Even if I tell you, you might not know who he is. Moreover, he doesn’t allow me to expose his identity.”","Grandmaster Xiao suddenly became excited upon hearing that. “Which","Grandmaster is your Master? Did he already advance into the Life Profound Realm? Can I meet him to get some pointers?”","Towards Huang Yueli’s excuse of some Master, Grandmaster Xiao didn’t doubt her at all.","Because Huang Yueli simply looked too young!","Although she had already disguised herself into a thirty over year old person, this age in God realm was considered as an adult.."]},{"number":2941,"title":"Chapter 2941 - An Extra (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Becoming a Spiritual Armament Master at this age meant that his innate talent wasn’t too bad.","But to come up with an innovative method of refining armaments? How was that possible?","Grandmaster Xiao totally didn’t believe in such a ridiculous thing!","It wasn’t just Grandmaster Xiao. Even other people present also thought in the same way. So everyone quickly accepted Huang Yueli’s excuse that her Master was a very able person who had gone into seclusion.","Below the stage, the Spiritual Armament Master who had admitted Huang Yueli had a regretful look on his face.","“No wonder! No wonder this Li Yuehuang was so arrogant! So, he was really teasing us. His real ability had long surpassed us ordinary Spiritual Armament Masters! Looks like he must have followed his Master and cultivated at places where there are not many people around. That’s why he did not obtain the Spiritual Armament Master’s badge! If I had known, I should have tried to get on good terms with him while no one else knew about this. Perhaps I might even be able to obtain some exclusive illustrations or learn some high level methods!”","Thinking of this, he felt extremely melancholic!","Of course, he was slightly puzzled because Huang Yueli looked as though she was a Lower Realm practitioner. He had probed her a few times and she didn’t refute it. Why did she suddenly have an incredible Master all of a sudden?","But it only took him a little while to convince himself. “I believe that Li Yuehuang doesn’t want to expose his Master, so that’s why he intentionally deceived me! He had been staying in the deep mountains and it’s normal to look so shabby. He looks no different from a country bumpkin from the Lower Realm! Sigh, one indeed can’t be judged based on their looks...”","Grandmaster Bai who had been standing beside Grandmaster Xiao was suddenly enlightened.","“No wonder I wanted to take you in as my disciple and you kept rejecting me!","So, you’ve already got such an incredible Master!”","Huang Yueli smiled and didn’t deny. But neither did she nod her head.","Grandmaster Bai looked at Huang Yueli and sighed. He was still feeling that it was a great pity.","A youngster with such innate talent and comprehension like Huang Yueli was very rare! If he could take her in as his disciple, when she became a top-rate Sky Gem Grandmaster in the future, it would definitely look good on her Master.","But her Master was someone who even Grandmaster Xiao also praised, so there was nothing that Grandmaster Bai could say about it.","Grandmaster Xiao heard the two of them indulge in small talk and he couldn’t help but interrupt out of anxiety.","“Ok, enough. Old Bai, just based on your armament refining standard, don’t try to fight with Young Master Li’s Master for him! You can talk about these in the future. The most important thing now is, Young Master Li, can’t you make it an exception and let me meet with your Master? His armament refining skills are very innovative and I have a premonition that God Realm’s armament refining standard will be greatly improved because of these new methods!”","Huang Yueli started to feel a little embarrassed by Grandmaster Xiao’s repeated questioning.","Where was she going to come out with a Master to show him!","Luckily, her acting skills had always been excellent. She showed a helpless look and shook her head. “Grandmaster Xiao, it’s not that This Junior is unwilling to help you. but... Master’s temper had always been so. I don’t dare to make him angry...”","Huang Yueli had already said it to this extent so if Grandmaster Xiao were to continue asking, he would be too insensitive.","Usually, Grandmaster Xiao would rely on his status and armament refining standard so he had no qualms to show anyone favors. But he was a person whom Huang Yueli wasn’t willing to offend.."]},{"number":2942,"title":"Chapter 2942 - An Extra (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Since he couldn’t meet with Huang Yueli’s Master, then only she would be able to answer his doubts.","Thinking of this, Grandmaster Xiao pulled Huang Yueli’s sleeve.","“Alright, since Senior doesn’t wish to meet anyone, I can’t force it upon him. Then... Young Master Li, since you’ve brought out these Spirit Armaments to show me, I believe that you must want to explore the armament refining method, am I right? Then let’s go to a quiet place and have a good discussion!” Saying that, he tugged Huang Yueli’s sleeve and wanted to walk inside.","“Ughh, this...”","To tell the truth, Huang Yueli was slightly overwhelmed by Grandmaster Xiao’s overly enthusiastic attitude!","Until now, she still hadn’t understood what the problem was with the Spirit Armament that she had refined, for him to act in such an astonishing manner!","She remembered that she had strictly followed the illustration book to refine the Spirit Armament?","Although she had made some modifications on her own, her experience wasn’t enough so there weren’t a lot of parts that she had modified...","But now, Grandmaster Xiao acted so passionately as though her Spirit Armament was extremely outstanding. This was simply surprising...","Huang Yueli’s dazed look was seen by Li Leyun, who was still standing by the door.","She stayed behind, originally to see Huang Yueli becoming a joke. Whoever knew that things would take such an unexpected turn. It was totally different from what she had anticipated!","Not only did the Spirit Armaments that she brought out not being despised by Grandmaster Xiao, he even treated her with such a sincere attitude!","Not only did he praise her Spirit Armaments, he even wanted to explore the Spirit Armament refining method with her!","This was simply placing Huang Yueli on the same level as herself!","But no matter how Li Leyun thought, she felt that thin fellow was just a Spirit","Armament apprentice! What means did he had, to let Grandmaster treat him in such a way?","Moreover, the three Spirit Armaments that he took out didn’t look very extraordinary. Weren’t those just standardized Spirit Armaments?","Seeing Huang Yueli and Grandmaster Xiao about to leave, Li Leyun couldn’t hold it in any longer and stepped forward while calling out loudly, “Wait a minute!”","Her voice was very loud and very unexpected, so everyone couldn’t help but turn back to look at her.","President Gao looked up and said in a surprised tone, “Young Miss Le? Why are you still here? Didn’t you leave earlier?”","Hearing that, Li Leyun almost threw up blood!","To her, it sounded as though he couldn’t wait for her to leave!","When she came, she was a talent that everyone looked up to. But now, it seemed that she had become an extra!","It was all because of this lad from the countryside!","Li Leyun’s cold eyes landed on Huang Yueli’s ordinary-looking face.","“Grandmaster Xiao, President Gao, I simply can’t understand this. That Li... Li something Spiritual Armament apprentice, what Spirit Armament did he bring that was so extraordinary? Earlier the three Spirit Armaments that I brought out were all refined according to the esoteric lore illustrations but yet, Grandmaster Xiao made it out to be worthless! But now? This fella took out three standardized Spirit Armaments but he praised it so much! What logic is this?”","Her voice resounded throughout the entire courtyard.","Hearing what she said, those Spirit Armament Masters, who were originally discussing, all turned quiet.","Many other people had such doubts. But no one dared to create trouble in front of those few Sky Gem Grandmasters, so none of them raised their doubts at all.","Now that Li Leyun had suddenly said this, everyone pricked up their ears.."]},{"number":2943,"title":"Chapter 2943 - An Extra (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","However, Grandmaster Xiao swept Li Leyun a glance and scoffed coldly. “On what basis do you want This Grandmaster to explain to you? Those with good foresight naturally can tell what’s so extraordinary about these Spirit Armaments. Those who can’t tell can only blame themselves for having lousy eyesight! Are you going to blame This Grandmaster for that?”","Huang Yueli’s eyes widened when she heard that and she showed even more respect for Grandmaster Xiao.","This old man was really arrogant!","But under the current circumstances where he had the corresponding ability as his support, it made her feel that he was rather adorable instead.","But... Huang Yueli wanted to know how outstanding her Spirit Armament was.","She felt rather melancholic when Grandmaster Xiao didn’t say anything more about it.","Li Leyun was so angry that Grandmaster Xiao said that to her in such a manner that her face turned into a maroon shade!","Embarrassing, it was such an embarrassment! As an ancient God clan talented lady, she had never been despised by anyone in this way ever!","Usually, even if she wasn’t in the Cloudy Qilin clan, as long as her identity as a member of the ancient God clan was announced, those humans would not dare to treat her with disrespect. Even those with stronger abilities than her would bow down to her.","This time in Sacred Phoenix Continent, she could not expose her identity hence she had a taste of being despised.","But Li Leyun was used to being arrogant so she wouldn’t be resigned to be dismissed so easily. She quickly regained her calm and sneered.","“Grandmaster Xiao, how will you be able to convince everyone with this attitude? If you don’t explain this clearly today, then you can’t blame me for overthinking things! Everyone knows that anyone who gains a word of praise from you, Grandmaster Xiao, would elevate their value by a hundred times. The Spirit Armament’s value would also increase dramatically! I suspect you have intentionally colluded with someone to boast an unknown Spiritual Armament apprentice at an occasion like this to elevate his status!”","Li Leyun’s words were sharp as she raised this accusation without holding back!","All the Spiritual Armament Masters instantly went into a flurry upon hearing that.","“What? There’s such a thing happening??”","“I don’t believe a man of Grandmaster Xiao’s status would need to do this kind of thing.”","“Although it can be said in that way, this matter is highly suspicious! A Spiritual Armament apprentice casually taking out three Spirit Armaments like this made Grandmaster Xiao give such praises?","“The main thing is these three Spirit Armaments just look so ordinary...”","Under Li Leyun’s incitement, a minority of the Spiritual Armament Masters slowly started to develop suspicions.","In reality, the things that Li Leyun said weren’t considered groundless.","The career of a Spiritual Armament Master was very particular.","Both were mid grade Spirit Armaments but some might be sold at a high price whereas others would be sold cheaply. It all depends on the Spiritual Armament Master’s fame.","In the past, there were several such incidents. Famous Sky Gem Grandmasters would intentionally praise the other party to raise their own disciple or other people’s value.","This was a matter which was extremely damaging to one’s status and the Sky Gem Glass Chamber had also set some restrictions to limit this kind of situation from happening. But unfortunately, it couldn’t be stomped out completely.","Everyone present originally couldn’t understand the reason for him to do this. But Li Leyun’s eloquence caused everyone to think in the wrong way.","In this way, the number of people who suspected Grandmaster Xiao and Huang Yueli increased.."]},{"number":2944,"title":"Chapter 2944 - An Extra (4)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Hearing the increasing doubting voices from the audience below the stage, Grandmaster Xiao’s expression darkened.","He had made his name several hundred years ago. Although he had a bad temper and was always picky and demanding, he had always upheld his status and would never do such a despicable thing like this for money.","It was exactly because of this which earned Grandmaster Xiao a good name within the Spiritual Armament Master circle. This was something that he was very proud of.","But now, someone actually suspected his innocence which he had maintained for many years!","Grandmaster Xiao’s veins on his forehead popped out and his heart was filled with fury.","Li Leyun wasn’t worried even when she saw him getting angry. She said complacently, Grandmaster Xiao, we believe that you won’t do such a thing! But we Juniors are worried that you might be cheated by someone with a vile character, so that’s why I’m asking you for some pointers...”","She didn’t say anything wrong. But in combination with that smug look and provocative tone, it made the listener feel extremely uncomfortable!","Since it had come to this, no matter how much he wasn’t dignified to reply to this kind of question, he had no choice but to give a response.","Otherwise, he was sure to become a scapegoat for this!","Helpless, Grandmaster Xiao gave a cold snort. “Alright, you guys want to know how good are the Spirit Armaments that Young Master Li had refined? Since that’s so, let This Grandmaster give you some information to raise your knowledge. At the same time, you will also find out how ignorant and how opinionated you are!”","Saymg that, he turned towards Huang Yueli and his tone instantly became gentle. “Young Master Li, this is such an embarrassment. I wonder if I can borrow your Spirit Armaments again?","Huang Yueli had already kept all the Spirit Armaments away earlier.","But since Grandmaster Xiao had requested, she didn’t hesitate and immediately retrieved those three Spirit Armaments once again.","Grandmaster Xiao hurriedly said, “Just that long sword would do.”","Huang Yueli shook her head and said, “Since you have to explain the situation, then it’s better to talk about all three Spirit Armaments. Otherwise, other people might claim that we’re playing some tricks later on.”","Grandmaster Xiao thought about it and felt that it was true, so he didn’t say anything to refute her.","Huang Yueli placed her Spirit Armaments down. Like the others, her eyes were fixed on Grandmaster Xiao, waiting for his analysis.","Grandmaster Xiao put on his gloves prudently once again and swept a glance at all the Spiritual Armament Masters below the stage.","“You little blind brats! Do you guys feel that this long sword is just an ordinary standardized Spirit Armament? Alright, let This Grandmaster show you something to clear your doubts!”","After he said that, he lifted the long sword and turned to a mechanism that was the height of two men tall.","Huang Yueli immediately recognized that mechanism in one glance. It should be a mechanism to assess the Spirit Armament’s might.","In the past when she was in Soaring Heavens Continent, every auction house would be equipped with this kind of mechanism. Although the array patterns in God Realm were different, the main structure was still the same.","This mechanism was here to aid him in his lecture. But Grandmaster Xiao was experienced and his foresight was very sharp. Basically, he only needed to use his eyes to accurately judge the grade and might of the Spirit Armament which he had not used previously.","Grandmaster Xiao walked to the assessment mechanism and stopped. Holding the hilt with both hands, he slashed the sword heavily towards the huge stone in front of him!","“Crack","A cracking sound instantly rang.","An evident crack appeared on the huge stone. Apparently, it was caused by the long sword.","“Wow— that’s so amazing!”","Someone in the audience cried out in surprise.","A crack appeared on the assessment mechanism during the assessment!"]},{"number":2945,"title":"Chapter 2945 - No Way To Duplicate (1)","paragraphs":["Translator. Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","This assessment mechanism was used to test all Spirit Armament’s might.","As long as any weapon wasn’t a Treasure Armament grade, even a Supreme grade Spirit Armament can be accessed on this mechanism.","Sometimes, during the assessment of some high grade Spirit Armaments or Supreme grade Spirit Armaments, it indeed would cause the mechanism to crack due to the tremendous amount of might in the Spirit Armament. But, now...","Grandmaster Xiao was just assessing a low grade Spirit Armament!","How was it possible for a low grade Spirit Armament to leave a mark on the assessment mechanism? It was even a standardized low grade Spirit Armament!","If Grandmaster Xiao had not picked up the long sword in front of everyone and walked over, some people might think that he had secretly made a switch!","And now, the assessment result was already out.","“70% increase in might!’ Grandmaster Xiao read out the indication on the assessment mechanism and revealed a smile. ‘The result is almost the same as what This Grandmaster had predicted! Ordinary standardized low grade Spirit Armaments’ attack power has an amplification rate of 30% or so. Those special illustrations can amplify the foundation by 10%! If This Grandmaster were to refine this, I should be able to increase the might to 60% and above!”","He paused and his gaze swept onto Huang Yueli. “But, 70% increase! This is something that not even I can achieve! Only this Young Master Li’s exclusive refinement skills can reach this result.”","The Spirit Armament Masters were all stunned to see this result!","No one expected Huang Yueli’s Spirit Armament to be this powerful!","On the surface, it looked like an ordinary long sword. But it actually contained such powerful might, which had surpassed their imagination!","Even Grandmaster Xiao also admitted that he couldn’t do it to such an extent!","Huang Yueli blinked. She finally understood what was going on.","Towards her own Spirit Armament’s might, she had a rough gauge in her heart. But she didn’t expect that Grandmaster Xiao was not able to refine a low grade Spirit Armament of the same might as hers.","No wonder Grandmaster Xiao admired her so much!","Grandmaster Xiao put down the long sword, put on the other two Spirit Armaments, and proceeded with the assessment. The result made one extremely surprised!","“The Armor’s defense power had been amplified to 60%! Spiritual Artifacts are used to raise the regeneration speed of Profound Energy. As compared to standardized Spiritual Artifacts, it is much faster by 50% and above!’","Under everyone’s watchful eyes, Grandmaster Xiao’s assessment was completed without any pretense.","He announced those shocking results, which were like nails hammered onto the board, and no one could raise any doubts about it.","The Spiritual Armament Masters lowered their heads and didn’t say a word. They should not express the shock in their hearts with words!","Why was it also the same standardized low grade Spirit Armaments, but yet someone else could make it contain such powerful might?","No wonder Grandmaster Xiao didn’t take any interest in Ji Yuankang and Li Leyun’s Spirit Armaments. As compared to Huang Yueli’s Spirit Armaments, their works were simply trash which was an eyesore!","“But... I really don’t understand how Young Master Li could contain such powerful might in the standardized Spirit Armaments? What’s the secret... on the inside?”","Grandmaster Bai, who stood by the side, blurted out his queries. It was also the same query that everyone had in mind.","But he had just said this and immediately realized that he had said the wrong things. “I’m sorry, sorry! I was casually asking. Young Master Li please don’t mind me!”","To a Spiritual Armament Master, one’s exclusive armament refining skills were their secret. And it wasn’t something that anyone could casually ask.."]},{"number":2946,"title":"Chapter 2946 - No Way To Duplicate (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Unless it was someone like Grandmaster Xiao, volunteered to give lectures and share his experience.","If the other party didn’t have any intention of sharing, it was an extremely disrespectful way to spy on other people’s refining method.","Huang Yueli wasn’t upset udlen she heard that.","Grandmaster Bai was a nice person. When she was an ordinary apprentice, he had been taking care of her so she felt grateful to him","Huang Yueli thought over it for a moment and said, “Actually, Ive been learning my Master’s exclusive armament refining method. So towards God Realm’s authentic standardized Spirit Armament refining method, I’m not familiar with it at all. So I don’t know what’s so different about my method against others. Today, I have brought my Spirit Armaments here, hoping to get Grandmaster Xiao’s pointers. So originally, I wasn’t thinking of hiding it from everyone...”","Hearing that, Grandmaster Bai’s eyes lit up and he instantly grew happy.","From Huang Yueli’s meaning, it seemed that she didn’t mind sharing her experience with them!","Grandmaster Xiao understood her meaning and looked at Huang Yueli with a slightly surprised look","Many Spiritual Armament Masters had hidden their comprehended Spirit Armament refining skills well, deeply afraid that others might find out about it. But this attitude, in a Sky Gem Grandmaster like Grandmaster Xiao’s eyes , they were simply too petty!","A person’s comprehension power was limited, after all, so they could only interact with the same leveled Spiritual Armament Masters. Only by using others’ strengths would they be able to make up for one’s weak points, and they would be able to make improvements.","Those who indulge in self- satisfaction and worry about others taking advantage of them would never be able to become a true Sky Gem Grandmaster!","Seeing that Huang Yueli had understood this logic at such a young age increased Grandmaster Xiao’s evaluation of her by another notch!","To be honest, Grandmaster Xiao didn’t know the reason Huang Yueli had agreed so readily. Other than wanting to interact with other Spiritual Armament Masters, she also had something else to back her up!","That was her overpowering innate talent!","Many of her armament refining techniques required extremely powerful fire and metal attributed innate talent before it could be displayed. So for practitioners who were not heaven grade geniuses would not be able to do it at Certain techniques might even require god grade innate talent before it could be completed.","So, even if they could understand what she was saying, there was no way to duplicate her techniques at all!","Grandmaster Xiao naturally didn’t know about these. But he had high expectations of Huang Yueli and didn’t want to let her be disadvantaged Hence he said, ‘Today, This Grandmaster is here to give a lecture, and not Young Master Li. It’s better to let me talk about this! From Young Master Li’s Spirit Armaments, This Grandmaster had comprehended several things, so I will pick a few important pointers to share with everyone.”","Immediately follovfrug that, Grandmaster Xiao started to talk about those unusual traits that he found from Huang Yueli’s Spirit Armaments.","This time, even Huang Yueli was also absorbed in his lecture.","After Grandmaster Xiao’s explanation, she finally understood where her Spirit Armament had gone wrong!","So, the energy field and materials fusion method was not written down in the books! The method that she came out from her own had a huge difference with","God Realm’s method._","No wonder, she felt that the power of those standardized Spirit Armaments was much lower than what she had imagined!","Hearing Grandmaster Xiao’s lecture, the other Spiritual Armament Masters were totally ashamed.","So, those standardized Spirit Armaments that everyone saw were actually that particular. There were so many variations to it, and the might that was displayed from it was so great!","They wondered which guru Li Yuehuang’s Master was.. He thought of so many novel ideas!"]},{"number":2947,"title":"Chapter 2947 - No Way To Duplicate (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Ordinary Spiritual Armament Masters were satisfied. But Grandmaster Bai and President Gao were mesmerized.","In order to protect Huang Yueli’s privacy, Grandmaster Xiao intentionally spoke about the difference between her method and the traditional method, but he didn’t mention how the exact difference was executed.","Ordinary Spiritual Armament Masters totally wouldn’t put so much thought into it. They also felt that they wouldn’t be able to refine it, so they felt that this explanation was already very adequate.","But in the ears of Sky Gem Grandmasters, Grandmaster Xiao’s words were no different from not mentioning anything at all !","Moreover, after Grandmaster Xiao’s analysis, Grandmaster Bai and President Gao felt that there was some profound theory in these Spirit Armaments. However, they could not pursue to find out more about it!","When Huang Yueli saw this scene, she smiled slightly and said, “Since","Grandmaster Xiao and my suspicions have been cleared, we can call it a day for today’s lecture. I think we should find a quiet place and continue to discuss this!”","When Grandmaster Bai heard that there was room for further discussion, he immediately said, “Good, good! Let’s change a place! It’s getting rather late now, so let me invite you to my home to have a meal!”","Grandmaster Xiao nodded upon hearing that and stood up.","They were about to leave but someone called to stop them.","“No, stop there. You can’t leave yet!”","Huang Yueli was stunned and she frowned when she recognized that it was Li Leyun’s voice.","The truth was already displayed in front of them and Grandmaster Xiao had already explained so adequately. Why was this woman so unyielding?","President Gao was enraged and he said in an unrestrained tone, “Young Miss Le, you might be an outstanding Spiritual Armament Master, but you shouldn’t be so ungrateful and repeatedly damage Grandmaster Xiao and Young Master","Li’s reputation! If you don’t stop, don’t ever step into Flame Square City’s Sky Gem Glass Chamber ever again! Men, send her out!”","The evidence was already so obvious but she was still hooting about it right here!","If this went on, how would other people view the Sky Gem Glass Chambers prestige?","Thinking of this, President Gao felt that he couldn’t be excessively tolerant and immediately called the guards to chase her away.","As a god grade genius , Li Leyun was a heaven grade genius and her cultivation wasn’t weak at all. She was a practitioner whose cultivation was already in the Dream Profound Realm end-phase. However, every Sky Gem Glass Chamber had its own exponents guarding the fort. Li Leyun was, after all, still very young. As compared to those experienced top exponents utho had cultivated for hundreds of years, she was still lacking.","Although she was not resigned to it and kept struggling, she was still thrown out of the Sky Gem Glass Chamber!","“Damn it! Damn it! Damn it!!!”","Li Leyun fell on the ground on her butt uith an extremely disheveled look!","As Grandmaster Xiao was giving a lecture in the Sky Gem Glass Chamber today, many practitioners had come on account of his reputation, hoping to see Grandmaster Xiao’s charm. So many practitioners were standing outside Sky Gem Glass Chamber’s entrance today, just waiting for him to appear.","In the end, they didn’t manage to see him. Instead, they saw a rather good-looking lady being thrown out of that place!","The practitioners were originally rather bored, but when they saw a commotion, they immediately crowded around.","“Who’s this? Why is she being thrown out?”","“From her looks, she seems to be a Spiritual Armament Master!”","“Spiritual Armament Master? A Spiritual Armament Master being thrown out, could it be that she had done something disgraceful?”"]},{"number":2948,"title":"Chapter 2948 - No Way To Duplicate (4)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","The practitioners crowded around Li Leyun as though they were looking at a rare item. They sized her up from head to toe and even made all sorts of ridiculous guesses.","Li Leyun had never suffered such humiliation and her face burned with shame. She couldn’t wish for anything more than to find a hole and burrow into it.","She was angry and anxious so she shouted, “Men! Men! Someone, come quickly! Damn, where did my guards disappear to! Come here immediately!”","Several Cloudy Qilin clan’s guards came along uñth Li Leyun. But not knowing why, when she was thrown out, none of the guards appeared at all.","She covered her face her hands and sat on the ground for a very long time. Then she finally heard a shuffle of hurried footsteps.","“Young Miss Leyun, Young Miss Leyun, you... what’s the matter with you?”","A group of guards pushed their way through the crown. When they saw Li Leyun sitting on the ground, they immediately rushed forward to help her up.","Li Leyun used the back of her hand and slapped the leader of the guards.","“Where have you guys gone to? This Lady had been humiliated but none of you are in sight. Then why do I even need you for? Simply a bunch of trash!”","The leader of the guards was slapped and a handprint instantly appeared on his face. There were even scratches from her sharp fingernails.","But he didn’t dare to show any displeasure at all. He hurriedly lowered his head and admitted his mistake. “Young Miss, This Subordinate had come too late. This Subordinate deserves to be punished, Young Miss please mete out the punishment! But should we leave this place first?’","Li Leyun originally wanted to throw her temper but upon hearing that, she recalled where she was right now and her complexion turned pale.","“Why didn’t you say it earlier, let’s quickly go! I don’t want to stay in this goddamn place a second longer! ”","The guards escorted Li Leyun and they swiftly left amid the discussions from the bystanders.","After they left a distance away, seeing that no one else was following them, Li Leyun finally heaved a sigh of relief.","She lifted the veil from her face and said angrily, “Didn’t This Lady tell you to wait at the entrance? Where did all of you go to?”","The guards were extremely terrified and reported in a low voice. “Young Miss Leyun, it’s... Young Master Moying has arrived in Flame Square City! According to regulations , we must proceed to meet him immediately and we cannot afford to delay any time! You mentioned that you will only leave the Sky Gem Glass Chamber this evening, so This Subordinate...”","When Li Leyun heard that, she went into a short blank and instantly widened her eyes in joy.","“What? What did you say? Brother Moying is finally in Flame Square City! I’ve waited for him for more than a month!”","The guard silently heaved a breath of relief.","Li Leyun’s temper was very bad and they didn’t manage to appear in time today. If she wanted to find fault uñth them, they would be in deep trouble.","Luckily, when Li Leyun heard the mention of Li Moying’s name, she cast every other thing to the back of her mind.","She had also temporarily forgotten about the humiliation that she suffered at the Sky Gem Glass Chamber earlier.","“Why didn’t you tell me earlier! Where is Brother Moying right now?”","“Young Master Moying has gone through Flame Square City and now, he should be back at Cloudy Qilin clan’s secret gathering point!”","“Good, that’s great!” Li Leyun jumped up excitedly. “What are you guys waiting for? Still not going to bring This Lady back? What if Brother Moying is too anxious while waiting for me?’","Li Leyun dashed out excitedly, not even taking the carriage.","When the guards saw her departing figure, they shook their heads.","Anxiously waiting for her? How could that be possible?","Li Moying was extremely moody whenever he saw her!"]},{"number":2949,"title":"Chapter 2949 - No Way To Duplicate (5)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Inside the Sky Gem Glass Chamber, Huang Yueli was totally oblivious to Li Moying’s appearance.","Li Leyun had just been chased out and Grandmaster Xiao couldn’t wait and hurriedly caught hold of her.","“Alright, the eyesore is finally gone! The rest of you can leave too! Young Master Li , quickly come along with This Grandmaster. Quick, tell me how on earth did you refine these Spirit Armaments!”","Grandmaster Xiao was so hospitable that Huang Yueli felt bad about declining so she could only follow him into the rear courtyard’s resting area for Sky Gem Grandmasters.","The moment they entered the room, Grandmaster Xiao pointed to the center seat and said, “Young Master Li, come, please take a seat!”","This time, he totally forgot about President Gao and Grandmaster Bai, the two other Sky Gem Grandmasters.","‘IXrvo maids were waiting inside the room and when they saw this , they were so shocked that their mouths were agape.","What was up uñth this? Grandmaster Xiao was treating a Spiritual Armament apprentice so politely, and even inviting him to sit on the host seat?","Grandmaster Xiao was usually a prudish person who wouldn’t even take a look at those Sky Gem Grandmasters whose standards were lacking!","However, Grandmaster Xiao couldn’t be bothered with what they were thinking and impatiently shook his hand. “Why are you still standing here? Why aren’t you going to brew some tea? Young Master Li, you’ve come so early to attend the lecture, so I guess you haven’t eaten anything yet, right? Ask them to serve some snacks!”","The maids came to their senses and hurriedly proceeded to carry out their duties.","Huang Yueli was at a loss to laugh or cry when she saw his hospitable attitude.","Grandmaster Xiao was someone without any motives. All he had on his mind was the art of refining Spirit Armaments!","He treated her with so much courtesy totally because of the exclusive method of refining Spirit Armaments. He felt that her skills were worthy of receiving this kind of treatment!","Moreover, if she was happy, she would reveal the new technique.","Thinking of this, Huang Yueli didn’t act pretentiously and sat on a chair by the side.","“Grandmaster Xiao, there’s no need to stand on ceremony. I’ve learned a lot of things from your lecture today, and I should say thank you instead! How about this, if you have any questions about my armament refining skills , feel free to raise them. I also have a lot of areas that I don’t understand, and I’m hoping to get some pointers from you!”","“Alright, sure, that’s great!”","Grandmaster Xiao got what he uñshed for so he naturally wouldn’t reject this opportunity.","Huang Yueli took out a few Spirit Armaments that she refined from her interspatial ring again and the three Sky Gem Grandmasters crowded around as they couldn’t wait to research these armaments in depth.","“Young Master Li, the position of the blade of this long sword, the energy field, and blade’s fusion position seems different from the ordinary standardized Spirit Armaments. Have you specially processed this area?’ Grandmaster Xiao observed for a moment and quickly raised his query.","Huang Yueli leaned closer to take a look Then she blinked, looking a little lost.","‘This... I wonder where is the position of the fusion point of standardized Spirit Armaments?”","She admitted that she didn’t do any special treatment for this position. But why would it make Grandmaster Xiao so surprised?","When he heard her ask that question, he was stunned as well.","There was a Spiritual Armament Master didn’t know the standard fusion point of standardized Spirit Armaments was! That was simply incomprehensible !","It seemed that Huang Yueli said that she had been following her Master to learn the art of Spirit Armament refining skills in the mountains and had never entered the cities was the truth!","Otherwise, how could it be that she totally had no knowledge of this at all?","Grandmaster Xiao pointed at the thinnest and sharpest blade position with his finger and said, “It’s right here!”"]},{"number":2950,"title":"Chapter 2950 - No Way To Duplicate (6)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Huang Yueli swept a glance and instantly understood it.","She smiled and said, “Oh, I see... All of you chose to set the fusion point on the sharp end of the blade because you thought that the sharp end is the strongest point when a practitioner attacks, and it would cause the greatest amount of damage, right?”","Grandmaster Xiao nodded and said, “That’s right. Isn’t it like this?”","Huang Yueli shook her head and said, ‘The truth isn’t so. When a genuine top exponent strikes, they wouldn’t attack in a straight line like this. Instead, they would lift the sharp end a little higher, and the force-bearing point is changed to this bottom position!”","Huang Yueli’s slender finger pointed to a position that was an inch below the sharp end.","‘This is because the end might be sharp, but it was simply too thin and too brittle. It’s very hard to take on a practitioner’s Profound Energy’s strong and continuous infill! If the force-bearing point is on the sharp end, it might raise the attack a little within a short period. But there is a high possibility of it being damaged within a quarter of an hour. So, the practitioners master swordsmanship would subconsciously avoid this Idnd of situation from happening.”","She paused and then continued, “Because of this, during actual combat, the force-bearing point of the standardized long sword would be conflicted the energy field’s fusion point. In this way, there is no way to display its full might!”","Grandmaster Xiao showed an enlightened look and he looked at Huang Yueli with great admiration.","“So, it’s like this! This Grandmaster had once wondered if the standardized weapons’ insufficient might were related to the position of the fusion point. But I’ve tested several times, yet am still unable to find the accurate fusion point. I didn’t expect you to find it so easily! You’re indeed learning from the best!’","Huang Yueli made it sound very easy, but for an expert like Grandmaster Xiao, he naturally knew the difficulty in achieving this.","If the force-bearing point was not at the sharp end, then specific position should it be at?","This was related to a practitioner’s habit of striking, the Spirit Armament’s material, the energy field’s intensity, and many other closely related elements.","As there wasn’t a specific illustration for indication, one could only depend on their awareness and play by ear when they were refining Spirit Armaments.","Huang Yueli could find the best fusion position so accurately. That didn’t just mean that she had an astounding power of comprehension. Moreover, her metal attribute innate talent was the most outstanding!","Hearing Grandmaster Xiao’s praise, Huang Yueli merely smiled and didn’t say a word more.","Of course, it wasn’t easy to find the precise fusion point. Even for her, she couldn’t just waste that mere two sets of materials to complete such a complicated piece of work","The reason she knew this was because she had attempted multiple times when she was in the Lower Realm. Her objective was to refine a genuine God Relic for Li Moying!","Back then, she had a certain guess regarding God Realm’s refining method but she couldn’t find any suitable materials to execute it.","Now that she had arrived in God Realm, she was systemically learning the Spirit Armament refining skills, and there were ample materials. So uñth the past years of experience accumulated, she had finally refined a powerful long sword!","Grandmaster Xiao sighed a couple of times and picked up the armor, then continued to research on it.","As he looked, he raised a few questions.","Huang Yueli answered all the questions in succession.","At the same time, she also took the opportunity to ask some questions which she encountered during the refining process.","Grandmaster Xiao reciprocated and also imparted his knowledge to her.","But after some interaction with Huang Yueli, the doubts in his heart grew even."]},{"number":2951,"title":"Chapter 2951 - Sky Devil Blood Ring (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Because the questions that Huang Yueli asked were simply too obvious!","It was so obvious that even apprentices who had just joined also knew the","Grandmaster Xiao simply couldn’t understand why such a peerless genius like Huang Yueli would ask these kinds of questions.","For an instant, he almost thought that Huang Yueli had taken someone else’s Spirit Armaments to deceive him She actually didn’t know anything at all!","But shortly after, Grandmaster Xiao dispelled this thought.","It was because uthen Huang Yueli replied to his questions, she discoursed knowledgeably. Her answers gave light to new inspiration for him, which opened up a new train of thought.","A Spirit Armament Master who gave such high leveled armament refining skills answers, how could she possibly be someone who is only angling for fame?","But it was very strange that she had no general knowledge at all!","At this moment, Grandmaster Xiao felt as troubled as the Inheritance Tower’s Huang Zixiao.","Facing such an abnormally strong genius, ordinary people would find it hard to adapt._","Grandmaster Xiao had a deep interest and Huang Yueli also learned a lot of things. The both of them hit it off immediately and they chatted through the night, still wanting more.","Seeing that dawn was about to break, President Gao reminded softly, ‘Grandmaster Xiao, Young Master Li, it’s getting late. Both of you should have a rest!”","Before Huang Yueli could say a word, Grandmaster Xiao waved his hand dismissively, ‘This Grandmaster is not tired, don’t disturb us from having an in-depth discussion on armament refining skills!”","However, when Huang Yueli heard what President Gao said, she thought of the time and found herself getting slightly tired.","When she was behind closed doors in Double Prosperity Inn, she stayed there continuously for an entire month and practically didn’t rest at all. After that, she finished refining the Spirit Armaments and just came out of the closed door cultivation when she heard that it was the day of Grandmaster Xiao’s lecture, she hurriedly rushed over to the Sky Gem Glass Chamber.","This kind of continuous consumption of energy, even if she was a god grade genius , or how dense or great the amount of Heaven and Earth Profound Qi in God Realm was, she also couldn’t continue in this state.","She said hastily, “Grandmaster Xiao, This Junior had been behind closed door refining armaments in the past few weeks and my concentration is slightly dwindling . there’s no need to be in such a rush. If you’re still interested in the discussion, I can come over to Sky Gem Glass Chamber tomorrow morning.","Hearing her say that, Grandmaster Xiao could only nod his head no matter how unwilling he was.","President Gao was listening by the side and he hurriedly added, ‘Young Master Li, you need not travel back and forth. The Sky Gem Glass Chamber has a few vacant guest rooms , so wouldn’t it be more convenient for you to stay here?” Huang Yueli thought about it briefly and nodded her head in agreement.","In this way, she spent a total of three days in the Sky Gem Glass Chamber discussing the art of refining Spirit Armaments.","Grandmaster Xiao had received God Realm’s orthodox Spiritual Armament","Masters training and had a rich experience. So he was well versed in various Spirit Armament refining methods like the back of his back There was practically nothing that he didn’t know.","Huang Yueli’s innate talent was so high that those doubts in her mind were quickly resolved under Grandmaster Xiao’s teachings!","After a short duration of three days, she already felt her Spirit Armament refining standard soaring!","The extent of her improvement was much more than when she first went into closed door cultivation one month ago!","Grandmaster Xiao also felt that he had benefited greatly from this.. “Young Master Li, after having an in-depth discussion with you, This Grandmaster feels that my previous armament refining skills were just too outdated! Now that I’ve been enlightened, I’m going into closed door cultivation once I reach home and practice on this thoroughly! When This Grandmaster has refined powerful Spirit Armaments, I will come and look for you for evaluation!’"]},{"number":2952,"title":"Chapter 2952 - Sky Devil Blood Ring (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","“Grandmaster Xiao, that’s just too kind of Huang Yueli’s lips curled up. “Unfortunately, my Master wants me to go around God Realm and go on more experience learning and I can’t always stay in the Glass Gem Chamber. So I’m not sure when will we be able to meet up in the future.”","She wanted to keep in contact with Grandmaster Xiao, but she was using a fake persona right now.","When she had resumed her original identity, Grandmaster Xiao would not be able to link her with this Li","Grandmaster Xiao could tell that she was rejecting his idea and he snorted in a dissatisfactory manner. The breath he breathed out was so strong that his mustache flew upwards.","“Why? You’re intending to turn your back on us now that you’ve got what you wanted? This Grandmaster is telling you, no way!”","Saying that, he took out a little ring from his shirt pocket and passed it to Huang Yueli. “Take this!”","Huang Yueli didn’t know if she should laugh or cry from hearing Grandmaster Xiao’s words. When she looked at the ring in front of her, she was stunned.","The ring that Grandmaster Xiao passed to her looked like a piece of jade, but it was in an extremely attractive blood red color. ‘There was a faint hint of dense energy within and on one look, one could tell that it was not an ordinary item.","“Grandmaster Xiao, this is...","Before Grandmaster Xiao could answer, Grandmaster Bai who was standing by the side cried out in shock, “Sky Devil Blood Ring?? This is the Sky Devil Blood Ring, right? On my god, Grandmaster Xiao , you’re giving such a valuable treasure away?”","Grandmaster Bai simply could not believe his eyes.","Grandmaster Xiao had refined a lot of high tiered Treasure Armaments , but it was still very rare to have a treasure like this Sky Devil Blood Ring.","Huang Yueli looked at them puzzledly and asked, “Sky Devil Blood Ring? What’s that?’","Grandmaster Xiao stuffed the ring into her palm “Nothing, it’s just a small plaything. Just take it!”","He said it in such an easy-going manner so Grandmaster Bai totally couldn’t take it and explained on his behalf. “Young Master Li, you don’t know about this. This Sky Devil Blood Ring is refined using a Sky Devil’s blood essence. Sky Devil’s blood essence is extremely hard to come by. You only need a drop of it, and you be able to escape most of the demon tribe’s soul trace prying. Unless you meet with a higher leveled demon tribesman than the blood essence’s originator, otherwise, no one will be able to see through your disguise.”","He paused for a moment and said, This Sky Devil Blood Ring that Grandmaster Xiao had refined was made out of a high leveled demon tribe general’s blood essence, who had been killed, one hundred years ago. The blood essence obtained back then could only refine three rings. The other two rings are in the hands of two top Life Profound Realm exponents, and Grandmaster Xiao couldn’t bear to sell the last ring. I didn’t expect him to give it to you as a gift!”","Hearing that, Huang Yueli immediately understood.","When she was in the Lower Realm, she had once read in various ancient records. She knew that God Realm was not the same as Soaring Heavens Continent, where there was only human race living here.","In God Realm, other than a large number of humans, God races’ innate talents were even higher. They were equivalent to the aristocrats governing level, but basically, they were not much different from humans.","Other than that, the demons could take in humans’ blood essence to raise their abilities. So there would often be demons capture humans for cultivation. In this way, a deep feud was forged between the humans and demon tribe.","God Realm’s demon tribe and the human race had always been in a state of war.","As for the Monster race, they were much slyer. The monster race’s innate talent was in training various spirit beasts and magical beasts. Moreover, their battle strength was extremely strong. Some Sky Fiends uñth very high innate talents could even surpass God race.","But the Monster race’s bloodline had a flaw, and they found it especially hard to reproduce. Hence their population had always been low.."]},{"number":2953,"title":"Chapter 2953 - Sky Devil Blood Ring (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","The Monster race had always maintained a neutral relationship with the human race and demon tribe.","When the human race had the upper hand, the monster race would have a close relationship with the human race. When the demon tribe’s ability was advantageous, they would lean towards the demon tribe.","Until now, the human race and demon tribe were still engaged in war. Many continent’s boundaries were battling the demon tribe.","The twelve ancient God clans in God Realm bore their grudges since ancient times. They would only be united when they were fighting against the demons.","As humans were protected by the God clans, they were willing to submit to them.","As for the positions of the twelve god clans, they would be gauged based on their merits on the battlefield against the demon tribe.","Cloudy Qilin clan’s territory was closer to the demon tribe so they were frequently engaged in battle. There were many brilliant feats that the clan’s strong exponents had achieved, hence their position in God Ream was extremely revered.","This situation was something that everyone knew in God Realm","When Huang Yueli was in the inheritance tower, she had once heard Huang Zixiao mentioning this. When she arrived in God Realm, she had a bit of understanding of it and was clear on the current situation.","But when she was in Soaring Heavens Continent, she had not seen any demons.","Even if she had arrived in God Realm, she had always been in relatively safe zones. Until now, she had yet to meet a genuine demon, nor did she come across any scenes where both tribes were engaged in battle, so it didn’t feel real at all.","It was until now that when she heard Grandmaster Bai saying these when Huang Yueli realized that the Sky Devil Blood Ring that Grandmaster Xiao had gifted to her was an extremely incredible piece of treasure!","When practitioners went into battle, they would only use their eyes to check out the enemýs situation. Powerful practitioners could use their soul trace to cover an area of ten miles to find out about the distribution scenario.","Huang Yueli’s ability wasn’t considered high in God Realm, so if she were to meet with any demon tribe’s top exponents, there would be no way for her to hide.","But if she had this Sky Devil Blood Ring with her, the situation would be different!","This ring was a priceless treasure to practitioners who were fighting in the war zone!","No wonder Grandmaster Bai was so shocked when Grandmaster Xiao gave it to her as a gift.","“It’s so incredible! Wouldn’t that mean that I would become invisible when I stand on the battlefield with the demons?” Huang Yueli gasped in surprise.","Grandmaster Xiao shook his head when he heard that. invisible? How could it be that easy? It’s just that they can’t use their soul trace to find you. But if the other party is standing at a close distance whereby they can see you with the naked eye, you will still be exposed. But when I was refining the ring, I’ve encased an invisibility energy field within. As long as you are at a distance of ten meters or more from the demons, you will be invisible. But during that period of invisibility, you can’t use any Profound Energy. Once there is any Profound Energy fluctuation, the invisibility effect would be lost.”","Huang Yueli was surprisingly happy when she heard that. At the same time , she was astounded by Grandmaster Xiao’s powerful armament refining abilities!","It was extremely difficult for someone to remain invisible in front of their opponents whose power surpasses themselves.","Generally speaking, the prerequisite for the invisibility array and Profound","Armament to come into effect was for the person who was using the armament to have the power of the opponent’s level!","But this Sky Devil Blood Ring could allow her to remain invisible in front of high leveled demons.","The only sad fact was it had no effect on human practitioners...","Hearing their conversation, Grandmaster Bai asked with a pained expression,","“Grandmaster Xiao, you really.. why must you give the Sky Devil Blood Ring to","Young Master Li? You can just give him any other Treasure Armament!”"]},{"number":2954,"title":"Chapter 2954 - Sky Devil Blood Ring (4)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","“He’s not a practitioner and he probably wouldn’t be on the battlefield. If the Sky Devil Blood Ring is worn by a Life Profound Realm practitioner, who knows how many demons that practitioner might be able to kill! Giving it to him is such a waste!”","Hearing Grandmaster Bai’s grieving, Huang Yueli also hesitated for a moment.","“Grandmaster Xiao, this ring is simply too valuable. If you wish to give me a keepsake, some other Treasure Armament is alright as well.’","Grandmaster Bai nodded his head furiously as he took a gratified glance at Huang Yueli, thinking that he had great foresight. ‘This young man indeed has a good sense of the overall picture.”","However, Grandmaster Xiao firmly shook his head. “In God Realm, no one dares to say that they would never meet with the demons. So as a safety precaution, you’d better keep this Sky Devil Blood Ring uñth you. Your life to the human race is very important. Based on your armament refining innate talent, you will definitely become a top rated Sky Gem Grandmaster in the future , and your contributions are no lesser than Life Profound Realm practitioners!”","Although Sky Gem Grandmasters do not fight on the battlefield, the various Spirit Armaments that they manufacture would save numerous practitioners’ lives.","They could also manufacture lethal large -sized mechanisms which could sometimes become the crux of deciding which side would win the battle.","Grandmaster Xiao believed that Huang Yueli would do well, hence he was very worried that she might have an early death during the process of experience learning.","After all, Grandmaster Xiao didn’t know Huang Yueli’s innate talent in terms of cultivation so he assumed that she was the same as many other Sky Gem Grandmasters. The battle power was almost similar to the same leveled practitioners.","With the Sky Devil Blood Ring, at least she would be able to save her own life if she ever met with the demon tribe.","As for the human race, they would generally not find trouble uith a Spiritual Armament Master.","In this way, Huang Yeuli was basically safe without any worries.","Huang Yueli could tell that Grandmaster Xiao wanted to protect the talents hence she didn’t reject it any longer and accepted the Sky Devil Blood Ring.","She wasn’t just a Spiritual Armament Master, but also a practitioner who god grade innate talent. If she had to fight with the demon tribe in the future which probably could not be avoided, perhaps this ring might be extremely useful!","Huang Yueli kept thanking Grandmaster Xiao.","He smiled and said, Treasure Armament is just a physical possession. If you are really thankful to me, you must come and examine my Spirit Armament when I refine even better Treasure Armaments. I am living in Empyrean Fox Continent, Medial Arch City. By then, if you have invented any new armament refining skills , we can share the information again.","Grandmaster Xiao had already put it in this way so Huang Yueli naturally couldn’t reject his request.","She repeatedly agreed to it and stood up to bid farewell.","When she walked to the entrance of the Sky Gem Glass Chamber, President Gao suddenly popped out from nowhere and called out to her.","“Wait, wait a minute! Young Master Li, I have a favor to ask.w” President Gao hesitated to continue with his sentence.","Huang Yueli blinked and asked puzzledly, “President Gao, you...”","He hesitated for a moment and opened his mouth to speak, ‘Well, it’s like this. Young Master Li, the Spirit Armaments that you refined uses a special method and many of our Spiritual Armament Masters in the Chamber are very interested. But our power of comprehension isn’t as high as Grandmaster Xiao. Just based on those few hours previously, we totally can’t tell the mystery of it at all. If it’s possible, can I ask you if you’re willing to sell your Spirit Armaments to the Sky Gem Glass Chamber..","Huang Yueli’s brows lifted in astonishment.","President Gao had been paying attention to her expression and when he saw that, he thought that she was unhappy. So he quickly added in, “After we have purchased the Spirit Armament, we will keep it within Flame Square City’s Sky Gem Glass Chamber and 1⁄4ill absolutely not allow it to be on loan. Nor uñll we disassemble the Spirit Armament! Please don’t worry about it! Of course, if you’re really unwilling. “"]},{"number":2955,"title":"Chapter 2955 - Bad News, They’re Fighting! (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","President Gao’s voice was getting softer as he spoke and uthen he came to the end of the sentence, it was full of guilt.","He was offering to pay for those Spirit Armaments, naturally not to use it, but to conduct research on it.","But a Spiritual Armament Master’s exclusive method had always been a secret that had not been revealed to outsiders.","Even though many people would secretly buy out other Spiritual Armament Grandmasters’ works to research on them, this matter wasn’t something scarce, nor was it something that could be stopped.","But to directly find that Spiritual Armament Master to purchase their refined armaments with such evident intention would easily enrage the other party.","Thinking of this, President Gao hurriedly added, “Young Master Li, if I’ve been too indiscreet, will you please...”","Before he could finish his sentence, Huang Yueli asked, “I can sell it to you. But how much are you intending to purchase it for?”","President Gao was stunned.","He didn’t expect Huang Yueli to ask him about the pricing the moment she spoke!","A Spiritual Armament Master was a noble profession and they had always been extremely high and mighty. Even if they wanted to talk about the pricing, they wouldn’t say it out so directly!","But he didn’t expect Huang Yueli to not avoid any taboo and just ask directly, then stared at him and waited for his reply.","President Gao came back to his senses and hurriedly replied, “This... one piece of ordinary standardized low leveled Spirit Armament costs about 10 thousand high grade cwstal jades. But Young Master Li’s Spirit Armaments are invaluable. If you sell it to a practitioner, you can sell at least 100 thousand high grade cwstal jades. We’ll go according to the Sky Gem Glass Chamber’s market rate and purchase it at double the price, one Spirit Armament for 200 thousand high grade crystal jades. I will take all the Spirit Armaments that you have. Do you think.. this is reasonable?”","Huang Yueli blinked and she bemoaned inwardly.","She recalled that just a month ago when she arrived at Flame Square City, the inn’s waiter told her that activating the teleportation array required 100 thousand high grade crystal jades. Back then, she only had a few hundred medium grade crystal jades in her pocket so that was an exorbitant price to her.","She didn’t expect to be able to sell her Spirit Armaments at this Idnd of pricing in such a short time.","Refining a Spirit Armament would take a maximum of two to three days but the number of crystal jades that she could sell at was sufficient to activate the teleportation array twice!","Grandmaster Xiao was listening to them and when he saw Huang Yueli not speaking, he assumed that she was still hesitating. Hence he advised, “Young Master Li, these Spirit Armaments might be sold to Sky Gem Glass Chamber, but without your armament refining method, the amount of knowledge ordinary people can learn from just looking is very limited. It’s impossible to copy the entire method. Moreover, President Gao’s pricing is considered fair. If you’re not satisfied with it, you can get him to raise the pricing a little!”","Grandmaster Xiao took a look at President Gao.","He immediately reciprocated and nodded his head as he said, “That’s right. I can offer 250 thousand high grade crystal jades a piece. Young Master Li, what do you think?”","He raised the price within such a short amount of time. It seemed that the Sky Gem Glass Chamber was really wealthy!","Huang Yueli’s lips curled upwards and she said, “l also intend to sell the Spirit Armaments to get some traveling expenses. Since President Gao has offered such a good price, it will save me the hassle of going to the auction house to do the trading. I’ll sell all the Spirit Armaments that I’ve recently refined to you then!”","As she spoke, she took out all the Spiritual Armament that she had refined within the past month and lined it up on the ground","She also knew that Sky Gem Glass Chamber was extremely wealthy. If she wanted to raise the price, she might be able to sell it at an even higher price."]},{"number":2956,"title":"Chapter 2956 - Bad News, They’re Fighting! (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","But on account of Grandmaster Xiao and Grandmaster Bai, she didn’t want to take advantage of them","In the future, she would need to interact with the Sky Gem Glass Chamber, so there was no need to earn everything from them at one go.","These were just low tiered Spirit Armaments, so these weren’t very expensive.","In the future , udlen she refined even higher tiered Spirit Armaments or even Treasure Armaments , that would be the time when she would start raking in cash.","President heard how straightforward Huang Yueli was and instantly became joyous. He thought even highly of Huang Yueli now.","“Good, that’s great! Treat that l, Old Gao, owes you a favor! In the future, if you need any help, feel free to look for me!” President Gao patted his chest and promised.","He hurriedly lowered his head , thinking to look at what Spirit Armaments that Huang Yueli was going to sell to him.","Immediately follovfrug that, he went into a blank. ‘These._ these... you’re going to sell all of these to us?”","President Gao’s eyes widened in disbelief.","On the ground were ten over pieces of Spirit Armaments which were neatly lined up. Moreover, Huang Yueli was continuing to take them out!","These dozens of Spirit Armaments were not repeated and each of them was different. Moreover, it had surpassed the normal three categories, namely weapons, armors, and Spiritual Artifacts.","The most important thing was these were all standardized Spirit Armaments. Those were all low tiered Spirit Armaments which had practically been refined based on the standardized Spirit Armament Illustration Book.","President Gao originally assumed that it was already very impressive to have three to five kinds of remodeled low tiered Spirit Armaments, and it would be more than enough for them to research on!","Whoever knew that Huang Yueli took out so many at one go!","“Alright, that’s all, a total of 20 pieces!” Huang Yueli finally finished taking out all of the Spirit Armaments that she had stood up and said with a smile.","President Gao’s lips twitched. “There’s actually... 20 pieces! Don’t tell me that these Spirit Armaments are all refined using your exclusive armament refining method?”","Remodeling a piece of Spirit Armament was already extremely difficult, not to mention remodeling a whole pile of them!","If every single piece was the same as the three pieces of Spirit Armaments that she took out previously, greatly uplifting the original standardized Spirit Armament’s might by so much, it would be a miracle!","Huang Yueli looked at him strangely and said, ‘That’s of course. These Spirit Armaments are refined using my method, so the might of these shouldn’t be too far off! President Gao, don’t worry, I won’t dupe you. If the Spirit Armaments aren’t any good, I won’t sell them to you for such a high price! If you’re worried, why don’t you ask Grandmaster Xiao to examine it first!’","She had already put it in that way, so President Gao immediately felt rather embarrassed.","“No, no, no, there’s no need to examine! Young Master Li’s Spirit Armaments are definitely the best...” He hurriedly declined.","However, Grandmaster Xiao instantly picked up one Spirit Armament and said, “Old Gao, how can you be so casual uthen you purchase Spirit Armaments? You haven’t even ascertained the Spirit Armaments’ quality and you’re going to pay for it. Surely you can’t just squander in this way, no matter how much money you have, right? Let This Grandmaster help you check!”","President Gao looked at Grandmaster Xiao’s back and went into a short blank, then he instantly came back to his senses.","This old fellow, he couldn’t wait to see the new Spirit Armaments that Huang Yueli had just taken out! Hence he intentionally found an excuse to do so.","But, this had indeed helped him greatly!","Grandmaster Xiao squatted on the floor felt all the Spirit Armaments one after another. He was also mumbling to himself.","‘This cutlass looks very powerful, and the armament refining method seems different from the previous long sword! How is this done?’"]},{"number":2957,"title":"Chapter 2957 - Bad News, They’re Fighting! (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","“And, and this dagger. The killing power is so high! This lad is so young, but he had such great mastery in refining weapons. It won’t take a few years for him to surpass me!”","‘Tsk tsk, even the armor is refined so well. This set of wrist guards is of the finest quality among the low tiered Spirit Armaments...”","As Grandmaster Xiao looked, he lamented and he couldn’t stop feeling regretful.","If he had known that Huang Yueli had so many other Spirit Armaments with her, he would have asked her to sell all of these Spirit Armaments to him instead!","Grandmaster Xiao thought that she only had those three pieces. Since he had already seen them, he gave up the chance to sell these Spirit Armaments to President Gao instead.","Now, he regretted his decision..","“Old Gao, we have been friends for so many years. When we were young, we also attended the auction together Grandmaster Xiao suddenly said without any warning.","President Gao had a shock. “Ughh. _ this","Wasn’t Grandmaster Xiao absorbed into looking at the Spirit Armaments? Why did he suddenly reminisce about the past?","“Since we have such close ties, we should share the good stuff, right? Old Gao, why don’t you resell these few pieces of Spirit Armaments to me! I’ll offer you double the price, one piece at 500 thousand jades, what do you think?” President Gao came back to his senses when he heard that. He turned around and saw Grandmaster Xiao holding tightly to a few pieces of Spirit Armaments, prepared to take it away the minute he nodded.","‘You.... No way! These belong to our Flame Square City Slw Gem Glass Chamber! I’m not selling! I insist on not selling!”","President Gao shot up like an arrow, preparing to snatch those Spirit Armaments back.","Grandmaster Xiao held onto the Spirit Armaments and shifted to the left and right while continuing to persuade him. “Old Gao, you can’t be so petty! It’s just a few pieces of low tiered Spirit Armaments. You can have as many as you want, so must you haggle over it with me? It’s not as if I won’t pay for it?”","“Just a few pieces of low tiered Spirit Armaments! Then don’t fight with me over them!” President Gao cried out in dissatisfaction.","Both Sky Gem Grandmasters were a thousand years old added together, but they were fighting over a few low tiered Spirit Armaments.","Their armament refining standard might be different, but there was practically no difference in their cultivation. They were both in Heart Profound Realm mid -phase, and their actual combat experience was practically zero.","So when they fought, they were equals, and there was no clear winner.","The surrounding Spiritual Armament Masters and female attendants originally were stunned by what they saw. No one thought of stepping up to pull them apart.","Huang Yueli’s sweat dripped dowm from her forehead as she was rather speechless. So she could only step up and separate the two of them.","“Alright, alright, both Seniors. It’s just a few pieces of Spirit Armaments, don’t lose your harmony over this small thing! Grandmaster Xiao, didn’t you tell me earlier if you wanted them? I can stay here for a couple of days more and refine a few for you!”","Grandmaster Xiao’s face was originally very furious, and he lost a few strands of hair on his beard during the fight.","Hearing that, his anger turned into joy. “Really? Young Master Li, you’re willing to refine some Spirit Armaments for me?”","Huang Yueli nodded and smiled, “I’m in need of money! Since there’s a chance to earn money, how can I miss it?”","The main thing was she had totally and thoroughly pondered over the refining method of these Spirit Armaments. So the speed of her refining would be much faster than before.","As they always said, awkward at first but skillful later on. It wasn’t something very troublesome, and it wouldn’t waste too much time.."]},{"number":2958,"title":"Chapter 2958 - Find Her, Dead or Alive (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","For Grandmaster Xiao, Huang Yueli stayed a few more days in the Sky Gem Glass Chamber to refine various types of standardized Spirit Armaments.","Centre of Sacred Phoenix Continent, Ice Moon Summit.","The usually bustling main hall was exceptionally quiet today.","A female attendant holding on to a tea tray walked softly, deeply worried that she might make a noise and agitate the currently furious clan leader in the main hall.","‘That bunch of scums from Cloudy Qilin clan is simply too much! How dare they touch our Sacred Phoenix Race’s god grade genius! Do they even still bother about the agreement all 12 god clans agreed to fight against the demon tribe? They publicly harm and murder other god clans. Are they intending to become a public enemy of the other god clans? Do they really think that we, Sacred Phoenix Race, have no top exponents? How can we swallow this after being bullied to this extent?”","Sacred Phoenix Race’s clan leader, Huang Tianhao slammed his fist on the table, and his powerful Profound Energy broke the table in half. The teapot and other porcelainware fell on the ground and shattered into pieces.","Even so, he still hadn’t vent his frustrations and kept walking about in the main hall frustratedly.","It wasn’t only Huang Tianhao. Everyone in the main hall had an indignant look on their faces.","Some were even very impulsive. They had already drawn their long swords out. If it wasn’t because someone was holding them back, they would have dashed out to exact revenge on those from the Cloudy Qilin clan!","Huang Sanbai lowered his head as he stood in front of Huang Tianhao.","He had a guilty look on his face, and he spoke with a quivering voice, “Clan Leader, it’s This Old Man.. This Old Man has let the clansmen down, and I’m really sorry about the Sacred Phoenix Race! If I had been able to detect Cloudy Qilin clan’s scheme in time and stood in front of Lass Li Cloudy Qilin clan’s people had appeared, she wouldn’t have fallen from Azure Luan and wouldn’t have gone missing...”","He choked while he spoke. He looked so sad as though his tears were about to fall.","Huang Sanbai originally was Sacred Phoenix Race’s oldest Elder, and before he returned to Ice Moon Summit, he had made sufficient preparations. He messed up his hair and clothes , appearing extremely miserable.","His acting skills were simply too convincing, and everyone saw him in such a shabby state, they couldn’t help but sympathize with him, pleading with the Huang Tianhao on his behalf.","“Clan Leader, we can’t blame Elder Sanbai for this matter! It’s all Cloudy Qilin clan’s men for being so despicable and shameless! Who would have thought that they attacked our god grade genius!”","“Isn’t that so? It must be intentional! They were aiming for our god grade genius!”","“We might be able to prevent it temporarily, but there’s no way we can protect her for life. Elder Sanbai, don’t blame yourself too much”","“Every injustice has its perpetrator. Let’s go look for those Cloudy Qilin clan’s scums to settle this!”","Everyone was indignant, and their fury took over their rationality.","Ice Moon Summit’s descendants had been waiting for the arrival of this god grade genius.","Tivo months ago, Huang Sanbai had already sent a report to Ice Moon Summit that he had already received the god grade genius. Her innate talent was indeed outstanding, and it was absolutely at a god grade’s standard.","When the news came, the entire Sacred Phoenix Race was bubbling with excitement, and everyone was very happy.","Originally, they were worried that the signal from the Lower Realm was a mistake, but now that their god grade genius had appeared, that reassured everyone!","Huang Tianhao had already instructed to arrange the residence and cultivation resources for Huang Yueli. He was prepared to nurture their one and only god grade genius properly.","Whoever knew that time passed by day after day. Everyone waited and waited , but they didn’t see the god grade genius appearing.","Even Huang Sanbai, who was sent to pick her up, had also gone missing.."]},{"number":2959,"title":"Chapter 2959 - Find Her, Dead or Alive (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Huang Tianhao sent a few batches of people out, but none of them were able to find them.","Today, Huang Sanbai finally returned to Ice Moon Summit with a few clansmen disheveled appearances.","Seeing Huang Tianhao, Huang Sanbai knelt on the ground and started to cry miserably.","Seeing him in such a state, the clan leaders heart thumped hard. He hurriedly asked about the situation","Huang Sanbai wiped the corner of his eye and said, “Clan Leader, This Old Man is guilty, This Old Man has let our clansmen down! ‘IÀ’VO months ago, I’ve already picked up our god grade genius. Her innate talent is outstanding, and she has good mannerisms. Everyone was very happy. On the third day, I brought her to take Azure Luan, hoping to return to Ice Moon Summit as soon as possible. Whoever knew... Whoever knew...”","Saying to this point, he sniffed a few times as though he was extremely aggrieved and could not continue","Huang Tianhao was extremely anxious, and he couldn’t help but stomp his feet. “Whoever knew what? What on earth is going on? Quickly tell us!”","Huang Sanbai dabbed the corner of his eye to wipe off the “tears” which were non-existent and said in a low voice, “Whoever knew that we had just left Soul Connection Ocean and bumped into those people from Cloudy Qilin clam They recognized me and started to attack me and Lass Li for no rhyme or reason! I didn’t expect them to strike us, so by the time I responded, it was already too late._”","‘The Azure Luan that we were riding was struck dead, and Lass Li fell from mid-air...","‘This Old Man also fell on the ground and fainted. When I regained consciousness, I hurriedly went to look for her, but Lass Li had already gone missing.”","Huang Tianhao’s expression was filled uñth shock, as though he had been struck by lightning!","He shook his head in a dazed expression and muttered to himself, “Impossible! This is impossible! How can this be? That._ That Huang Yueli, she.. could she really...” Speaking of this point, Huang Tianhao suddenly thought of something and agitatedly ran towards Huang Sanbai. Grabbing his collar, he said, “Huang","Yueli fell from the sky, but it doesn’t represent that she had died! Where is she? Didn’t you guys go search for her?”","Huang Sanbai gave a bitter smile and said, “Clan Leader, how could This Old Man possibly not search for her? I only came back now because I’d been searching for her near the surroundings at the location where the incident happened! This Old Man had been searching for her tirelessly for the past few days and nights, but I couldn’t find her at all...”","“In the end, This Old Man proceeded to meet up with those young clansmen in Soul Connection Ocean and utilized all our power to search around the surrounding tow-ns and cities. But there were no leads at all...”","Huang Tianhao’s eyes “How can a living person suddenly go missing? If she’s alive, we must find her, but if she’s dead, we should be able to find her corpse as well!’","A cold glint flashed past Huang Sanbai’s eyes, but that sinister expression only lasted for a second, so no one noticed it at all.","‘There are two possibilities for Lass Li’s disappearance. One is that she wasn’t injured too badly and managed to escape but lost her way. The other iy._ she had been taken away from the people from Cloudy Qilin clan!’","Huang Sanbai didn’t continue with his sentence , but the meaning in his words was very clear.","If Huang Yueli was only lost, under such a massive search in Sacred Phoenix Continent, how could they possibly not find her?","So, although he said there were two possibilities, there was actually only one.","Huang Tianhao trembled. He already had a similar guess in his mind, but he didn’t dare to believe it!","Clenching his fists, he tried hard to make himself calm down a little.","“Elder Sanbai, are you certain that you saw who attacked the two of you?”"]},{"number":2960,"title":"Chapter 2960 - Find Her, Dead or Alive (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","“This sort of matter... we can’t talk about it so carelessly. There would be big trouble if we accuse the Cloudy Qilin clan wrongly! Although we have always been on loggerheads with them, with the mutual agreement that binds us to fight against the demon tribe, they... would they be so bold?”","If they killed other god clans’ disciples, that would mean that they had violated the agreement. They would also become the public enemy of all god clans.","If it was manslaughter, they could forget about it. But such blatant interception of other god clans people was totally unreasonable!","Moreover, ever since the agreement had been formed, Cloudy Qilin clan and Sacred Phoenix Race had endless frictions of various magnitudes in the past thousands of years. But other than a few accidents, there were no incidents where an intentional murder was committed.","This time... why did this happen?","Huang Sanbai knew that his Clan Leader wasn’t so easy to fool, so he had already thought of an excuse.","His lips curled and revealed a non-visible sneer. Then he immediately spoke grimly, “Actually, I’ve also thought about this. I wonder if the demon tribe had intentionally tried to incite the feud between our two clans so they found someone to pretend to be from the Cloudy Qilin clan and attack us. This Old Man doesn’t want to accuse the wrong person! But the younger clansmen that I brought along to Soul Connection Ocean tried to intercept our god grade genius, and even had a conflict with our clansmen!”","Huang Sanbai immediately pointed out their clansmen as his witness.","These people had all witnessed Li Moying appearing in Soul Connection Ocean and Serene Rain Town. Many of them were injured by him and his guards.","As Huang Sanbai spoke, he secretly felt delighted. He had to thank Cloudy Qilin clan’s god grade genius to appear so coincidentally, which gave evidence for his lies!","This time, Huang Tianhao had no choice but to believe in this!","The clan leader turned pale with fright. “What? There’s such an incident? Cloudy Qilin clan... how dare they do this!”","Huang Sanbai sneered, “Why do they not dare to do? Clan Leader, there’s something else beyond your imagination! The leader of those Cloudy Qilin clan’s practitioners is the god grade genius whom they picked up more than one year ago! This man is true as the rumors say. From his bone age, he looks like he’s not even 25 years old yet, but his cultivation is already at Heart Profound Realm. Moreover, his battle power is astonishing. Even This Old Man almost lost against him. Oh, right, he also contracted an ancient spiritual beast","Qilin!”","Huang Tianhao was shocked by this astounding news. Even after a long time, he still hadn’t come back to his senses!","It was until Huang Sanbai urged him softly did he regain his senses. “Cloudy Qilin clan’s god grade genius is actually... actually so incredible! No wonder those scums from the Cloudy Qilin clan have nothing to fear! With this genius around, it will just take a few more decades and we, Sacred Phoenix Race will have to live our days by submitting to them!”","Huang Sanbai sighed. “This person’s innate talent is indeed not bad. But from what This Old Man thinks, Lass Li’s innate talent might not be any weaker than his! If we could nurture her properly, it would be hard to tell who’s much more incredible. Alas... sigh! No wonder the Cloudy Qilin clan was so anxious. They rather violate the agreement to fight against the demon tribe and insist on killing Lass Li!”","His words were said to be adding oil to fire.","Huang Tianhao’s heart was filled with pain, and his fury was instantly ignited!","At this moment, there was only a last sliver of doubt in his heart, but that had been diminished by that extremely vexed emotion.","He banged the table with his fist loudly, stood up, and roared angrily, “Men!","Quickly go gather all the Elders and core disciples to the main hall now!”"]},{"number":2961,"title":"Chapter 2961 - Find Her, Dead or Alive (4)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","“I don’t care what they are doing, just get them to come over immediately! We, Sacred Phoenix Race... cannot suffer in silence! I must let those Cloudy Qilin clan people pay the price for their actions!”","The guards outside the main hall rarely saw the magnanimous clan leader flaring up like this. All of their faces turned pale, and they hurriedly ran off to gather those people.","Not too long later, Sacred Phoenix Race’s Elders gathered in the main hall.","Huang Sanbai gave a brief reiteration of the scenario again, and in an instance, the entire main hall was drowned with angry voices!","“Cloudy Qilin clan has gone overboard!”","“They can’t stand the fact that we, Sacred Phoenix Race also has a god grade genius, so they’re just worried that we will compete with them in the future, isn’t it?”","“Damn it, they deserve to die! Clan Leader, we cannot let this matter go to rest.","We must head over to Cloudy Qilin clan and demand justice!”","“That’s right, we’ve suffered enough these years! If it wasn’t for that agreement, we would have gone over to the Cloudy Qilin clan to settle the debt with them! Since they violated the agreement first, then we need not stand on ceremony as well!”","Public anger spilled over the whole group, but some people managed to maintain their sense of rationality.","“Clan Leader, it is indeed extremely infuriating for such a thing to happen. But as for how we should deal with this scenario, we need to look at a long-term plan...” Elder Meng coughed loudly a few times to interrupt the momentum.","Huang Tianhao was already burning with rage by Huang Sanbai’s incitation, so how would he be able to listen to this kind of advice?","But as Elder Meng held high prestige in the clan, he suppressed the urge to scold her. His tone was still very frustrated as he said, “Elder Meng, Cloudy Qilin clan has already climbed on top of our heads, and you’re telling me that we need to look at a long-term plan? What plan? This time, we must make them pay the price in blood! I will immediately send someone over to Cloudy Qilin clan!”","Elder Meng felt anxious and hurriedly persuaded, “Clan Leader, taking action privately like this is wrong as well, isn’t it? By then, if we cause an internal rift among the god clans, other people might say that we, Sacred Phoenix Race, were the ones who provoked them first! I didn’t say that we will not be exacting revenge, but we must have reasoning and evidence. We must first raise an application to the God Clan Alliance and sue the Cloudy Qilin clan for murdering our clan’s god grade genius, and expose their crime to the world! By then, all the god clans will stand on our side and the Cloudy Qilin clan can forget about being absolved from the crime!”","Huang Tianhao was, after all, a clan leader, and he knew the complexity among the god clans more than anyone else.","Earlier, he lost his head because of anger. Hearing what Elder Meng said now, he realized that he had been too impulsive earlier.","He took a deep breath and calmed down a little. “That’s right. Elder Meng, what you said is right! Before we take action, we have to tell the other god clans about Cloudy Qilin clan’s crime to justify our actions...”","Huang Sanbai’s brows shifted slightly when he heard that and instantly had a feeling that trouble was about to brew.","If Huang Tianhao were to bring this matter to the God Clan Alliance, there was a 99% chance that those schemes that he did would be exposed.","Cloudy Qilin clansmen were idiots. They would definitely try to clear their name if they were accused in such a manner.","If both parties were to go into a confrontation and if Cloudy Qilin clan was able to provide some evidence, he would be in trouble by then..","Thinking of this, Huang Sanbai suddenly had an idea and butted in, “Clan Leader, what Elder Meng said is reasonable. But this matter isn’t as simple as what she thinks! We cannot abruptly just spill the beans on this matter!”","Huang Tianhao’s brows creased.. “What do you mean."]},{"number":2962,"title":"Chapter 2962 - Find Her, Dead or Alive (5)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Huang Sanbai said, “Those people from the Cloudy Qilin clan attacked me and Lass Li in the wilderness. There weren’t any other witnesses around at that time. If they insist that they hadn’t done this, no one would be able to prove it!”","Hearing that, the practitioners around were all stunned, as everyone remained pensive in their thoughts.","Huang Sanbai knew that things were looking good and hurriedly added,","“Moreover, we didn’t officially announce the news that we, the Sacred Phoenix Race, has a god grade genius. Various large forces have their channels and might have received this news, but other than the few of our clansmen who went to pick her up, no one else had seen Lass Li herself! Perhaps, Cloudy Qilin clan might grab hold of this point and say that we don’t have any god grade genius at all. It’s just a lie to scheme against them!”","“Outrageous! Simply a load of rubbish! If those Cloudy Qilin clan’s scums dare to say that, I will rip their mouths!” Someone instantly jumped up in fury.","Huang Sanbai intentionally shook his head helplessly. “What use is there to rip their mouths? The main thing is this matter can’t be explained clearly! If it comes to that, we would still have to rely on ourselves to exact revenge on them, isn’t it? But there would be plenty of eyes on us by then. So if we want to take action, it might not be that easy!”","Huang Tianhao listened and his brows creased even tighter.","“I didn’t expect Cloudy Qilin clansmen to be so despicable and sinister! Elder Sanbai, based on what you said, no matter what we do, it’s just not right. Then what should we do then?”","Huang Sanbai pretended to think about it for a moment and said, “Based on what This Old Man thinks, we should settle this in private! Moreover, we don’t need to officially declare war with the Cloudy Qilin clan in their face. Didn’t they harm our god grade genius through underhanded means? Then why don’t we also kill their god grade genius? This is called paying them back in their coin! Moreover, the person who harmed Lass Li is that god grade genius. If we kill him, we can exact revenge for Lass Li!”","The Elders present all pondered over this and immediately started to echo in agreement.","“Elder Sanbai’s idea is the best!”","“It’s so reasonable, too reasonable! Cloudy Qilin clan also didn’t officially announce that they have a god grade genius, isn’t it? When we kill him, we can also say that god grade genius was something that they made up to frame us!”","“Elder Sanbai is indeed a veteran. Your idea is indeed the best!”","Hearing everyone’s approving voices, Huang Tianhao nodded his head. “Since this is so, then we shall do according to Elder Sanbai’s suggestion! The person who will be chosen to complete this mission...”","Before he could finish his sentence, Huang Sanbai stood up.","“Clan Leader, it is This Old Man’s mistake that Lass Li had got into trouble. So leave this matter to me. I’ll do my very best to atone for my mistake!”","Huang Tianhao nodded and said, “Alright, I’ll leave this matter to you then!”","Huang Sanbai cupped his fists respectfully with a solemn expression.","No one knew that he was feeling extremely elated in his heart!","Even though he wasn’t able to find Huang Yueli, nor could he obtain the Sky Phoenix Ring, if he could take this chance to get rid of the Cloudy Qilin clan’s god grade genius, that would be huge merit!","By then, he would become Sacred Phoenix Race’s hero and his status would be elevated even more.","That meant that he would be able to utilize even more resources to find Huang","Yueli!","No one knew if that lass was dead or alive.","But even if she was dead, he would still get the Sky Phoenix Ring out from her corpse!"]},{"number":2963,"title":"Chapter 2963 - Who Is More Disadvantaged? (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","They reached a consensus at the Sacred Phoenix Race’s meeting so Huang Sanbai quickly left the Ice Moon Summit to seek out Li Moying’s whereabouts.","Whenever he thought about Li Moying’s shocking innate talent and strength, as well as his contracted ancient spiritual beast Qilin, he was afraid that he might fail miserably in this easy task.","So, he specially asked Huang Tianhao for another two Dao Profound Realm Elders to go along with him.","His return this time had caused a very huge commotion in the main hall.","Hence, even though Huang Tianhao kept repeating that the contents of the meeting should not be leaked out, various large forces’ scouts had already received news of this and secretly broadcasted it.","Li Moymg, who was in Flame Square City, received this news three days later.","Li Tian Yi was shaking in fear and trepidation when he passed the letter with the word “Confidential” printed on top. Then he waited apprehensively for Li Moying’s response.","After this time, all the guards already knew how much this future clan leader valued his wife from the Lower Realm, Even Huang Sacred Phoenix Race people had deemed Huang Yueli as dead. It was imaginable just how upset Li Moymg would be after he found out about this.","Li Moying didn’t usually flare up, but if he did, it was something that no one could handle...","However, out of Li Tian Yi’s expectation, Li Moying didn’t move at all after he read the letter’s contents. Maintaining the same posture, his finger that held the letter trembled, which revealed the enormous fluctuation within him.","The angle at which Li Tian Yi stood only allowed him to see Li Moying’s fringe.","It covered half of the latter’s face, so he couldn’t see his expression at all.","On seeing Li Moying not speaking, Li Tian Yi asked cautiously, “Young... Young Master, Sacred Phoenix Race’s news might... might not necessarily be true. Don’t... don’t need to bother too much about it. Young Miss Huang is a god grade genius, after all, so she must have some way to protect herself. We... we’d better continue to look for her..","Although he said this, Li Tian Yi was just trying to comfort Li Moying by saying these words.","Even he also believed that unless Sacred Phoenix Race had concrete evidence, otherwise they wouldn’t come to this conclusion over their most valued god grade genius...","Their poor Young Master Moying, he had become a widower at such a young age.","Moreover, Li Moying and Sacred Phoenix Race’s young lady’s relationship seemed very good. The guards were worried that their Master would be given a severe blow because of this. If it affected their cultivation, it would be the entire Cloudy Qilin clan’s loss.","Li Moying still didn’t say a word so Li Tian Yi shut his mouth in embarrassment.","He didn’t know what he should say, to comfort Li Moying.","But if he didn’t say a word, the room’s gloomy and strange atmosphere made one felt unbearable.","Not too long later, Li Tian Yi’s back was drenched in sweat.","Not knowing how long had passed, Li Moying stood up, turned towards the door, and wanted to walk out.","Li Tian Yi came to his senses and hurriedly followed after him. “Young Master, Young Master, wh... where are you going?","However, Li Moying didn’t answer him. Or perhaps, it could be said that he totally couldn’t answer him at all.","Because in the very next moment, Li Moying’s body suddenly swayed to the left and right, then he fell.","Li Tian Yi was stunned and couldn’t react in time. But in the next moment, he was shocked!","Li Moying’s willpower was invincible in the hearts of all Cloudy Qilin clan practitioners.. No matter what kind of difficult situation he was in, there was nothing that could make him fall!"]},{"number":2964,"title":"Chapter 2964 - Who Is More Disadvantaged? (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","But now....","Li Tian Yi jumped up. “Young Master, Young Master! Wh... What’s the matter with you? Men, Men, come quickly!!”","At the same time, Huang Yueli, who was refining the Spirit Armaments for Grandmaster Xiao in the Sky Gem Glass Chamber, suddenly felt her right hand tremble.","Immediately following that, the flame beneath the armament furnace lost control and scuttered up into the sky!","“Rumble—”","A loud sound was heard and the armament furnace exploded violently. A gust of black smoke spread in the surroundings.","Huang Yueli was tugged hard from the back and fell heavily on the ground. Because of that, she managed to evade the rampant flame that was spewing explosively.","“Young Master Li, you... don’t you know how to avoid it? Do you know how dangerous it was earlier? When a Spirit Armament furnace explodes, one might die if you don’t evade in time!” Grandmaster Xiao’s exasperated voice rang.","Huang Yueli then dazedly realized that she was distracted!","For an instance, her mind seemed to have flashed past an image of Li Moying spitting up blood and becoming unconscious. It made her heart feel a piercing pam.","Later on, she lost control of her right hand. Originally, she should be making a hand gesture to lower the temperature. But it became one which raised the temperature instead and the armament furnace simply exploded!","Huang Yueli took a look at the pitch-black scene in front of her and she wanted to cry but there were no tears.","Exploded! She actually caused an explosion!","Ever since she started learning armament refining in her past life, she had never made the furnace explode!","But now, not only did it happen, it was even in front of Grandmaster Xiao...","Earlier, she claimed confidently that she would be able to refine all those standardized Spirit Armaments once again. But the result was she caused an explosion not too long after...","This was really embarrassing!","Grandmaster Xiao only gave a slight frown. “Young Master Li, you’re very young and your workmanship is very good, so naturally you’re bold as well! But in the process of refining Spirit Armaments, any kind of accident might happen to us, Spiritual Armament Masters, so you should be even more careful! Like today, you didn’t even run away when it had exploded. This isn’t simply playing a joke with your safety!”","Even though an accident like this happened, Grandmaster Xiao didn’t think much of it.","Other than Huang Yueli this kind of devil-like level character, which other Spiritual Armament Master had never exploded their furnaces when they were young?","Even Grandmaster Xiao had also spoiled dozens of Spirit Armament furnaces when he was still a Spiritual Armament Master!","Seeing that Huang Yueli was still so young, it’s perfectly normal to have a little accident when she made a small mistake.","Moreover, the Spiritual Armament furnace that Huang Yueli was using was simply too rundown. It was already a miracle that it only started to break down now. He wondered to himself, “For a Spiritual Armament Master of his standard, why did he need to use such a rundown furnace?","“Surely, it’s not because he’s this stingy, right? He couldn’t bear to part with a cent at all!","President Gao also thought of the same thing so he immediately sent someone to give Huang Yueli a new Spiritual Armament furnace.","When Huang Yueli saw that it was new, she felt that she had profited from it.","It wasn’t that same low grade inferior product that she bought earlier. From the looks of it, it seemed extremely superior. No matter if it was the materials used to make the furnace or the engraved patterns on the sides, they were extraordinary. Moreover, it didn’t seem to be like those models of the standardized Spiritual Armament furnaces that she had seen.","Grandmaster Xiao fiddled with his beard and nodded when he saw this furnace.","“This Spiritual Armament furnace isn’t too bad.. It can barely match up Young Master Li’s workmanship! Anyone can tell that the rundown furnace from earlier couldn’t take a deviant flame’s high heat!”"]},{"number":2965,"title":"Chapter 2965 - Who Is More Disadvantaged? (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Never in Grandmaster Xiao’s imagination would he have thought that Huang Yueli had already used that ‘rundown furnace’ to refine a whole pile of Spirit Armaments.","Moreover, she even used the True Phoenix Fire then. As compared to the deviant flame that she was using now, to conceal her identity, the temperature was much higher!","But under her powerful control, that low-quality Spirit Armament furnace didn’t malfunction at all.","However, she didn’t bother to explain too much. Huang Yueli merely said “Thank you” and received the Spirit Armament furnace.","In that instance when she relit the flame, her mind flashed past a thought.","That scene that surfaced earlier, was it real or fake? Surely, Li Moying wouldn’t really... have met with some kind of danger, sustaining a heavy injury and coughing out blood, right?","Just thinking of this made her hand tremble again.","She almost caused another explosion in the Spirit Armament furnace once again!","Luckily, that furnace was good quality stuff and was extremely solid. Hence it wasn’t damaged that quickly.","Huang Yueli quickly retracted her thoughts and suppressed the uneasiness in her mind, as she continued to refine once again.","The moment she was fully concentrated, her attention was undivided and all Huang Yueli could see was the Spirit Armament which she was refining.","Grandmaster Xiao and the others stood in a distance, worried that she might cause another explosion again.","In the end, after the initial chaos, Huang Yueli quickly entered into the situation and her hand gestures were becoming swifter and precise as time went by...","At the later stage when the Spirit Armament was about to form, her fingers moved so swiftly that it made everyone’s eyes go blurry. Even for an experienced veteran like Grandmaster Xiao, he almost lost track of her movements.","“Oh my gosh, this.. what kind of hand movement is that! How could he be so fast?”","“Before Young Master Li started to refine, he already told This Grandmaster that when he fuses the energy field and materials, it required his soul trace to find out the link and changes between the two items and slowly find a compatible fusion point... this is an extremely intricate work! He... how could","he...","“Young Master Li seemed as though he hadnt thought carefully over this. It was all based on his instinct!”","If it was said that Huang Yueli’s explosion was a mistake that made these few Sky Gem Grandmasters wrongly think that she was a novice, hence her techniques were still not proficient.","But now, everyone had already forgotten about the little episode that had happened earlier. They were completely awed by her skillful tactics!","The speed of a Spiritual Armament Master refining Spirit Armaments was mainly decided by experience.","As compared to those veteran Spiritual Armament Masters who had hundreds of years of experience, Huang Yueli’s display of speed was not inferior in any aspect!","But she looked really young...","This kind of contradiction made the three Sky Gem Grandmasters think that they were dreaming!","It only took less than one hour for Huang Yueli to produce her first Spirit Armament.","She wiped the sweat from her forehead and lifted her hand to open the Spirit Armament furnace lid.","“Grandmaster Xiao, this is the long sword which I showed during the lecture.","I’ve refined another piece accordingly. Please examine it!”","She wore a pair of specialized insulated gloves to take out the long sword, then passed it to Grandmaster Xiao.","Grandmaster Bai and President Gao also crowded around, as their eyes opened wide, looking at those smooth lines on that beautiful long sword.","It only took such a short amount of time to refine. The three of them were worried that Huang Yueli had cheated on the workmanship and materials of the Spirit Armament!","But after taking a look, the finished product was so beautiful that they couldn’t pick out a single flaw at all.","Moreover, the long sword’s exterior was no different from ordinary improved standardized Spirit Armaments. But it was strange because it somehow felt that this sword was even more beautiful than the original piece.."]},{"number":2966,"title":"Chapter 2966 - Who Is More Disadvantaged? (4)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","As though there was a kind of invisible glow that was released from the sword blade.","The three of them looked at the long sword without blinking, forgetting to talk as they revealed a look of admiration.","Seeing that they were absorbed in this, Huang Yueli shrugged her shoulders indifferently and continued to refine the next Spirit Armament.","By the time they came back to their senses, they discovered that Huang Yueli had already lit the fire. Then they looked at each other in dismay.","President Gao asked in astonishment, “Why didn’t Young Master Li rest before he continued to refine? Can his body take it?”","Refining Spirit Armaments was absolutely an exhaustive job that required a large amount of Profound Energy, stamina, and concentration.","So Spiritual Armament Masters would spend a certain amount of time to cultivate, mainly not to fight, but to have sufficient energy to support the high intensity of refinement.","The more complicated the Spirit Armament, the more energy they consumed.","Taking Huang Yueli’s exclusive method to refine Spirit Armaments as an example, the might of the armament was much stronger than ordinary Spirit Armaments. So naturally, the refining process was also more complicated.","Through the Sky Phoenix Ring, Huang Yueli had suppressed her cultivation at the tenth stage realm early-phase.","To President Gao and the others, based on her cultivation, she should have been tired out from just refining a long sword!","Whoever knew that she seemed as though she didn’t consume much energy and didn’t even bother to drink water before she started refining the second piece of Spirit Armament.","Grandmaster Bai was also a little worried and he frowned. “Can Young Master Li take it? Even if he was in a rush for time, surely he can’t ruin his body in this way, right? At most, he can just refine lesser armaments! If this goes on, if he faints in the middle of refinement, it might cause another explosion again! Shall I go give him some advice? What do you think, Grandmaster Xiao?” Grandmaster Bai turned and looked at Grandmaster Xiao as he spoke.","But Grandmaster Xiao seemed as though he didn’t hear what he said. He held on to the long sword with both hands and stared at it fixedly.","President Gao also found it a little strange and asked, “Grandmaster Xiao, what are you looking at? This sword... is there a problem with it?”","“What’s the problem? The problem is major!” Grandmaster Xiao jumped up in a second. Carrying the long sword, he ran out of the courtyard. “This lad, he’s a top grade genius Spiritual Armament Master. No one has his level of comprehension! ”","“Huh? What do you mean??”","Grandmaster Bai and President Gao took a look at each other and they were totally bewildered. They couldn’t understand what Grandmaster Xiao meant.","But seeing that he had left, they also hurriedly chased up to him.","Grandmaster Xiao ran to the courtyard and stopped right in front of the Spiritual Armament might testing mechanism.","Grandmaster Bai then understood what was going on. “It looks like Grandmaster Xiao wants to test Young Master Li’s newly refined Spirit","Armament’s might!”","President Gao burst out into laughter on seeing this. “Old Xiao, you’re too particular! The Spirit Armament that Young Master Li refined so last-minute definitely can’t be compared to that piece which he took out at the lecture. That long sword should be the best among the numerous long swords that he had refined in the past! Why did Old Xiao come here to test it? Could it be that he wants to exchange with me if this is not as good as the other piece? I’m not a fool, I won’t exchange with him!”","President Gao assumed that he had seen through Grandmaster Xiao’s mind!","Speaking of this, Grandmaster Xiao indeed was on the losing end. But the principle was always ‘first come first serve’ , even more so for transactions!","It was simply a brilliant and wise choice to ask to purchase the Spirit Armaments!","He wrapped his arms around his chest in a relaxed manner, watching Grandmaster Xiao lifting the long sword and striking it down on the assessment mechanism!"]},{"number":2967,"title":"Chapter 2967 - Who Is More Disadvantaged? (5)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","“Bang—!”","A loud reverberation was heard and an eye -catching crack appeared Mith the sound on the assessment mechanism’s boulder.","President Gao looked on with admiration. “Indeed Young Master Li’s workmanship. Even if it was such a hurriedly finished Spirit Armament, it could even leave a crack on the assessment mechanism It’s really. E”","Before he could finish his exclamation, he suddenly paused with widened eyes. He stared straight at the figures on the assessment mechanism.","‘This... this...”","President Gao’s mouth was agape. He wanted to say something but he was like a mute who couldn’t make a single sound.","Grandmaster Xiao’s face was filled u?th smiles as he kept the long sword. “Hehe, Old Gao, you’re absolutely right! It’s indeed Young Master Li’s workmanship. He casually refined a long sword and its might is much higher than the previous one! The upgrade in the arrack power has reached 75%!”","President Gao couldn’t say a single word for a long time. He felt a dull pain in his chest and almost fainted from it!","Earlier he was being so complacent, feeling that he had gained an advantage in getting a better Spirit Armament than Grandmaster Xiao. Whoever knew that it only took a couple of breaths for reality to strike him on the face!","Where was he going to put his face as a Sky Gem Grandmaster and branch President!","Moreover, wasn’t this a little too ridiculous?","Everyone knew that uhen a Spiritual Armament Master was meticulously refining a Spirit Armament, the amount of time and energy spent would increase along with the powerful might.","Young Master Li had rushed to refine this but it didn’t seem as though he had spent too much energy on refining the Spirit Armament. How could it possibly be much better than the selected one?","President Gao couldn’t comprehend it so he deemed it as a Idnd of luck.","“Hmpf, your luck is pretty good! You’re lucky to have met Young Master Li outdoing himself, hence coming out with this long sword! But this Idnd of luck would most probably happen only once. You just have one piece of Spirit Armament which is better than mine. The other 19 pieces would definitely lose out to me! In conclusion, I’m the one ???????? benefitted the most!’","President Gao was rather disgruntled initially. But he looked at it from another perspective and sorted out his thinking.","He didn’t believe that Huang Yueli would be able to surpass the standard every single time !","However, Grandmaster Xiao’s smile didn’t disappear on hearing that. Not only so, but he also spoke with a happy tone, “Old Gao, are you that certain that Young Master Li is only lucky?”","President Gao snorted. “If it’s not luck, what else could it be?”","He didn’t doubt Huang Yueli’s armament refining ability, but no matter how powerful she was, surely she couldn’t go beyond logic, right?","Grandmaster Xiao gave a meaningful smile and said, “Alright, then we’ll just wait and see!”","President Gao subconsciously frowned when he heard that. He looked suspiciously at Grandmaster Xiao.","‘This wily, old fox, what was he up to? He seems very confident? Could he be pretending? Is there some plot that I missed out on??”","President Gao couldn’t understand, so he stood by the armament refining room’s entrance to wait for Huang Yueli to complete the refinement.","After another hour or so, Huang Yueli walked out again, holding a piece of armor.","‘”Grandmaster Xiao, this is the second Spirit Armament. Please take a look.”","Grandmaster Xiao received it with a big smile and asked concernedly, “Young Master Li, it’s been hard on you! You ought to take a break after continuously refining Spirit Armaments! Old Gao has already got the maids to prepare some tea and snacks..”"]},{"number":2968,"title":"Chapter 2968 - Who Is More Disadvantaged? (6)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","However, Huang Yueli remained unmoved.","Shaking her head, she said, “No thanks, Grandmaster Xiao. I’m in a rush for time so it’s better to complete refining first! Today, I’d have to complete at least ten pieces of Spirit Armaments. In this way, I only need to refine the remaining ten pieces tomorrow and my mission is completed.”","Hearing that, even the composed Grandmaster Xiao’s expression also became twisted.","“Refining ten Spirit Armaments in a day, and he was going to refine continuously for two days!”","“Who did this lad think he was?’","“Even if his Spirit Armament refining skills were proficient and his speed was very fast, but does he even know how much Profound Energy would be consumed?”","“Forget about the fact that he was just a tenth stage realm practitioner. Even if his cultivation was in Dream Profound Realm end-phase, he might not be able to hang on!”","Grandmaster Xiao naturally couldn’t have thought that Huang Yueli’s true cultivation wasn’t in the tenth stage realm, but was in the Dream Profound Realm mid-phase.","Moreover, Huang Yueli was a genuine practitioner who had undergone strict training. Her endurance wasn’t something that those pampered Spiritual Armament Masters could compare with.","Grandmaster Xiao was feeling worried but when he saw Huang Yueli lighting up the furnace again, he didn’t interrupt her. Instead, he looked at President","“Old Gao, shall we have a bet?’","President Gao saw Grandmaster Xiao shovfrug a strange smile , resembling a fox, and the alarm bells in his heart started to ring.","“Bet? What bet? I’m not betting!” Grandmaster Xiao was never one utho would take a disadvantage. President Gao wasn’t that silly to fall for his trap.","Grandmaster Xiao unhurriedly lifted the armor in his hand and said, “Are you certain that you not bet? I’m preparing to go assess this armor’s defensive power. If it isn’t as powerful as the one that you have, then I’ll pay for all those twenty pieces of Spirit Armaments that you have! If this piece is more powerful...”","‘Then I’ll help you pay for all your twenty pieces of Spirit Armaments!”","President Gao hastily continued and shouted, “Alright, I’ll accept your bet!”","The Spirit Armaments that Huang Yueli sold to him were expensive. One piece cost 250 thousand so everything added together would cost five million high grade crystal jades!","It was enough to purchase a mid grade Treasure Armament.","To President Gao, this was a huge expense.","Although he didn’t mind this amount of money, since someone was offering to pay the bill, that would be for the best. So how could he miss out on this chance?","Moreover, in President Gao’s opinion, Grandmaster Xiao must have lost his mind to raise such a bet!","How could this second piece of Spirit Armament be more powerful than the previous piece?","Unless the sun rose from the west, otherwise such a ridiculous matter would not happen at all!","Grandmaster Xiao’s lips curled up as he knew Old Gao would definitely fall for The two of them had known each other for so many years, and he had been tricked so many times. But yet he still didn’t learn his lesson. Sigh..","Grandmaster Xiao didn’t say anything more and directly walked to the assessment mechanism, placing the armor on top.","It only took a few seconds for the result to be out.","‘This armor’s defensive power is much higher by 65% than similar standardized armors! The one with you is only higher by 60%. So the one that I have is a little stronger...” Grandmaster Xiao smiled slightly as he spoke slowly. Then he cupped his hands at President Gao, “Old Gao, thank you for giving in to me! You’re so kind to give me five million high grade spirit cwstals. I’ll happily accept it then._”","President Gao’s eyes turned green with envy upon seeing this result.. He cried out in disbelief, “Impossible! This is not possible!”"]},{"number":2969,"title":"Chapter 2969 - Too Despicable and Shameless (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","“How could such a thing happen? You must have done something to the assessment mechanism!” President Gao said disgruntledly.","At the same time, he shot up to the side of the assessment mechanism and started to examine it carefully.","“What tricks are you up to? We have been buddies for so many years. Aren’t you being unkind, trying to cheat my money in this way!’","Grandmaster Xiao had a helpless look on his face. “Old Gao, do you think I’m that kind of person? I usually like to crack jokes uith everyone, but to commit fraud u?th the assessment mechanism is something that I will never do!”","President Gao was so infuriated that he lost his rationality. Now that he calmed dowm a little and thought things through, it was indeed so.","As one of God Realm’s top rated Sky Gem Grandmasters, Grandmaster Xiao respected his occupation very much.","He might deceive people in other matters, but when it was related to Spirit Armaments , he would not talk about it blindly.","But if Grandmaster Xiao didn’t commit fraud, wouldn’t that mean..","President Gao’s eyes widened as he looked at the armor that Grandmaster Xiao was holding and that long sword which he couldn’t wait to keep in his realm ring, his eyes slowly turned green u?th envy.","“So.. so, these Spirit Armaments are really... are they really better than those that he previously refined??”","Grandmaster Xiao nodded solemnly, “That’s right!”","“But, this... this isn’t logical, right? Young Master Li only took less than one hour to refine a Spirit Armament. Based on his cultivation and experience, this should already be the limit, so how could he also balance the quality of the armament? How does he even do this? Moreover speaking, the Spirit Armament that he brought to ask you for pointers , shouldn’t those already be his best works?”","President Gao frowned , unable to comprehend the situation.","Grandmaster Xiao looked pensive and said, “Actually, This Grandmaster sort of understands what is going on...”","“What’s going on?” President Gao asked in anticipation.","Grandmaster Xiao said, “Let me put it in this way. Those Spirit Armaments that Young Master Li brought out during my lecture were already his best works. But now, he’s improved again!”","“Improved?? Are you joking??” President Gao was dazed, not knowing if he should laugh or cry. “It’s just been one night, and his Spirit Armament refining standard had such a great improvement? Those Spirit Armaments’ power might have increased by 5%, but based on the limits, increasing by 5% is as difficult as climbing up to the sky! Why would he suddenly, suddenly.. imp.","Improve.. ”","Speaking to this point, President Gao suddenly thought of something, and his voice abruptly stopped, looking at Grandmaster Xiao in disbelief.","Grandmaster Xiao sighed softly and nodded his head. “It should be exactly as what I thought. Earlier when I was discussing V’?th Young Master, I corrected some of the mistakes that he made and also shared my understanding of the art of refining Spirit Armaments. Young Master Li might have listened to me and immediately put into practice the improvements.”","President Gao was tongue-tied. “But... but this is even more ridiculous! Those techniques that you told him earlier require a long time to practice in order to master them, not to mention using them when refining armaments! Ordinary people wouldn’t be able to digest it completely and apply it, even in a few years!”","“But Young Master Li isn’t an ordinary person!” Grandmaster Xiao sighed v??th emotions.. “He could possibly be the most heaven- defying Spirit Armament refining genius that I have ever met!”"]},{"number":2970,"title":"Chapter 2970 - Too Despicable and Shameless (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations I Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","‘That’s right. Young Master Li’s innate talent is indeed something that no one could match... I wonder is his Master is, to be able to teach such a monster like him? Perhaps, that person might be a top exponent who had advanced into Life Profound Realm.” President Gao mumbled to himself, trying to guess Huang Yueli’s background.","As he spoke, he looked at Grandmaster Xiao.","A delighted smile hung on the latter’s face.","President Gao suddenly realized what was going on and couldn’t stop himself from shouting. “You! You intentionally duped me! You have such good foresight, and you’ve even examined those Spirit Armaments at proximity earlier. Have you already seen that these Spirit Armaments are much better than the earlier batch? Is that it?”","“Ughh, thiy._ Cough cough, cough cougll_.” Grandmaster Xiao coughed hard in an attempt to conceal the smile on his face.","However, it was already too late for him to do this. President Gao wasn’t a fool, so he had completely understood was going on.","He was so angry that he jumped up and brandished his fists, wanting to give him a good punching!","“Old Xiao, how can you intentionally dupe me like this! You’re simply too despicable and shameless!”","Grandmaster Xiao immediately started to run and evade President Gao’s attacks. “Aiyo, Old Gao, saying that is too much! We have already knowm each other for so many years, so ??????? would I intentionally dupe you? This is a coincidence._ a coincidence..","“Coincidence, my foot! Do you dare say that you didn’t intentionally lure me to bet with you? You know that you would win long ago, isn’t it?’ President Gao chased after him relentlessly.","Grandmaster Xiao cried out innocently, “How can you blame me? Didn’t you feel that you would definitely win, so that’s ????? you bet with me? If you won, could I say that you are duping me? Are you intentionally trying to renege on your debt?”","“You still dare to deny it! I’ll fight it out u?th you!”","The two of them created a big fuss, and their voices were very loud, which alarmed Grandmaster Bai, who had already gone back to his room to rest.","Seeing the two of them like this, Grandmaster Bai didn’t know if he should laugh or cry. He found some men to pull them apart.","‘The two of you are already so old. Why are you still acting like when you were young? Why have you started to fight again? Where’s Young Master LP Has he already finished refining the Spirit Armaments? If he comes out and sees the two of you Sky Gem Grandmasters in this state, what would happen to our Sky Gem Glass Chamber’s reputation?”","President Gao was pulled to a corner, but he was still very upset and had a dowmcast look on his face.","But quite a number of young Spirit Armament Masters had gathered around in curiosity. So he had to maintain his branch President’s reputation and just barely managed to sit down.","He took a teacup and kept gulping down the drink, ignoring Grandmaster Bai.","Grandmaster Bai could only turn towards Grandmaster Xiao. “Grandmaster","Xiao, what’s going on? Weren’t the two of you doing fine earlier?”","Grandmaster Xiao had no misgivings and roughly explained the dispute they had earlier.","Hearing that, Grandmaster Bai’s eyeballs almost popped out!","“What? How is that possible? Grandmaster Xiao, are you joking ??? me? I’m a","straight person, and I ????? really believe that it’s true!’","Grandmaster Xiao sneered, “Would This Grandmaster joke with you on this kind of matter?”","“But.. but...”","Just as Grandmaster Bai looked dazed, Huang Yueli opened the door and walked out from the armament refining room.","“I’ve finished refining the third Spirit Armament.. Will the both of you please do an examination?”"]},{"number":2971,"title":"Chapter 2971 - Too Despicable and Shameless (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Huang Yueli looked at Grandmaster Bai and went into a daze, “Grandmaster Bai, you’re here too?”","No one expected Huang Yueli to come out so quickly again!","Moreover, she said... she had already completed the third Spirit Armament!","Grandmaster Xiao’s smile froze, and there was no way he could maintain his calm. “Th... Third piece? Have you really refined the third Spirit Armament? You’re that fast!”","eedless to say, President Gao and Grandmaster Bai were speechless.","Huang Yueli placed the Spirit Armament into Grandmaster Xiao’s hands and shrugged. “Alright, I have to continue being busy. If Grandmasters don’t have any issues, you","don’t need to wait at the entrance. When I have finished refining all the armaments, I will send it over to you!”","Grandmaster Xiao laughed dryly, “We’re still ok, and it’s not tiring. We might be old, but we still have the energy to take a few steps.”","Huang Yueli looked strangely at Grandmaster Xiao upon hearing that.","He could rest but wasn’t willing to! Could this be some strange habit of those Grandmasters? Did they like to take a walk to work out for no particular reason?","But Huang Yueli didn’t think too much about it. She simply walked straight back into the armament refining room and continued to refine.","The minute her figure vanished from sight, Grandmaster Bai jumped up and urged, “Quick, quick, bring that piece of Spirit Armament to the assessment mechanism! I must","witness it with my own eyes, so see if you’re lying to me or not!”","Time passed slowly and the sun was now descending in the west.","When it was midnight, Huang Yueli had indeed finished refining all ten Spirit Armaments!","Seeing those Spirit Armaments nearly lined up on the table, President Gao, Grandmaster Bai, and Grandmaster Xiao were so shaken that they could not describe their shock","with mere words!","Huang Yueli... she really managed to do it!","She had completed an impossible mission!","If it wasn’t for the truth that was put in front of them, no one in the world would ever believe in such a ridiculous thing.","This young man in front of them did not only have outstanding innate talent. His comprehension, endurance, energy were all first-class. He could be said to be the most","outstanding armament refining genius for three lifetimes. Using heaven-defying and devil to describe him was not exaggerated at all!","Huang Yueli was totally exhausted.","She had continuously refined 10 low grade Spirit Armaments in such a short amount of time. To her, it was an extreme challenge.","After all, low grade Spirit Armaments could be said to be her current stage standard limit!","Moreover, she had been extremely meticulous while refining each piece of Spirit Armament. She kept on analyzing, hoping to do her best effort. In this way, the","consumption of her mental power was much greater.","Under President Gao’s hospitality, Huang Yueli had her dinner then returned to her room. Then she dropped onto the bed and fell asleep.","The next day, the situation was the same.","Ever since Huang Yueli woke up in the morning, she entered the armament refining room and started to refine the Spirit Armaments.","tt was until midnight when she completed another 10 pieces of Spirit Armaments. She had finally completed refining all the standardized Spirit Armaments.","Huang Yueli was completely exhausted, and when she looked at them, she found that they looked very blurry. That was a sign of depletion of energy.","But looking at those twenty nearly arranged, shining Spirit Armaments, her eyes glimmered with delightfulness and satisfaction.","As expected, even if it were Spirit Armaments from God Realm, it didn’t daunt her as well!","n the future, she must refine Li Moying’s strongest inherent fated Holy Armament!."]},{"number":2972,"title":"Chapter 2972 - Too Despicable and Shameless (4)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","It shouldn’t be too far off to realize her objective!","Grandmaster Xiao, will you please do an inventory check on these Spirit Armaments. If there are no problems, we can proceed with the transaction!”","Grandmaster Xiao didn’t even bother to look and beamed as he said, “Young Master Li, I’ve already checked on these Spirit Armaments and every single piece is the finest","quality! I didn’t expect you to immediately utilize those techniques that I’ve taught you. Your power of comprehension is really too shocking!”","To be praised by a peak rate Sky Gem Grandmaster like Grandmaster Xiao, other Spiritual Armament Masters would be shaking with agitation at this point.","But Huang Yueli merely smiled and replied courteously, “Grandmaster Xiao, you’ve overpraised me! Do you think that there are any problems with these Spirit Armaments?”","Hearing Huang Yueli repeating her question once again, Grandmaster Xiao suddenly came to his senses and said, “Oh, there’s no problem at all! Let’s settle the bill right","now!”","Saying that, he didn’t put his hand into his pocket. Instead, he walked to President Gao and said, “Old Gao, why are you in a blank? Quickly pay for it!”","resident Gao felt extremely aggrieved!","But one had to accept to lose since they agreed to bet. It would be even more embarrassing if one reneged on the debt!","Moreover, he was a Sky Gem Grandmaster so he wasn’t lacking in that bit of money...","resident Gao was gloomy for a second. Then he took out a gold-rimmed black card from his realm ring.","“There are a total of twenty low grade Spirit Armaments. Adding on to those twenty pieces that you’ve given me, it’s a total of forty pieces. Each piece is 250 thousand high","grade crystal jades so it works out to be a total of ten million crystal jades. It’s not easy to hold on to so much money, so I’ve deposited it in this crystal card.”","Huang Yueli received the crystal card and her eyes lit up. “So, this is the legendary crystal card! It’s my first time seeing it!”","Ever since she ascended, she had stayed in various inns and saw those wealthy God Realm practitioners taking out their crystal cards to settle the bill.","Every single time, it would attract a round of gasps and envious looks.","Even the innkeeper and waiter’s attitude became respectful.","She didn’t expect herself to become an owner of a crystal card now!","Huang Yueli expressed her satisfaction. “Since this is so, I’d like to thank all of you for your passionate hospitality!”","The three of them were shocked by Huang Yueli making such a big deal out of this.","The crystal card might be a thing that represented one’s status in ordinary practitioners’ eyes. But to Spiritual Armament Masters, that wasn’t some kind of treasure at all.","In God Realm, as long as one saved up ten thousand high grade crystal jades at one go, one would be able to obtain the lowest grade white crystal card. The black gold","crystal card that Huang Yueli was holding might be higher by several grades, but based on her armament refining skills, there would be plenty of money for her to earn in","the future!","She wouldn’t even bother about this crystal card by then.","“Alright, President Gao is indeed a generous and frank person to pay upon receiving the goods! It was a pleasant cooperation. If you have any other good deals like this, we","can continue to cooperate next time! If there’s nothing else, I’d make a move first!”","Huang Yueli didn’t care about what they were thinking. As long as she received the money, she was prepared to leave in contentment.","But she had just taken a step when she remembered another thing. Then she turned around.","“Right, I almost forgot the most important matter!”","“Young Master Li, what other matters are there?”","The three of them were stunned.","Huang Yueli turned to President Gao. “President Gao, other than attending Grandmaster Xiao’s lecture, I came to the Sky Gem Glass Chamber because I wanted to apply for","the Spiritual Armament Master’s badge...”."]},{"number":2973,"title":"Chapter 2973 - Too Despicable and Shameless (5)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Saying this, President Gao and the others suddenly remembered that the badge which Huang Yueli wore was still a Spiritual Armament apprentice’s badge.","He hurriedly said, “I see. Young Master Li, why didn’t you say this earlier! I’ll get you the badge immediately!”","resident Gao turned around and was just about to leave. Then he thought for a moment, stopped, and frowned.","“But, there’s just one thing... based on your standard, even we Sky Gem Grandmasters are not as good as you. It’s fine even if we give you a high ranking Spiritual Armament","Master’s badge! But according to the Sky Gem Glass Chamber’s Headquarters’ regulation, we can only award the corresponding certification to the Spirit Armament that","you have refined. I wonder if Young Master Li knows how to refine high grade Spirit Armaments? If you know, I can give you the high rank Spiritual Armament Master","badge. If not, I can only distribute you with the low rank badge.”","Originally, based on Huang Yueli’s disguised bone age, even if she managed to refine a mid grade Spirit Armament, she would already be a peerless genius.","But now, President Gao was asking if she could refine high grade Spirit Armaments.","The three Sky Gem Grandmasters thought that Huang Yueli’s innate talent was so heaven-defying that all the miracles that happened to her seemed very normal.","However, Huang Yueli was about to disappoint the three of them.","She shook her head and said, “I can only refine low grade Spirit Armaments for now. But President Gao need not feel awkward about this. I just want a Spiritual Armament","Master’s badge, so that I can use the Sacred Phoenix Race’s teleportation array...”","resident Gao said in enlightenment, “With the low rank Spiritual Armament Master’s status, Sacred Phoenix Race will allow you to use the teleportation array. That’s no","need to worry about it.”","Huang Yueli smiled, “That’s great.”","She received the low rank Spiritual Armament Master’s badge from President Gao and pinned it on the upper right position above her chest.","After that, she waved and walked away quickly.","While she walked, her footsteps were light and quick. She felt as though she was about to fly!","After experiencing those few months of impoverished lifestyle, this was the first time she felt that having money was really great!","With the ten million high grade crystal jades in her hand, it felt even better by a thousand hundred times than when she first sold her Profound Armament in her past life!","Based on this, Spiritual Armament Masters were indeed a moneymaking occupation. She had to refine armaments properly so that she could provide for her husband in the","future!","Whatever her husband took fancy to, she would buy it! She had the money, so she could be wilful about it!","Li Moying’s uniquely handsome countenance appeared in her mind, and she suddenly felt that she missed him even more.","She wondered what Li Moying was doing well in the Cloudy Qilin clan? Was he cultivating hard?","Very soon, she made her way back to the Double Prosperity Inn.","When the innkeeper saw her walking in, he abruptly stood up and spoke in an unfriendly tone. “Young Master Li, where have you been to? I didn’t see you for the past few","days and I thought you had slipped off, preparing to renege on the bill! I’m telling you, you didn’t check out of your room in the past few days and I had been keeping it for","you. You need to pay for it! Don’t even think you can skip paying for it!”","When Huang Yueli left, she was tied for time and was in a rush, so she naturally didn’t think about checking out.","She knew that it was her fault so she spoke courteously, “Innkeeper, it’s my negligence. But don’t worry, I’ll definitely pay for...”","Before she could finish her sentence, the innkeeper cut her off.","“Pay for it? You said you would pay for it? Did you think that I will believe a liar like you?!”."]},{"number":2974,"title":"Chapter 2974 - Too Despicable and Shameless (6)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","“When you first came in, I already found it strange. A Spiritual Armament apprentice like you can’t even pay for the deposit? From the looks of it, you’re indeed tricking me!","I’m telling you, if you can’t pay today, I will..., this... what is this??”","The innkeeper stared at the black gold crystal card that Huang Yueli put in front of him, and his eyeballs almost popped out!","“Black... black gold crystal card?? This... this is a counterfeit, isn’t it?”","Huang Yueli was speechless upon hearing that. “Can you even counterfeit something like this?”","Of course, it wasn’t a counterfeit!","There was only one Skyline Bank in the entire God Realm and that was commonly managed by all twelve God clans. No one would dare to create any counterfeit in front of","them.","“B... But...”","This grade of crystal cards are not even owned by some middle rank Spiritual Armament Masters, moreover for a Spiritual Armament apprentice like her?","Thinking of this, the innkeeper’s swept a glance on the badge pinned on her chest.","He was immediately stunned. “You... this.. this badge... when did you turn into a Spiritual Armament Master??”","The innkeeper subconsciously rubbed his eyes, thinking that he might have seen it wrongly!","A month ago, when Huang Yueli just came to stay here, she brought out a Spiritual Armament apprentice badge. It had only been such a short duration and she had already","become a Spiritual Armament Master??","Was he still dreaming?","Not only was the innkeeper stunned, even those guests who were crowded around were also stunned by this.","Originally, they only wanted to take a look at the fella who dared to renege on the bills at Double Prosperity Inn. But in the end, they saw a low rank Spiritual Armament","Master!","A Spiritual Armament Master’s status was noble and their quantity was very rare. Most practitioners had never met one at such proximity in their entire lives!","“This young man is actually a Spiritual Armament Master!”","“I didn’t expect us to be staying in the same inn as a Spiritual Armament Master. It’s such an honor!”","“This innkeeper is also very amusing. He’s a Spiritual Armament Master, so why would he renege on the bill? Moreover, what if he doesn’t pay? It’s already very good for him","to be willing to stay in Double Prosperity Inn!”","The discussions were fluctuating and when the innkeeper heard that, his face flushed slightly.","A Spiritual Armament apprentice wasn’t considered as something but a genuine Spiritual Armament Master wasn’t an existence that merchants like them could afford to","offend!","He hurriedly said, “So... Young Master Li, you’re a Spiritual Armament Master! Why didn’t you say so earlier! Please don’t take it against a nobody like me for offending you","today. Please show mercy on me. I’m really sorry about it...”","Huang Yueli stood at the original spot, ignoring the surrounding gazes, regardless if it was worship or disdain, without any change in her expression.","She tapped the side of the table with the black gold crystal card. “Then the payment for the room stay...”","“Oh, Young Master Li, why are you asking me about the payment! Like what the customer said earlier, it’s our inn’s honor for you to come here and stay...”","Huang Yueli shook her head and interrupted him. “It’s just payment for the room, would I take advantage of you? I will pay for it! Just deduct the crystal jades for the","duration that I’ve stayed! Right, remember to deduct another day’s payment. I am staying here tonight and will leave Flame Square City tomorrow.”","When the innkeeper heard her say that, he didn’t dare say anything else.."]},{"number":2975,"title":"Chapter 2975 - So Impressive (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","He carefully received the crystal card and deducted the month-long payment.","Actually, the total was just merely three or four high grade crystal jades. It didn’t even amount to the loose change in the crystal card, so Huang Yueli couldn’t find the joy of spending any money at all.","The innkeeper held the crystal card with two hands and respectfully passed it to her.","“Young... Young Master Li, your crystal card!”","Huang Yueli nodded her head, kept the card, and returned to her room.","In the dark and silent night, Huang Yueli lay on her bed but somehow, she couldn’t sleep at all.","Her thoughts had already drifted to the man who had disappeared for more than a year.","She had been rushing on her journey in this period and would deliberately or unintentionally run into some practitioners and ask about the news from the Cloudy Qilin clan, especially if it was related to Cloudy Qilin","clan’s god grade genius.","Unfortunately, other than the initial few Sacred Phoenix Race practitioners, the other ordinary practitioners knew nothing about Li Moying at all.","Many people didn’t know about the Cloudy Qilin clan’s god grade genius, and neither did they believe in Huang Yueli’s words. They assumed that it was impossible to attain god grade innate talent and the so-called god","grade genius was fabricated by the god clans to intimidate those ordinary humans.","Although there wasn’t any news of Li Moying, Huang Yueli always felt that he should be cultivating hard in Cloudy Qilin Continent!","Yesterday morning, when she was refining armaments, that sudden image that flashed past her mind made her heart instantly grow tight!","She seemed to have seen Li Moying throwing up blood...","That scene was just a hallucination but it looked extremely realistic. It instantly scared her out of her wits and directly caused the Spirit Armament furnace to explode.","Later on, although she realized that it was fake, her heart was still apprehensive. She simply could not calm down, no matter what.","It shouldn’t be real, right? It’s impossible to be real!","Li Moying’s innate talent was so high and his character was so composed. He was also the core for the entire Cloudy Qilin clan and had a noble status. Why would he possibly meet with danger for no rhyme or reason?","But luckily, the same image didn’t appear in the next two days after that.","“It must be because I missed him too much, that’s why it caused this hallucination... sigh!” Huang Yueli shut her eyes and muttered to herself, “But tomorrow I will set off. If everything goes smoothly, I will be able to","teleport to the Cloudy Qilin clan in less than two weeks. By then... we will be able to meet again!”","Thinking of the shocked look when Li Moying saw her again, Huang Yueli’s lips curled into a smile.","On the second day, she woke up and headed to look for the innkeeper on the first floor to check out of her room.","The innkeeper kept flattering her and sent her off with utmost gratitude.","Huang Yueli had already checked out the location of the teleportation array, and she headed over there straight.","However, just as she was passing by a corner, a carriage suddenly stopped at a distance near her.","Immediately following that, a young lady’s graceful figure got down from the carriage.","Huang Yueli was in a daze. That figure looked a little familiar...","Young Miss Leyun!","The mid rank Spiritual Armament Master, who was embarrassed by Huang Yueli in the Sky Gem Glass Chamber, created trouble unreasonably, and was finally chased out by Grandmaster Xiao!","Although she had a veil over her face, Huang Yueli recognized her without any problem.","“This woman didn’t leave Flame Square City?”","Huang Yueli’s brows rose in slight astonishment.."]},{"number":2976,"title":"Chapter 2976 - So Impressive (2)","paragraphs":["Logically speaking, Leyun was someone who minded her reputation very much.","She was embarrassed at the Sky Gem Glass Chamber, and the ordinary people had on the streets also crowded around her to see her pathetic sight. So how could she even possibly have the cheek to continue staying in Flame Square City?","Suspicions filled Huang Yueli’s heart, but she didn’t bother to think too much about it. With a nonchalant look, she continued to walk forward.","When Li Leyun got off the carriage, she was troubled and her expression was dazed. Even her footsteps weren’t stable.","She slipped and bumped into Huang Yueli.","The latter didn’t expect Li Leyun to suddenly fall. But her reaction was extremely swift and immediately stepped back.","Hence, Li Leyun who was originally supposed to fall on her suddenly plopped onto the ground on her face.","The surrounding guards all ran forward.","\"Young Miss Leyun, you... how are you? Why did you suddenly fall?\" \"Are you hurt anywhere? Can you still stand?\" All of the guards looked tense and their hearts were pounding with fear. Li Leyun originally was very arrogant and her temper was terrible. Moreover, she had been feeling upset over Young Master Moying in the past few days! She vented her anger that she suffered from Li Moying on the guards. All of them were tormented badly and no one dared to offend that young miss at all.</pre>","Now, they didn't pay any attention and caused her to slip and fall! They could imagine just how miserable they would become. As expected, Li Leyun had just stood up and flew into a rage. She howled angrily, \"You bunch of trash, where have you guys hid yourselves to slack off again? Are there any guards who act like you guys? What use do I have for you?\" She was exasperated and she took out the whip that was hung by her waist, lashing it out towards the guards. All of them didn't dare to make a sound. They didn't even dare to evade her move.</pre>","Li Leyun whipped them a few times but it didn't make her feel any better. When she fell earlier, many pedestrians had seen her and she was thoroughly embarrassed! Moreover, this was the second time in just a few days! More importantly, the dress that she was wearing was brand new! Previously, she heard Brother Moying talking about the popular flowing dress in Soaring Heavens Continent, and that was the dress that Li Moying's Lower Realm wife loved wearing the most. Li Leyun tried to find out from other people and finally managed to form the correct design of the flowing dress. Then she looked for the most outstanding tailor in Sacred Phoenix Race to make the dress.</pre>","She had to say that this flowing dress design was indeed very exquisite. After she put the dress on, she felt that she was even more beautiful now. It also attracted many young ladies' envious gazes. But now, this fall caused her reputation to be destroyed! Li Leyun was furious and she turned her head to stare that the unlucky fellow who bumped into her and said nastily, \"Men, catch that scum who intentionally bumped into This Lady! How dare he cause me to be embarrassed, I will absolutely not let...\" She stopped in the middle of her sentence and finally took a clear look at the person who was standing in front of her.</pre>","Huang Yueli's disguised countenance had become one of Li Leyun's most hated person! The incident that happened in the Sky Gem Glass Chamber was something that she would never forget in her entire life! Originally, Li Leyun was already prepared to find a chance to catch Huang Yueli and give her a good beating. But because of Li Moying's sudden appearance in Flame Square City, she couldn't care about that then. Now, the enemies had crossed each other's path. A sinister sneer appeared on Li Leyun's face. \"So, it's you!\".</pre>"]},{"number":2977,"title":"Chapter 2977 - So Impressive (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","“Li Yuehuang, This Lady was troubled over the fact that I couldn’t find you, and here you are! It’s just nice, you’re digging your grave on your own!”","Huang Yueli met Li Leyun’s jealous and hateful gaze with a composed look.","Her lips curled slightly. “Young Miss Le, wow! You’re indeed a mid rank Spiritual Armament Master, you’re so impressive! Even when you stumbled and fell, you also need to","blame it on other people. I was just finding it strange. A mid rank Spiritual Armament Master should at least be in Dream Profound Realm mid-phase, isn’t it? Why can’t you","even walk properly? There aren’t any holes on the ground, how did you even fall? Even a three-year-old child is better than you!”","“Peet!”","When Huang Yueli said those sarcastic words, someone among the crowd instantly burst out into laughter!","It was because what she said was spot on! This matter was simply too amusing!","All the citizens in God Realm were practitioners and their balancing ability was something that Lower Realm ordinary people could not compare with. It was really rare for","someone to fall while walking.","If one fell accidentally, one would naturally blame themselves for failing to look carefully. Who would even blame the guards for not holding on to her?","“What’s the matter with this Spiritual Armament Master? Could there be a problem with her legs?”","“Who knows? She seems to be on familiar terms with that young man, perhaps she intentionally fell on him?”","“Hmm, what you said might be possible...”","Hearing those various ridiculous deductions from the bystanders, Li Leyun’s face flushed into a beetroot shade!","Someone actually compared her with this country bumpkin! It was simply the greatest insult to her.","She, Li Leyun, was to marry a peerless top exponent like Li Moying. This fella couldn’t even be compared to Li Moying’s finger!","Li Leyun jumped up in exasperation and flicked her whip towards the top of Huang Yueli’s head without any warning!","When Huang Yueli saw that, she squinted her eyes, and a cold intent flashed past.","Originally, she had no intention to clash with Li Leyun. After all, she was rushed for time and didn’t want to care about other people’s matters. Even when Li Leyun spoke","rudely, she was too lazy to rebuke her.","Whoever knew that this woman could not tell good from bad and even wanted to hit her!","Huang Yueli wondered which clan nurtured Li Leyun to become so arrogant and wilful!","At this moment, Li Leyun’s whip, which was flowed along with the wind, was about to land on Huang Yueli.","“Heavens! How could this woman be so vicious!”","“This buddy, be careful!”","“Quick, move aside!”","Li Leyun’s move blinded the entire group of bystanders.","Dream Profound Realm mid-phase cultivation was considered as top rated among the younger generation, moreover for ordinary citizens?","Everyone thought that the slim Huang Yueli would be seriously injured under this powerful attack.","Li Leyun naturally also thought so. She saw Huang Yueli standing still without even trying to hide and assumed that she was too shocked to move.","“A trash like you dares to go against This Lady?” She laughed sinisterly and increased the strength in her hand!","But whoever knew, the whip had landed halfway and stopped.","o matter how hard Li Leyun tried, it stopped in mid-air.","“Damn it, what’s going on!”","Li Leyun lifted her head in exasperation, only to realize the tail of the whip was held firmly in Huang Yueli’s palm.","That pair of hands were slender and beautiful, simply no different from a lady’s hand.."]},{"number":2978,"title":"Chapter 2978 - So Impressive (4)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","But under her control, Li Leyun’s rampant attack was reduced to nothing.","Li Leyun was stunned momentarily, not believing her eyes.","She subconsciously pulled backward, hoping to pull her whip back!","She tried once, and it didn’t move.","The second time, it also didn’t move.","Third time...","Li Leyun was tugging harder and harder, and she had used up all her energy. Her face flushed red, but she didn’t have any way to recoil the whip back at all.","At this point, everyone could tell that the young man, Huang Yueli’s disguised look, was a top exponent who didn’t reveal his power!","As for Li Leyun, in a bid to save her reputation, she continued to tug hard at her whip.","A faint smile curled up on Huang Yueli’s lips, and she suddenly released her right hand’s grip.","The next moment, Li Leyun felt the whip loosening. The tremendous impact made her lose control of her body, and she staggered back continuously, unable to stop. In the end, she landed on the ground on her butt.","‘Wow...”","Amid the bystanders’ gasps, Li Leyun sprawled on the ground in a disheveled look.","This fall directly made her see stars.","By the time she regained her senses, she realized that everyone was laughing at her, and she exploded into a rage!","It was her third time falling on the streets!","Moreover, this time was even more embarrassing than the previous two times. It was because she was the one who initiated the provocation. She wanted to teach the other person a lesson, but in the end, she was the one who ran into bad luck!","Luckily, this fall seemed very serious, but she wasn’t badly hurt. Only her butt was in pain.","Li Leyun bore with the pain and embarrassment, jumped up, and glowered at Huang Yueli. “Damn it! How dare you attack This Lady! You... are you tired of living!”","Huang Yueli blinked and asked with an innocent expression. “Attack? Since when did I attack you? Young Miss Le, you must speak with a conscience! Earlier, you were the one who tried to hit me. I held on to the whip for defense. Later, I saw that you were trying to pull the whip back, so I just let it go! I was thinking on your behalf, but you actually claim that I attacked you?”","Saying that, she turned to the surrounding practitioners and said in a clear, loud voice, “Everyone, you’ve witnessed the situation earlier. Will you please judge what is right?”","At this moment, the total number of bystanders increased again.","The two of them were surrounded by mountains of people.","Earlier when Li Leyun attacked, everyone saw Huang Yueli easily defeating the opponent.","“That’s right, that’s right. It’s this Young Miss Leyun’s fault!”","“This Young Master is already very magnanimous. He was whipped by her but only made her fall down. If I were him, I would definitely hit her back!”","“I wonder which force nurtured this genius, and how great is her innate talent? So what if she’s a Spiritual Armament Master? She is so arrogant, so she deserves to be taught a lesson!”","“That’s right. Her skills are no match for him, but she still has the cheek to complain here?”","Li Leyun’s brash look had already caused a public outcry.","Hearing their words, Li Leyun’s face flushed green then white. Pointing at Huang Yueli’s nose, she berated, “Shut up! Don’t try to shove your false arguments down their throats. Men, capture him!”","The guards exchanged glances and hesitated. However, they didn’t dare to defy Li Leyun’s orders so they could only step forward.."]},{"number":2979,"title":"Chapter 2979 - This Voice... (1)","paragraphs":["Translator: Misty Cloud Translations Editor: Misty Cloud Translations","Huang Yueli was surrounded by people but she was still calm and unhurried.","“Why? Didn’t you say earlier that you want to teach me a lesson personally? But now you’re sending your guards here as cannon fodders? Did you feel that you can’t beat me, so you’re frightened?”","Li Leyun was so stifled that she almost threw up blood.","What Huang Yueli just said had poked at her sore point once again!","Li Leyun had always prided herself as a heaven grade genius so even in a god clan like the Cloudy Qilin clan, she had always been on top rate level.","Never in her dreams did she expect herself to be taught a lesson by a human at such a small place!","Moreover, the other party’s ability had evidently surpassed her by so much...","The blow to her was simply too huge!","Not to mention that this human’s innate talent in Spirit Armament refining had totally crushed hers!","Li Leyun was put in an awkward position and her heart was filled with jealousy. She wished for nothing more than to strangle Huang Yueli to death!","On the surface, Huang Yueli looked calm and composed. But she was actually observing her surroundings as her thoughts raced past swiftly.","Li Leyun only brought four guards with her. But their cultivations should be higher than Li Leyun herself, which were around Dream Profound Realm end-phase.","Huang Yueli’s combat power far surpassed same leveled practitioners, so dealing with Li Leyun was a simple feat.","But it wouldn’t be easy for her to successfully escape from those higher leveled practitioners in front of her...","It seemed that she had to make use of the surrounding environment to create a commotion to escape.","Just as Huang Yueli was pondering over what course of action to take, a voice suddenly rang from a distance away.","“What are you guys doing here? Why is it so noisy?”","Following the voice, a tall young man made his way through the crowd and approached them.","Seeing Li Leyun, he asked in shock. “Young Miss Leyun, what are you doing here?”","When Li Leyun saw him, she excitedly jumped up. “Tian Yi, go beat that fellow for me. He disrespected me!”","Li Tian Yi was the guard who was allocated to Li Moying, and he was also ranked first.","Ordinary clansmen would not get the chance to stay by the future clan leader’s side. Li Tian Yi’s innate talent was extraordinary and his background wasn’t bad as well.","Li Tian Yi frowned but did not act according to her order.","‘Young Miss Leyun, no matter what conflict you have, can’t you stop creating a ruckus at my Young Master’s door? Can’t you settle your dispute elsewhere? Young Master had not shut his eyes for the past three days, and he finally just laid down to rest. But the commotion you created woke him up again.”","Hearing that, Li Leyun’s aggressive temper immediately died down. Her arrogant and wilful attitude disappeared and her tone instantly softened.","“Ah... this... I’m sorry, I didn’t do it on purpose...”","Li Tian Yi didn’t say anything much to her and just turned around as he indicated for the crowd to disperse. “Everyone, please go. There’s nothing much to look around here.”","Most people would not listen to the instruction after being chased away in such a manner.","But Li Tian Yi t s dressing, aura, and cultivation made them feel that he wasn’t a simple person. The bystanders had enough of watching the fun and since they were worried that they might get into trouble, they could only leave.","A strange feeling arose in Huang Yueli’s heart as she watched them.","Li Leyun’s arrogant character had completely changed because of this young man’s words.","She wondered who was the “Young Master” that this young man was referring to?."]},{"number":2980,"title":"Chapter 2980 - This Voice... (2)","paragraphs":["It was obvious that Li Leyun’s expression turned frightened when she heard the title “Young Master”.","Huang Yueli found it strange but she didn’t ask too much about this.","Being entangled with Li Leyun had wasted a lot of her time.","Now that Huang Yueli had already taught her a lesson, she didn’t want to stay here any longer.","Seeing the crowd dispersed, Huang Yueli also smuggled among them and prepared to leave.","Li Leyun turned her head and when she realized that Huang Yueli was about to slip away, she immediately shouted, “Li Yuehuang, you’re still trying to escape! Stand right there!”","When Li Tian Yi heard her sharp cry, he frowned. “Young Miss Leyun, if you’re not here to visit our Young Master, please leave immediately! Otherwise, if Young Master is enraged, none of us can take responsibility!”","Li Leyun’s face flushed pale and she stared fiercely at Huang Yueli. “Count yourself lucky! Next time if I ever see you again, I’ll not let you off!”","Saying that, she couldn’t be bothered with Huang Yueli and immediately followed behind Li Tian Yi, entering into a courtyard a short distance away.","That scum had offended her so even a thousand deaths weren’t enough to make up for it. But she could not afford to delay her visit to Brother Moying because of this small matter.","Hearing that he was in a bad mood, she decided to take advantage of this while he was feeling frail. She would show concern for him and make him fall in love with her.","Li Leyun and Li Tian Yi disappeared behind the courtyard door.","The bystanders on the streets also dispersed.","Huang Yueli stood in the empty street, and her gaze followed behind Li Leyun in a daze.","When she came back to her senses, she didn’t know what was going on because she followed them to the courtyard door. But stopped short of walking in.","Two guards appeared at the entrance and pulled out their long swords, blocking her way.","“Who are you?! This is a private residence, please leave immediately!”","Huang Yueli then regained her senses as she looked at that heavily guarded gaze on those guards’ faces. She instantly became embarrassed.","It indeed seemed rather suspicious of her to intrude into another person’s courtyard for no reason.","She didn’t know why she actually followed Li Leyun sneakily to this place. It was like some mysterious power that was pulling her along...","Just as Huang Yueli hesitated, the room suddenly broke out in a clamor.","There were mixed sounds like porcelain ware dropping on the ground, giving off an ear-splitting noise, a young lady’s screaming, and also...","There seemed to be a faint angry howl from a man.","This voice—!","Huang Yueli’s heart jolted. For an instance, she even felt that she had heard Li Moying’s voice!","But... how was this possible?","The guards saw her standing still and their expressions turned unfriendly as they unleashed the Profound Energy within them. Then they barked, “Why are you still standing here in a daze? Still not going to leave? If you still don’t leave, don’t blame us for attacking you!”","Huang Yueli frowned slightly. She wasn’t afraid of these two guards in front of her. Although their cultivations were much higher than hers, it was still difficult for them to pose a genuine threat to her.","But Huang Yueli knew that she was at fault, so she wasn’t willing to argue with them.","“I’m sorry, I’ve walked to the wrong door. I’ll leave right now...”","Huang Yueli cupped her fist in her other hand and stepped back.","Just in that instance when she turned around, a messy shout was heard from the rear courtyard.","Huang Yueli l s footsteps halted and she couldn’t help but stop and listen again.."]},{"number":2981,"title":"Chapter 2981 - 1 This Voice... (3)","paragraphs":["However, this time, she didn’t hear the voice that she was anticipating hearing.","“Are you leaving or not?” The guards urging voices were filled with threats.","It seemed as though they were about to attack if she hesitated any longer!","Huang Yueli hurriedly said, “I’ll leave right now. Please don’t be so hasty...” When she walked away, the two guards stared at her tightly until she walked to the end of the street. They heaved a sigh of relief when they totally couldn’t see her at all.","It wasn’t because the guards were overly anxious, but the responsibility for them to guard Young Master Moying was simply too important!","Even the clan leader wasn’t as important as Young Master Moying. After all, a god grade genius represented the entire Cloudy Qilin clan’s future!","Moreover, this was the Sacred Phoenix Continent’s turf. If Young Master was exposed, it would cause a huge controversy.","Huang Yueli walked along the streets slowly as she recalled the voice that she heard in the courtyard.","Although it was just a cold “Shut up”, the tone and voice was deep and sexy. It seemed extremely similar to her husband’s voice!","But Huang Yueli knew that Li Moying would absolutely not appear in Sacred Phoenix Race’s turf. All these were probably because she missed him too much, and it was just her hallucination.","“It’s better not to let my thoughts run wild! Today, that Leyun had wasted too much of my time! If this continues, it will turn dark soon...”","Huang Yueli shook her head and continued heading towards the teleportation array.","Flame Square City’s teleportation array wasn’t difficult to find. It was just beneath the city wall on the east, and it occupied a large space.","Arrays were distributed into nine layers, and each layer was repeatedly overlapped, radiating outwards.","Huang Yueli was considered a professional, and she could tell that this nine layered array was essentially the same. But it was linked together through special methods and rare treasures. Each time a layer was added, the might would be amplified and could teleport to a place even further than the previous.","Outside the array, there were three teams of soldiers who were standing guard and patrolling the area. Seeing Huang Yueli walking close, one soldier stepped forward immediately and stopped her. “Halt! It’s the military area up ahead and non-military personnel are not allowed to come near!”","Huang Yueli walked up to explain, “This buddy, I want to use Flame Square City’s teleportation array. I wonder if you can help me convey this message?”","“You wish to use the teleportation array?” The soldier frowned when he heard that. “What did you think the teleportation array is for? Do you know how much crystal jades you need to spend for one-time teleportation? If it’s not a pressing situation on the battlefield, it’s impossible to activate the teleportation array! You’d better stop dreaming and go back quickly!” Huang Yueli was rejected immediately, but she wasn’t too anxious over it.","Theoretically speaking, the teleportation array was indeed built to fight against the demon tribe. Only military personnel were allowed to utilize it.","But actually, various large forces would usually activate the teleportation array for other reasons. They would often see if the person who applied to use the teleportation array was an important figure.","Huang Yueli hurriedly grabbed a handful of medium grade crystal jades and stuffed it into the soldier’s hand. She also said at the same time, “Buddy, can I trouble you to help me pass the message? I’m a Spiritual Armament Master from the Sky Gem Glass Chamber, and my name is Li Yuehuang. I’m asking to use the teleportation array so that I can take part in the war against the demon tribe at the frontline.”","The soldier received the bribe and silently thought that this fellow was rather street-smart.","But when he heard what she said, he had a huge shock."]},{"number":2982,"title":"Chapter 2982 - This Voice... (4)","paragraphs":["lan","Only now did he notice the Spiritual Armament Master’s badge that was pinned on Huang Yueli’s chest. His attitude immediately changed.","“Oh... you’re a Spiritual Armament Master! I must have been blind earlier. If I’ve offended you, will Master Li please accept my apologies! I wonder where would you like to be teleported to?”","Huang Yueli replied, “Empyrean Fox Continent, Blessed City.” Before she came, Huang Yueli had already studied God Realm’s map in detail, and she had set the teleportation destinations.","Flame Square City’s teleportation array distance was extremely limited. It would at most step over to the distance of two continents, the furthest reaching Blessed City in Empyrean Fox Continent.","Blessed City was located in Empyrean Fox Continent’s most southern end. The exterior of the city was an important warzone where humans and the demon tribe engaged in battle. It was extremely messy, and danger lurked everywhere. Ordinary practitioners would normally not head to that place.","But to save time, Huang Yueli decided to be teleported to the furthest place from here.","The soldier turned around and headed to the sentry post to report on this. Shortly after, a practitioner dressed in a commanding officer’s uniform appeared and verified Huang Yueli’s identity.","After verifying that Huang Yueli was indeed a noble Spiritual Armament Master, the commander’s attitude became extremely deferential.","“Master Li, I heard that you want to go to Empyrean Fox Continent’s Blessed City?”","Huang Yueli nodded and replied, “That’s","right.”","The commander looked her up and down, then said, “Master Li, you might not know the current situation recently. In the past two months, Blessed City had been repeatedly attacked by the demon tribe and had been in a tight state of security. Heading to Blessed City now is extremely dangerous. If you’ve got nothing on there, it’s better to take another route.”","Huang Yueli asked, “Which other routes would allow me to cross over two large continents?”","The commander was stunned. “This... crossing two large continents is of course not possible. Other than heading through Blessed City’s route, which was specially constructed to fight the demon tribe. The other routes would only lead to the sides of Black Tortoise Continent...”","Hearing that, Huang Yueli frowned. If one continent only could lead to the next continent, then the total time she spent on the journey alone would take at least half a year.","She thought for a moment and said, “Then I’d better head to Blessed City!”","Huang Yueli thought silently, “I’m just going to stay in Blessed City for a day or two. After that, I will teleport to another continent. Surely I won’t be that unlucky to meet with trouble, right?” The commander saw her insistence and didn’t continue to persuade any further. “The fee for using the teleportation array is based on distance. So the pricing would not be the same. To teleport to the neighboring Black Tortoise Continent, you only need to pay 100 thousand high grade crystal jades. But if you’re heading to Empyrean Fox Continent, the price would be 250 thousand crystal jades. The price might be more expensive, but the cost of maintenance for the teleportation array is also very high...”","Before he could finish explaining, Huang Yueli nodded and said, “This I know. Can I pay using the crystal card?”","Saying that, she took out the black gold crystal card.","Seeing that high grade crystal card in her hand, the commander’s eyes widened, and he thought inwardly, “I’ve met with a tycoon today!” Guests who came to use the teleportation array were mostly rich and powerful people but most of them would feel that the fee of teleportation was too high.","The commander said a little more because he noticed that Huang Yueli was a low rank Spiritual Armament Master.","After all, 250 thousand high grade crystal jades to a low rank Spiritual Armament Master was a huge expense. Whoever knew, Huang Yueli simply took out her black gold crystal card casually!"]},{"number":2983,"title":"Chapter 2983 - Exclusive Fragrance (1)","paragraphs":["The commander received the crystal card and deducted the fees.","Huang Yueli asked, “How long does it take to activate the teleportation array?”","The commander smiled and said, “It’s a coincidence that you’re going to Blessed City. We have just received an order to teleport a few lords from the god clans to the battlefield with the demon tribe. You can teleport along with them. In around an hour, you can set off.”","Huang Yueli revealed a satisfied smile, “That’s","great!”","Flame Square City, Cloudy Qilin clan’s secret base.","Li Leyun followed Li Tian Yi through the front courtyard, all the way to the main hall entrance.","The latter stopped in front of the room door and raised his hand by the side of the door. But he hesitated for a long time, not knocking. Li Leyun looked at him curiously, “Why aren’t you knocking on the door?”.","Li Tian Yi suppressed his voice and said, “Young Master had been cultivating in the past few days but he didn’t manage to breakthrough. In fact, his Profound Energy suffered a backlash and his mood is extremely irritable. Whoever appeared before him would be berated. Moreover, he had been drinking in the past few days..” Li Tian Yi showed a sorrowful expression.","Li Moying’s current condition simply made the guards worried!","Ever since the news of Huang Yueli’s possible death was heard, he had been leading his days in a drunken stupor. Whoever dared to persuade him would end up badly injured by him!","Seeing the usually calm and composed Young Master Moying who was unfazed by any circumstances slowly degrading himself, everyone felt extremely shocked!","No one expected Li Moying to have such deep feelings for his Lower Realm wife ... Originally, the guards assumed that he didn’t know how to please young ladies when those rich, young girls offered themselves to him! So, it was because the person wasn’t right. These rich, young ladies were not the love of his life...","Li Tian Yi was worried but he didn’t say the real reason for Li Moying’s depression.","Because Li Moying had already given an ultimatum that no one was allowed to leak out the information between him and Sacred Phoenix Race’s god grade genius’s relationship.","So, the guards merely used the excuse that Li Moying had a mishap during his cultivation. When Li Leyun heard that, she didn’t suspect anything at all.","She immediately turned anxious and said, “How can Brother Moying do this? It’s very normal to suffer a backlash during cultivation and it could happen to anyone! His innate talent is so high, even if he meets with a bottleneck, he will definitely be able to pass through it smoothly very soon!”","Li Leyun pushed Li Tian Yi, who was blocking the door, aside.","“All of you are so useless. You can’t even persuade your Young Master properly. Let me do it!”","Saying that, she pushed the door open and jogged right in.","“Wait, Young Miss Leyun!”","Li Tian Yi couldn’t stop her at all and could only watch her rushing towards the volcano.","He shut his eyes, not daring to look! The scene following that was extremely miserable! As expected, before Li Leyun had reached Li Moying, she already sensed rampant and disorderly energy that filled the entire room.","This energy was released from Li Moying. The nearer she got, the more powerful that Profound Energy suppression felt.","Li Leyun was impacted suddenly, and her feet softened, almost unable to take it!","But she clenched her teeth and worked up her Profound Energy. Steadying herself firmly, she continued to trudge towards him."]},{"number":2984,"title":"Chapter 2984 - 4 Exclusive Fragrance (2)","paragraphs":["Li Moying was currently seated on the chair. His elbows were on the armrest, propping up his head.","His pitch-dark eyes were as black as the eternal night, yet it radiated a strange cold glint.","He leaned against the chair, lifting his eyes slightly. It seemed as though he saw her, but also as though he didn’t.","Li Leyun felt a sign of danger as his gaze swept past her. But that threat was tagged along with an astonishing charm. It attracted her to keep walking towards him, even though she knew that she was walking towards a bottomless abyss without any regrets...","Li Leyun’s heart palpitated swiftly. Although her physical body was unable to take on Li Moying suppression and her fingers were starting to turn icy cold, she didn’t stop moving","“Brother Moying, you... what’s the matter with","you?”","Li Moying totally ignored her. His slender fingers picked up a wine cup and placed it to his lips. Lifting his head, he drank the entire cup of wine in one go.","It was only now that Li Leyun realized that the entire room was filled with a thick stench of alcohol.","Evidently, Li Moying had drunk a lot of wine when he was here alone.","Thinking of that, she hurriedly walked forward, intending to grab the wine cup away from him.","“Brother Moying, you can’t continue drinking like this! I heard from Tian Yi and Tian Er that you threw up blood a couple of days ago when you were cultivating, and your meridians are already damaged. You should be resting properly right now, how can you drink? Brother Moying... AH!” Li Leyun was practically leaning onto Li Moying, hoping to express her gentleness to him.","However, right before her fingers were about to touch his shirt, a huge impact suddenly attacked her!","Li Leyun was caught off-guard and instantly fell backward!","When she fell to the ground, her expression was still in a daze, apparently unaware of what had just happened!","She did not think that Li Moying wouldn’t even allow her to touch him and just threw her off directly.","Li Tian Yi was looking at the door, and he shook his head silently.","He knew that this would happen. Li Leyun was too opinionated. Did she think that their Young Master would allow anyone to go near him just because he was drunk?","Or did she assume that she held a special place in Li Moying’s heart, which would make him look at her differently?","Li Leyun was pushed to the ground, and her face flushed red from embarrassment.","However, she clenched her teeth and stood up after a short moment.","No way, she couldn’t just give up like this! This was a rare chance!","She had to make her Brother Moying sense the gentle and meticulous side of her. In this way, when he regained his consciousness, he would be touched deeply by her deep sentiments!","“Brother Moying, you... please put down the wine cup, will you?”","She walked towards Li Moying once again. But this time, she took extra caution, not daring to go too close. Neither did she dare to touch him again. She persuaded him cautiously from a distance away. Li Moying seemed to have heard her voice and his gaze swept past her, then suddenly stopped!","His pupils constricted, staring tightly at Li Leyun as he revealed a shocked look.","Li Leyun saw the change in expression and assumed that he recognized her and was touched by her gentleness. She hurriedly said, “Brother Moying, you... are you clear-minded now? I’m Li Leyun! You shouldn’t drink anymore. I’ll help you back to the room, okay?”"]},{"number":2985,"title":"Chapter 2985 - Exclusive Fragrance (3)","paragraphs":["However, Li Moying didn’t answer her.","He looked at her from head to toe, as a hazy image appeared in front of his eyes. That familiar flowing dress, the hem was like a floating cloud. It felt as though the young lady whom he had loved for two lifetimes had once again appeared before him, coming close to him.","Moreover, he seemed to have smelled that familiar scent.","Seemingly as though there was.","That was Huang Yueli’s exclusive fragrance, which would rove over him every single night in his dreams.","“Li’er... is... that you?”","His thin lips parted as though he was mumbling something. But he spoke so softly that even Li Leyun, who stood a short distance away, could not hear him clearly.","Li Leyun was excited by his scorching gaze, her heart beating so hard that it seemed as though it was about to jump out from her throat.","Li Moying had never gazed at her with so much concentration before this.","Li Leyun had wondered to herself many times in the past, thinking of the feeling of being gazed at so gently and attentively by Li Moying.","It was only now that she realized that this man seemed cold and emotionless. But when he was gentle, that gaze could simply drown someone...","Li Leyun’s cheeks blushed, and she was even more certain that Li Moying had been touched by her gestures.","She walked up quickly and tried to walk next to Li Moying.","This time, Li Moying didn’t attack her. On the contrary, his gaze quietly stayed on the young lady in front of him, not shifting away at all.","Li Leyun realized that he didn’t reject her and happily stretched out her hand, intending to help him up.","“Brother Moving, you...”","Whoever knew, the moment she spoke, it was like a stone dropping into the water. It instantly broke the daze that Li Moying was in.","His dark gaze instantly became clear.","“It’s not her!”","“This voice... it doesn’t belong to my Li’er!”","Detecting Li Leyun nearing him, he raised his right hand and threw her off once again!","With a “bang”, Li Leyun’s body flew out.","If it wasn’t because Li Tian Yi had already realized that something was amiss and dashed over timely to catch her, Li Leyun would suffer from a serious injury this time!","Even so, Li Leyun’s right ankle was fractured by the huge impact. She was in so much pain that her complexion turned pale.","However, as compared to the pain, the greater impact for her was that Li Moying had actually pushed her aside once again. Moreover, his attack was so heavy, totally disregarding the fact that she was a lady!","“He... how could he do this?”","“Earlier, he was the one who looked at me in utmost adoration, as though I am his only true love.”","“Why did things suddenly change in the blink of an eye?”","Not only did Li Moying push her away, but his gaze also turned as cold as ice. There was none of the gentleness left from before!","Just as Li Leyun was in a daze, Li Moying had already stood up and walked right out of the door.","When he passed by Li Leyun, he didn’t even take a look at her.","She turned anxious and cried out, “Brother Moying, you... where are you going?”","Li Moying swept her a glance and said in a biting cold voice, “You’re not qualified to wear this dress. Change out of it and don’t ever let me see you wearing a flowing dress ever!”","Li Leyun’s eyes widened in shock. Never in her wildest dream had she imagined that Li Moying actually would say such a thing!","She thought that putting on this dress would enable her to attract Li Moying’s gaze, to let him notice her exceptional beauty..."]},{"number":2986,"title":"Chapter 2986 - Exclusive Fragrance (4)","paragraphs":["The more Li Leyun thought, the more unreconciled she was, and she gritted her teeth.","“No, I won’t change out of it. I like this dress! Why is it that only that woman can wear, and I can’t? This is my freedom!”","Li Moying sneered, “Freedom? If you want freedom, then don’t appear in front of me! You’re not changing, is it? Tian Yi, go help her!”","“Yes, Young... huh, what?”","Li Tian Yi subconsciously agreed to Li Moying’s order but when he subconsciously understood what he said, the former was stunned.","Did he hear him wrongly? She was their clan leader’s niece!","“Didn’t you hear what I said?” Li Moying’s voice grew colder as he swept him a deep gaze that made one shudder.","Li Tian Yi felt his leg turning soft.","Ever since he received the news of Huang Yueli’s demise, Li Moying was like a changed man. He was simply even scarier than the demon tribe!","The sweat on Li Tian Yi’s forehead dripped down, totally unsure of what he should do!","He wasn’t Li Moying and didn’t have the guts to offend the clan leader’s niece. But his Master’s command was something that he didn’t dare to not abide...","He could only brace himself and persuade her. “Young Miss Li, why don’t you just change out of that dress? Young Master is in a bad mood now, so why must you go against him?”","“I...” Li Leyun’s face was not reconciled!","She was the Cloudy Qilin clan’s god grade genius!","Not only was a god clan’s status noble, her innate talent just merely just second to Li Moying’s! She also had gorgeous looks!","Why didn’t Li Moying take any fancy to her, and keep thinking about his Lower Realm wife? No matter how beautiful that woman was, she was just a lowly human who couldn’t even be compared to her finger!","Li Leyun felt extremely aggrieved but Li Moying’s might was simply too powerful!","Under his piercing gaze, Li Leyun’s heart was quivering and she felt terrified from the bottom of her heart. She didn’t dare to go against him.","Biting her lip, she was just about to get up to change.","Suddenly, Li Moying’s brow creased and he stopped. Then he walked towards her.","Li Leyun was stunned but she suddenly jumped with joy. Li Moying walked next to her on his own. It was the first time she met with such a thing! Could it be that this man had finally seen how beautiful she was, compared with his human wife, and had a change of heart? Li Moying walked nearer and without saying a word, he stretched his hand out towards Li Leyun’s chest.","Her face flushed red. “Brother Moying, what are you doing...”","Li Tian Yi was totally stunned. His mind was in a mess, not knowing what his Young Master wanted to do!","Earlier, didn’t he view Li Leyun with disdain to the point that he couldn’t even tolerate her wearing the flowing dress? Why was he stretching his hand out to touch her breasts","now?","This... Was he overstimulated?","However, Li Moying seemed as though he didn’t notice their abnormality at all.","He stretched out his hand towards Li Leyun’s chest but he didn’t touch her at all. Instead, using two fingers, he picked up the small piece of a leaf which was stuck on her shirt.","No one noticed that Li Moying’s fingers were shaking slightly.","He took that piece of leaf and placed it under his nose to take a whiff. His expression which was cold like ice finally loosened a little.","This smell... was so familiar! It was obviously the scent of the fragrance sachet that his Li’er loved the most when she was in Soaring Heavens Continent!"]},{"number":2987,"title":"Chapter 2987 - Exclusive Fragrance (5)","paragraphs":["This incense was made using tender buds from the Lingering Pheromone Tree, which were then dried. It was a kind of condiment and a kind of plant that only Soaring Heavens Continent had.","Since her past life, Huang Yueli had been personally plucking the leaves to blend her fragrance sachet. She gave him quite a few sachets as well.","So, this scent was deeply etched in his mind. No matter how long time went by, he would never forget about it.","n","It was no wonder that when Li Leyun walked near to him today, he had accidentally mistaken her as Huang Yueli while he was drunk.","It wasn’t only because she was wearing Li’er’s favorite flowing dress, but mainly because a slight hint of Huang Yueli’s scent was on her as well.","But, why would Li Leyun have Huang Yueli’s scent?","Thinking of this, Li Moying’s gaze turned extremely cold. He stared at Li Leyun and hissed through gritted teeth, “This leaf... where did it come from?”","“Huh? W...What?”","Li Leyun still hadn’t recollected her senses.","She assumed that Li Moying was smitten by her but in the end, he didn’t even touch her at all. Instead, he took away a small piece of something from her that she hadn’t even seen clearly! Immediately following that, Li Moying started to interrogate her. She hadn’t even understood what he was trying to ask, so she naturally didn’t know how to answer him.","However, Li Moying wasn’t very patient. His heart was burning with anxiety, feeling both excited and fearful!","There wasn’t any Lingering Pheromone Tree in God Realm, so this leaf could only be brought from Soaring Heavens Continent. Among the newly ascended practitioners, only Huang Yueli came from there!","So he could practically confirm that Li Leyun and Huang Yueli had crossed each other’s path. Moreover, there was a 90% chance that it happened on her way here today!","Although that might be the case, he had already been disappointed multiple times previously. So this time, he didn’t dare to believe that he would be so lucky!","Li Moying looked at Li Leyun who was hemming and hawing and his fury got the better of him because of his anxiousness.","He raised his hand and grabbed Li Leyun’s collar, fiercely interrogating her, “Speak right now! When you came over earlier, who did you bump into? Why would this leaf fall on your shirt! Spill it out now!”","Li Leyun had never seen him acting in such a ferocious manner and she was frightened out of her wits!","It was until now that she realized that Li Moying had taken a piece of leaf from her shirt!","But she usually minded her image very much. As long as her shirt was tainted with a bit of dust, she would never wear it again. How could it be that a fingernail piece of leaf was stuck on her, and she didn’t even notice it?","Unless...","Li Leyun suddenly recalled the scuffle that she had with Huang Yueli earlier at the entrance.","She was in a hurry and bumped onto Huang Yueli, causing her to fall.","Back then, she fell quite badly!","This lead was either stuck onto her when she fell or it must have dropped from that stinky lad!","Li Moying’s gaze turned icy cold. Li Tian Yi was worried that he might really hurt their clan leader’s niece so he wanted to step up to persuade him. But he was in awe of the former’s aura and didn’t dare to go near at all.","Li Leyun was so scared that her teeth were chattering. She put on a brave front and said, “This should be... it should be something that I smeared at the courtyard entrance...”","“Courtyard entrance?” Li Moying frowned.","“Right. Earlier, I was... a young fellow intentionally tripped me, so I fell. Later on, we started to quarrel... this young fellow had obviously done it on purpose...”"]},{"number":2988,"title":"Chapter 2988 - Exclusive Fragrance (6)","paragraphs":["Li Leyun speedily explained the entire situation.","Lastly, she didn’t forget to intentionally badmouth Huang Yueli, hoping that Li Moying would be able to stand up for her and teach this stinky brat a lesson!","Whoever knew, Li Moying only heard the first part and loosened his grip, dashing out of the entrance.","“Young Master Moying, where are you going? Wait... Wait up!”","Li Tian Yi hurriedly chased after him.","Li Leyun slumped onto the floor, feeling all the energy in her body had been sucked dry within an instance!","Earlier, Li Moying looked simply too terrifying and scary!","Moreover, she didn’t even know how did she offend him!","Could the problem be that she had bumped into that stinky lad at the entrance earlier? Was Li Moying trying to take revenge for her by dashing out in a hurry?","If that was true, then the fright that she had gotten today was totally worth it!","She didn’t know how Li Yuehuang had offended Li Moying, but from his furious look, that lad would probably suffer in his hands!","Li Moying was currently extremely anxious. The speed of his footsteps increased to the point that he was almost about to fly!","Li Tian Yi brought a few guards along, chasing after him but they could not match his speed at all!","Li Yuehuang...","Weren’t those three words Huang Yueli in reverse?","Li Leyun also said that the young man was a Spiritual Armament Master, and he also had the Lingering Pheromone Tree’s leaf on him!","This person was definitely his Li’er. Otherwise, how could there be such a coincidental matter under this heavens!","As to the question of why he looked different from his gorgeous Li’er, that was very easy to explain. Huang Yueli had always been skilled in disguises and she had the top-tier Holy Armament, the Sky Phoenix Ring, which could conceal her cultivation.","No wonder Sacred Phoenix Race’s men couldn’t find her after such a long time of searching!","He knew that his Li’er had not died! She was alive and well, moreover, she was somewhere near him!","Thinking of this, Li Moying couldn’t wait to run over to Huang Yueli’s side and hug her tightly.","He used his fastest body movement Profound Skill and perfectly coordinated it with his thunder attributed Profound Energy, dashing out of the courtyard like a bolt of lightning.","There was naturally no one else at the entrance.","Li Moying used the shortest amount of time to go through all the streets in the surroundings. But he didn’t manage to find anyone like Huang Yueli.","Out of no choice, he could only stop and delve into his thoughts.","It had already been two hours after Li Leyun and Huang Yueli’s argument. Based on his little fox’s speed, she was able to go through half of Flame Square City within this amount of time.","Since she was no longer in the surroundings of these few streets, then it would become slightly difficult to find her.","Flame Square City’s paths led everywhere, so who knew which direction had she gone in?","In the time that he used to think, Li Tian Yi and the others finally chased up. Panting, they bowed respectfully to him.","“Young Master, you... where are you going!”","Li Moying frowned slightly and opened his mouth to say, “That Spiritual Armament Master who argued with Li Leyun is most likely Huang Yueli.”","“What??”","The guards were astounded.","No one expected to hear this piece of news.","After all, based on Li Leyun’s saying, that Spiritual Armament Master, who dared to argue with her so many times, was a man!","Li Moying didn’t bother to explain to them and asked directly, “Where is Li Leyun? Is she still in the courtyard?”"]},{"number":2989,"title":"Chapter 2989 - Where Did She Go? (1)","paragraphs":["“Ughh, oh, yes, yes!” The guards hurriedly responded.","Li Moying reacted instantly and immediately headed back to the courtyard in quick steps.","Now, the only person who possibly knew Huang Yueli’s whereabouts was Li Leyun.","Li Tian Yi and the others saw Li Moying leaving like a gust of wind and cried bitterly inwardly.","Whenever it had to do with this Sacred Phoenix Race’s young lady’s matters, their composed future clan leader would become extremely irritably. They totally couldn’t cope with his train of thoughts at all, so they could only follow behind him, running around like idiots","When Li Moying dashed into the courtyard, Li Leyun was still in a daze on the floor.","Seeing Li Moying running in again, she excitedly welcomed him. “Brother Moying, did you catch that stinky brat who bullied me? Is","he...”","Li Moying couldn’t be bothered to listen and asked directly, “Which direction did he take? Can you remember?”","“This...” Li Leyun was stumped.","When she and Huang Yueli parted ways, all she had on her mind was to meet Li Moying quickly. So she didn’t notice which direction Huang Yueli had gone to.","Li Moying waited for a couple of seconds and urged impatiently, “Where did he go? You argued with him for such a long time, didn’t you notice which direction did he went??”","Li Leyun was frightened by his anxious and fierce tone. Her thoughts were in a mess, and she totally could not recall the scenario at that moment.","When Li Moying saw this, his anger spiked up again, and he simply could not stop himself from wanting to hit her.","Luckily, Li Tian Yi and the others had already caught up to him. He stood behind Li Moying and weakly gave a reminder, “Young Master, This Subordinate was at the entrance earlier and I seem to have seen Huang... ughh... Young Master Li heading that way...”","Li Tian Yi pointed towards the east and Li Moying immediately stared at him. “Why didn’t you say so earlier!”","Saying that, he didn’t wait for Li Tian Yi to explain and left in a gust of wind again.","Li Tian Yi wanted to cry because he felt aggrieved!","OVP","He wanted to explain, but whoever knew his Young Master’s body movement Profound Skill to be so incredible! As compared to the latter’s performance in the Cloudy Qilin clan, his speed had almost doubled!","Ila","In a blink of an eye, he was already gone without a trace. Li Tian Yi chased after him with all his might, to the verge of throwing up blood, but was still unable to chase up to Li Moying...","“Senior Brother Tian Yi, what’s going on? Why is Brother Moying in such a hurry? Did that Li Yuehuang offend Brother Moying? It’s just like what I said, that stinky brat is so bold. As a lowly human, how dare he offend us Cloudy Qilin clan, simply digging his own grave! After Brother Moying finds him, he must teach that brat a lesson!” Li Leyun walked over as she spoke with deep hatred.","Li Tian Yi swept a glance at her. “If you don’t wish to be beaten to death by Young Master, it’s better to stop bad mouthing Young Master","Li!”","Li Leyun didn’t expect him to say that and was stunned momentarily, “Huh? Why? He’s just a lowly human!”","Li Tian Yi saw how ignorant she was and didn’t bother to persuade her any further. Anyway, he had already fulfilled his duty to remind Li Leyun. Since she didn’t heed his advice, it had nothing to do with him!","The most important matter now was to quickly find Li Moying!","Thinking of this, he hurriedly led his men and ran out again.","Flame Square City’s paths were built in an extremely structured manner.","Li Tian Yi headed towards the east. Although he didn’t have Li Moying’s speed, he wasn’t worried that he might lose track of him."]},{"number":2990,"title":"Chapter 2990 - Where Did She Go? (2)","paragraphs":["But Li Tian Yi believed that Li Moying would definitely search while he walked. But in the end, Li Moying shuttered past various streets and only stopped when he reached the foot of the east city wall.","Li Tian Yi and the others stopped behind Li Moying, panting heavily.","“Young... Young Master! There were several bustling streets along the way where we passed by earlier, and... and there are some inns. If Young Miss Huang was in Flame Square City, it is possible that she might stop at those places. We... should we turn back and take a look?” Li Tian Er suggested.","Li Moying only shook his head.","Lifting his head, he looked in the distance away, at the teleportation array which was heavily guarded by hundreds of soldiers. The gaze in his bewitching plum blossom eyes turned serene and deep. “No need, since Li’er walked towards the east, she had most probably come here.” He replied in a deep voice.","“Huh?” The guards widened their eyes, not understanding why Li Moying was so certain.","Li Moying didn’t bother to explain. In reality, he didn’t know how to explain.","This was his instinct. Or perhaps, it was because he had enough understanding towards Huang Yueli. That was why he could make a precise deduction on her actions.","His Li’er wasn’t interested in the reputation as a Spiritual Armament Master. The reason why she went to Sky Gem Glass Chamber and had a conflict with Li Leyun was most probably because she wanted to obtain the Spiritual Armament Master’s badge to derive at a certain","aim.","This aim was very easy to guess. It was because she wanted to use the teleportation array.","Huang Yueli should have been attacked by someone. Even under the protection of the Sacred Phoenix Race’s Elder, she was heavily injured and went missing.","Moreover, after she managed to escape, she didn’t show herself directly. Instead, she put on a disguise and appeared in Flame Square City, pulling wool over those people’s eyes.","This meant that his Li’er had met with an extremely powerful enemy, and that was why she acted so cautiously, not daring to give the game away.","Hence, according to Huang Yueli’s usual behavior, she would not choose to stay long in Flame Square City. Instead, she would hurry towards a safe place.","She didn’t know anyone in God Realm so there were only two places that she could go to.","One was Ice Moon Summit, which was where Sacred Phoenix Continent’s lineage was. The other... was where he was, the Cloudy Qilin Continent!","But he didn’t know what choice would Huang Yueli make in the end?","Just as Li Moying was pondering over this, the soldiers near the teleportation array discovered their existence and strode over. “Who are you guys? So many of you lingering near the military zone, what are your motives?”","The team leader eyes them suspiciously. The lot of them held their weapons with both hands tightly, showing a guarded look.","This group of people was dressed luxuriously and their cultivation levels were extremely outstanding, especially the leader, Li Moying. His countenance was handsome and his temperament was noble. Just one look and they could tell that he was an aristocrat.","When this kind of person appeared near the teleportation array, it was impossible for them to take the wrong direction and get lost!","Li Tian Yi hurriedly walked up. “This buddy, my Young Master is here to look for someone. May I ask... did a Spiritual Armament Master surnamed Li come by earlier?”","The soldier’s face was even more bewildered, “Why are you asking about this?”","“Ughh, this...”","Li Tian Yi was indeed a Cloudy Qilin clan’s talented practitioner. His thoughts raced swiftly and he soon found an excuse.","“My Young Master and Master Li have been great buddies for many years.”"]},{"number":2991,"title":"Chapter 2991 - Where Did She Go? (3)","paragraphs":["“We unintentionally found out that Master Li was in Flame Square City today, so we thought of coming to catch up with him. Whoever knew that Master Li just happened to leave today, so the two of them just missed each other! So, that’s why my Young Master specially rushed over here, hoping that he could meet with Master Li!”","Seeing the team leader not saying anything, Li Tian Yi added, “Young Master Li saved my Young Master previously, so he’s Young Master’s savior! They haven’t met for many years and if they missed this chance, who knows when the next chance might come by!”","The team leader finally believed Li Tian Yi after hearing him speak so earnestly.","“The Master Li you are talking about, is he a low rank Spiritual Armament Master who is around the age of 30?”.","Li Tian Yi saw Huang Yueli’s countenance previously so he kept nodding his head. “That’s right! That’s him! Young Master Li isn’t very tall, but his looks are rather attractive. He’s also a little tanned.”","Hearing his apt description, the team leader let down his guard.","He shook his head regretfully, “Sigh, the person you are describing is indeed Master Li Yuehuang! Alas, you have just missed him! Master Li had just left Flame Square City a quarter of an hour ago!” “What? That’s impossible!”","Hearing that, Li Moying could no longer suppress his anger.","His expression was originally cold and solemn, but his darkened expression made it look even more callous and imposing.","The team leader’s knees almost gave way when he saw Li Moying’s expression. But he braced himself and said, “Why would I lie to you? Master Li had indeed left.”","“How is that possible?” Li Tian Yi saw his Young Master on the verge of flying into a rage and hurriedly stood out to ask on his behalf. “Activating the teleportation array requires a lot of energy. Just redrawing out the array patterns and preparing the exhaustive materials for the array would take two to three days, isn’t it? How could he leave so quickly?”","As a genius from the Cloudy Qilin clan, Li Tian Yi used the teleportation array frequently and he was extremely clear about the situation for this.","It was exactly because there were so many restrictions using the teleportation array which was why those important figured from genuine large clans rarely used it. Instead, they frequently used flying ships. The team leader immediately explained, “This was because Master Li came at a convenient timing. There were a few ancient god clan practitioners who also wanted to use the teleportation array and we were already preparing for it a few days ago. Since Master Li came, he teleported along with them.”","“What? How. Could it be so coincidental! Are you certain that they’re already teleported? Will it be too late to stop the teleportation now...”","Before Li Tian Yi could finish his sentence, Li Moying’s figure swayed and he had already dashed past the group of people into the teleportation array. “Young Master—!!” Li Tian Yi cried out in shock!","All the soldiers hadn’t realized what had happened until Li Tian Yi cried out, and they recovered their senses.","All of them looked horrified!","Li Moying’s body movements were even more erratic than a ghost!","There were so many soldiers here and they had surrounded Li Moying and the others. But he still managed to break through their encirclement effortlessly!","In fact, all the soldiers did not even see his figure. They only saw a shadow flash past them and he was gone!","“Young Master, you can’t do that! The teleportation is currently in progress, and it’s extremely, extremely dangerous!”","Li Tian Yi paled with fright and hurriedly chased after him.","He really didn’t expect that whenever something was related to Huang Yueli, Li Moying would change into another person!"]},{"number":2992,"title":"Chapter 2992 - Where Did She Go? (4)","paragraphs":["His usual calm and stable demeanor were totally gone.","He didn’t even cherish his own life.","The teleportation array was an array that tore the space apart. Once activated, it was very difficult to stop. For those who tried to barge in while it was already in the middle of being activated, the intruders might be swept into an infinite void space. The worst scenario was that they might be torn into shreds by the space’s storm!","Alas, Li Tian Yi’s speed just couldn’t match up to his Young Master.","He had just run for a few hundred meters and Li Moying’s figure had already appeared in the middle of the teleportation array.","“Damnit! Li’er had indeed just left!” Li Moying’s fist punched heavily on the patterned round stone pillar by the side.","The materials used to construct teleportation arrays were top-quality Spiritual Armament materials in God Realm. There was no need to doubt the quality of the hardness. But Li Moying’s punch caused multiple cracks in the entire pillar.","“Cr-ac-k...”","After several dull sounds, the entire stone pillar shattered into a pile of rubble beside his feet.","“Hey, how can you guys damage...” At this moment, the commander who was in charge of the teleportation array heard the soldiers’ report and hurried over. He just happened to see Li Moying punch the circular stone pillar! The commander immediately shouted to berate him. Just as he was about to give them a stern lecture, it took less than a second for him to see the stone pillar sh... shattering... The commander’s voice suddenly stopped as though something was stuck in his throat, totally unable to say a single word at all! This... what kind of ability was this!","Terrifying! Too terrifying! “Could it be that a Dao Profound Realm strong exponent had come to our Flame Square City?”","“But doesn’t this young man look a little too young? How could his cultivation possibly be in Dao Profound Realm? Or could it be that he had used some secret arts to conceal his real age?”","Li Moying heard a voice and looked at the commander, then he walked towards the latter.","“You... you... who on earth are... are...” The commander stared at Li Moying, but under his strong might, he couldn’t even say a complete sentence. Li Moying asked, “That Master Li... where is the destination that he had teleported to?”","When the commander heard this question, he looked at Li Moying defensively and asked, “You... Why are you asking this? It’s... it’s a military secret about the use of the teleportation array! I will never tell you!”","Li Moying’s brows creased and his Profound Energy was instantly unleashed! “Oof...”","The commander’s meridians and dantian suffered an intense impact and blood gushed up his throat, causing him to almost throw up blood!","His chest was in severe bouts of pain, which made him unable to breathe!","Li Moying asked coldly, “Where did Li Yuehuang go to? Quickly tell me! I’m not very patient today!","He retracted a bit of Profound Energy and the commander finally found himself able to breathe slightly.","But he clenched his teeth and said, “No... no way, I won’t tell you! How dare you openly attack Sacred Phoenix Continent’s guards, to force me to tell you about the military secret! I will absolutely not yield to you!”","The commander looked at Li Moying suspiciously, as though he was the demon tribe’s spy!","Li Tian Yi took a look and he was worried that Li Moying might kill the commander and soldiers in a fit of anger!","He stepped up and persuaded. “Young Master, you...”","Li Moying heard his voice and stretched out a hand, indicating for him to keep quiet."]},{"number":2993,"title":"Chapter 2993 - Empyrean Fox Continent, Blessed City (1)","paragraphs":["Immediately following that, Li Moying’s fingers flipped, and he retrieved a token from his interspatialring. “Now, can you answer me?”","An icy, cold voice rang, and the commander’s mind “buzzed” as though he heard a thunderclap, which caused him to go into a trance.","Li Moying’s slender, powerful fingers were entwined with a metal attributed chain. Below the chain was an exquisite identity token.","This was something that ancient god clans used to differentiate their clansmen!","At the same time, it was a sign of a god clan’s noble status.","The commander hadn’t expected the handsome, young man standing in front of him to be a noble member of the god clan. Moreover, from his cultivation and the number of guards following him, the former was able to judge that Li Moying’s status in the clan wasn’t low at all!","However, this wasn’t the most shocking thing.","What left the commander in disbelief was that Li Moying was from the Cloudy Qilin clan!","Why had Cloudy Qilin clan’s men come to Sacred Phoenix Race?","Various large continent’s patrolling guards weren’t able to stop a genuine top expert from the god clan, but it was impossible to totally differentiate people from the Cloudy Qilin clan.","However, various ancient god clans had their pride.","Sacred Phoenix Race and Cloudy Qilin clan were at loggerheads for such a long time. Even if they didn’t restrict the other party’s clansmen to enter the Continent on which they were governed, the other party wouldn’t enter it casually. Instead, they would choose to ignore each other.","So, why did this man appear at this place? The commander stared blankly at Li Moying’s identity token and couldn’t say a word for a long time.","Li Tian Yi was worried that his Young Master would fly into a rage again and hurriedly scolded the commander, “Why are you in a daze? Aren’t you going to tell us clearly where Li Yuehuang, Master Li, had gone to!”","An ancient god clan’s identity was much higher than ordinary clansmen. Moreover, even if it was based on military ranks, once god clans entered the battle, the basic rank they hold was sufficient to control him, a human commander.","The human commander didn’t dare to dawdle and hurriedly said, “Master Li’s destination is Empyrean Fox Continent, Blessed City!”","“What? Blessed City??”","Hearing that, Li Moying’s guards all had a huge fright!","“Blessed City was the most dangerous warzones in the entire God Realm. Why would Young Master Moying’s wife go to that place?” “Logically speaking, shouldn’t she be heading to Sacred Phoenix Continent’s central, Ice Moon Summit, back to her clan?”","Li Tian Yi frowned and asked, “Are you sure? Why would Master Li go to Blessed City for no reason?”","“This... I’m not too sure. I told Master Li that Blessed City is a troubled spot and is extremely dangerous, but he insisted on going there. I... I can’t stop him at all!”","Li Tian Yi and the others exchanged a glance, feeling very uneasy. “This was such an abnormal situation. Had Huang Yueli met with trouble? If this was the case, won’t our Young Master go crazy?”","The few of them sized Li Moying up cautiously but found that Li Moying’s expression seemed even more relaxed than earlier.","“The teleportation distance is the furthest from Sacred Phoenix Continent to Empyrean Fox Continent, having to pass through two large continents. Moreover, Blessed City has an even longer teleportation array. If he wanted to go to Cloudy Qilin Continent, taking this route will save a lot of time...”","Li Moying muttered to himself for a moment and his tightly creased forehead slowly eased.","“Li’er, you have indeed chosen to look for me!”","Li Moying’s heart seemed as though it was soaked in lukewarm water, which was filled with warmth."]},{"number":2994,"title":"Chapter 2994 - Empyrean Fox Continent, Blessed City (2)","paragraphs":["After being separated for more than a year, his Li’er was also thinking of him. She couldn’t wait to meet him at all...","Li Moying kept his identity token and abruptly turned to leave.","“Enough, let’s go!” Saying that he led the way to leave.","Since he already knew that Huang Yueli was on her way to look for him, and roughly knew about her route, then he could rest assured.","Although it was not impossible to head to Empyrean Fox Continent through the teleportation array, the amount of time needed to prepare the teleportation array’s materials for activation would take almost one whole day.","Li Moying could not even bear to wait for an hour right now, what more to wait for an entire day!","Luckily, the flying ship that he brought out from the Cloudy Qilin clan was still parked outside Sacred Phoenix Continent in a hidden location. So taking the flying ship would be much faster than the teleportation array. Perhaps, he might even arrive in Blessed City earlier than Huang Yueli.","By then, he would be able to welcome his Li’er.","He started to wonder about the adorable expression that Huang Yueli would show when she saw him appearing suddenly at the instant when she walked out of the teleportation array.","Li Moying’s lips couldn’t help but curl upwards when he imagined the scene.","As for Huang Yueli, she was suddenly in the middle of being teleported. Hence she totally didn’t know that so much had happened in this short amount of time that she had left.","There were a total of five people who were being teleported.","Among them, there were four ancient god clan practitioners. Judging from their aura they seemed to be from the Empyrean Fox Clan. Moreover, from the obvious military ranks on their shoulders, one could tell that they had attained outstanding military achievements on the battlefield.","O","Other than that, there was a luxuriously dressed young man.","His countenance was extremely handsome and even a little feminine. But his temperament was outstanding. An eminent aura was overflowing from him, even though he was just standing there.","When he saw Huang Yueli walking in, his lips curled into a smile with a frivolous hint to it.","Huang Yueli shot him a warning gaze and did not engage in conversation. Instead, she looked for an unremarkable position and sat in a cross-legged position.","This was long-distance teleportation so they would not arrive instantly. They had to teleport across two continents so the minimum amount of time taken to travel within the void space would be around three days or so. She would be able to take this time to adjust herself.","When the Empyrean Fox clan’s practitioners saw Huang Yueli walking in, all of them frowned.","“What’s going on? Why did a human walk in?” One of them questioned. The team leader who led Huang Yueli bowed and apologized. “Master Divine Lieutenant, I’m really sorry. This Young Master Li happened to be heading to Blessed City as well. Since it’s so coincidental, why don’t we just let him teleport together! He will not disturb you.” Empyrean Fox Clan’s practitioners looked displeased and they said, “What’s the situation? The cities administered by Sacred Phoenix Race are really lawless! The teleportation arrays were built to fight against the demon tribe, and we’re heading to Blessed City to carry out important military affairs. Why are we bringing these two trashy humans along for? Simply a waste of resources! Aren’t you going to get them to scram right now!” The team leader smiled apologetically and said, “Masters, please be appeased! We didn’t casually let anyone come in. These two gentlemen here, one is a Spiritual Alchemist, and the other is a Spiritual Armament Master. Even on the battlefield frontline, they are useful people. Sirs, please let it go and let them tag along.”","Hearing that, the Empyrean Fox Clan practitioners’ expressions turned slightly better."]},{"number":2995,"title":"Chapter 2995 - Empyrean Fox Continent, Blessed City (3)","paragraphs":["In the God Realm, one’s birth might be important. But one’s strength and ability mattered even more!","Spiritual Alchemists and Spiritual Armament Masters were occupations that God Realm admired very much. These two people with these statuses made the Empyrean Fox Clan practitioners unable to say words of rejection. “Since that is so, let them tag along then! Have the resources for the teleportation been prepared? Quick, don’t waste time. We have already been delayed in Flame Square City for so many days!”","“Yes, yes, the teleportation is almost about to start. Masters, will you please sit near the array eye, in case you are injured by the impact when the array activates! During the process of teleportation, everyone, please do not attempt to stand up. The resistance in the void space is very huge and once it has surpassed the array’s boundary, you might be thrown out. By then, it’s possible to be swept into the space’s storm which is life-threatening! Even if you manage to stay alive, there’s no way to arrive at the destination properly. Moreover, no one knows where you might land! So, please be very careful!” The team leader warned repeatedly.","The Empyrean Fox practitioners were rather impatient and snorted coldly, “Do we even need your reminder? It’s not the first time we’re using the teleportation array! Quick, make haste!”","The team leader nodded his head and bowed as he backed out. Apparently, he didn’t dare offend these high and mighty god clan practitioners.","Huang Yueli was listening and felt that she had gained more knowledge.","The things that the team leader said were not written in the books which she had read. These warnings to her were rather useful. After the team leader left, the remaining five people also sat down just like Huang Yueli.","But the Empyrean Fox Clan’s practitioners didn’t want to mingle with humans, so they especially sat opposite Huang Yueli.","On the contrary, the frivolous-looking handsome man walked directly towards Huang Yueli and sat next to her.","Huang Yueli felt that he was a little too close for comfort and couldn’t help but nudge to the side.","But, she didn’t think too much about it. She assumed that the other party thought that she was also from the human race, so he wanted to get on closer terms with her.","But not too long later, after the exterior array patterns had been activated, the entire teleportation array started to vibrate violently!","A huge light sphere enveloped the six of them and the bursts of energy waves scuttered towards them from the outside. All the surrounding Heaven and Earth Profound Qi gathered towards the direction of the teleportation array!","The light sphere was turning brighter and brighter and even more eye-piercing!","Finally, after a wave of explosive sounds, a light pillar shot into the sky from the teleportation array’s position!","This enormous, powerful energy that had gathered through the array instantly exploded and tore the void space apart!","Huang Yueli and the others were also pushed into the void space along with the light pillar.","In this instance, the explosion of the energy caused the ground to shake. The magnitude of it was too huge and even Huang Yueli felt dizzy from it.","She hurriedly sat cross-legged, shut her eyes, and silently worked up the “Nine Phoenix Transformations” cultivation method.","The disorderly Profound Energy within her body was slowly being directed into the correct path, and Huang Yueli’s pale complexion turned normal.","She slowly opened her eyes to discover that the six of them were already in a void space.","The surroundings were pitch-black, and the sparkling stars were shining brightly, like diamonds on black velvet, which gave off a vague kind of beauty.","They were enveloped in the light ball, and it portrayed various kinds of array patterns.","Huang Yueli took a look and discovered that the majority of these array patterns were mostly defensive and speed arrays."]},{"number":2996,"title":"Chapter 2996 - 6 Empyrean Fox Continent, Blessed City (4)","paragraphs":["Other than her, Empyrean Fox Clan’s practitioners were also cultivating in a cross-legged position.","Their eyelids didn’t even move, totally immersed in their world. Apparently, they were already used to teleportation and didn’t find it novel at all.","However, the human man next to Huang Yueli kept sizing her up with his eyes peeled.","This glare was too direct and it made Huang Yueli feel a little offended.","She turned around and looked at him coldly, secretly releasing a bit of Profound Energy pressure, hoping to strike the other party in awe.","Whoever knew, that man seemed as though he didn’t feel any pressure at all. Not only did he not show any pained expression, but his lips also curled up with a playful look in his eyes.","“Both of us are humans. Aren’t you a little... too much by doing this?”","Huang Yueli’s brows twitched in surprise.","This man looked as though he was just in the tenth stage realm. At most, his cultivation would be in Dream Profound Realm mid-phase. She didn’t expect him to not bat an eyelid under her suppression.","It seemed that he had either concealed his real cultivation, or he should have met with some kind of extraordinary encounter and wasn’t an ordinary person... Huang Yueli didn’t bother about this at all.","Because she didn’t feel any murderous or evil intentions from him. Rather, he was just curious about her.","Although that was the case, Huang Yueli felt that it was necessary to warn him.","“I’m not on close terms with you, can you please stay a little further away from me! I also want to cultivate!”","Saying that she stood up and walked a rather far distance away from the man before she sat down. Then she shut her eyes and instantly started to cultivate.","The man rubbed his nose dully, but there wasn’t any embarrassed look on his face at all.","The only human companion here ignored him. Helpless, he could only sit down and cultivate quietly.","The teleportation light sphere traveled steadily in the void space. It was extremely quiet on the outside.","Time passed tranquility in this manner and three days went by very swiftly.","The leader of the Empyrean Fox Clan’s practitioners suddenly opened his eyes. “It’d take another one hour or so and we would be arriving at Blessed City!”","“That’s great! The amount of time we spent traveling this time is much longer than expected. Finally, we’re heading back to Blessed City.”","“Isn’t that so? I can’t get used to eating the food in Sacred Phoenix Continent. If we still don’t come back, I’m not going to be able to take it any longer!”","Amid the joyous discussions, the elder leader coughed heavily.","“Enough, is there a need to be so happy? We came back to Blessed City this time not to come back to visit our relatives or to go have fun! The demon tribe had been showing up frequently around Blessed City and had already attacked the neighboring few towns and cities recently. A large number of humans had been captured, and they died from having their blood essence sucked dry! There are quite a number of our Empyrean Fox Clan’s clansmen as well! After we go back, we must immediately enter into Level 1 state of readiness!”","Hearing that, those Empyrean Fox Clan’s practitioners revealed worried expressions.","“In the past, the demon tribe would have activity during winter. Why have they started to create chaos so early this year?”","“I think something’s strange about this!”","“The clan sent us a message that the demon tribe that attacked Blessed City this time has quite several Sky Devil rank exponents. They have probably come with ill intentions!”","Whilst the few of them were talking, the light sphere that enveloped them suddenly gave off a burst of bright light, and the vigorous vibrations started once again!","Huang Yueli immediately shut her eyes to adjust her breathing.","It seemed that they had already arrived near Blessed City, and they were about to leave the void space!"]},{"number":2997,"title":"Chapter 2997 - Shameless Plan (1)","paragraphs":["The vibration of the light sphere that tore past the sky of the void space boundary lasted for a very long time.","Huang Yueli waited quietly.","She knew that Blessed City’s teleportation array had already been activated. After the light sphere appeared from the void space, it would be pulled in and gradually descend on the designated position.","Finally, the vibrations gradually grew weaker.","NV","Huang Yueli squinted and half of the sphere had already appeared on the exterior of the void space...","But just at this moment, “Rumble...”","A loud noise resounded and the light sphere vibrated once again!","Moreover, this time, the situation was very unusual. Strong crashing noises, shattering noises kept ringing. The light sphere no longer swayed simply to the left and the right. Instead, it shook in all directions without any regulated pattern.","The six people in the light sphere were unable to sit tight. All of them fell onto the floor, covered in dirt.","“What’s going on? What exactly happened?”","The Empyrean Fox Clan’s practitioners detected the abnormality and the colors on their faces changed. The Leader of the pack spoke gravely, “The situation is not wise. We... seem to be attacked by the demon tribe!” “What? How could we be so unlucky!”","“The demon tribe is simply too sinister!”","“We’re done for, we’re done for! The exterior defense is the weakest when the light sphere passes through the boundary of the void space. Based on the intensity of this attack, our light sphere would be broken very quickly!”","“What should we do? The demon tribe came prepared. It seemed that they sent out a lot of people to besiege us!”","Huang Yueli frowned slightly as she looked straight out of the light sphere.","Rays of different attributed energy crashed on the light sphere.","The difference between this energy and ordinary Heaven and Earth Profound Qi was that there was a rampant and irascible presence hidden inside.","Every single impact made the light sphere’s glow darken a little. The array patterns drawn on the light sphere were already blurry and unclear, as though it had completely lost its effect.","“Could this be the demon tribe’s demonic power? It is indeed extremely powerful and the destructive power is shocking...”","“Although the demon tribe can’t construct long-distance teleportation arrays, their destructive power is much stronger than ours!” A voice on Huang Yueli’s right sounded.","She looked up and saw that human Spiritual Alchemist, who had already walked next to her.","Detecting Huang Yueli’s gaze, he blinked and said, “This Young Master, I feel that the both of us are about to run into bad luck!”","“What do you mean?” Huang Yueli went blank.","She instinctively felt what the man said was a little strange. If it was about bad luck, the six of them were apparently in a huge crisis. But this person emphasized “the two of them” were going to run into bad luck...","Putting it in that way, was to convey their contempt towards the god clan, or...? While Huang Yueli was still pondering, she suddenly sensed that something was amiss.","The four Empyrean Fox Clan practitioners had always turned around and looked at Huang Yueli and that young man in an uncomfortable gaze.","“Hey, you two humans!” The elderly leader shouted in an unfriendly manner.","Huang Yueli and the human Spiritual Alchemist shut their mouths tacitly, ignoring the other party. The elderly man’s expression turned ghastly. “That Spiritual Alchemist and that Spiritual Armament Master, I’m calling the both of you! What kind of attitude is this?”","The human man dug his ear and said slowly, “Oh, so you’re calling us...”"]},{"number":2998,"title":"Chapter 2998 - Shameless Plan (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 2998 Shameless Plan (2)","“Yes, the both of you. Stop your pretense!” A young Empyrean Fox clan practitioner lost his patience and was about to rush up to scold them.","The Elder leading them hurriedly pulled him back, made eye contact with him, and indicated for him to stay calm.","The young practitioner regained his senses and shut his mouth.","Huang Yueli was even more bewildered. From their actions, it seemed as though there was some sort of scheme...","She blinked and said indifferently, “This young buddy here is right. We have names, so what do you mean by ‘two humans’? Even if you don’t know our names, you should know that we are a Spiritual Armament Master and a Spiritual Alchemist. Greeting us as Masters should be the basic courtesy, isn’t it!”","“Just you two! Did you think you deserved to be addressed as Masters by our Divine Lieutenant??” The young practitioners almost flew into a rage again.","The Elder coughed slightly and opened his mouth to say, “Both Masters, please accept This Lieutenant’s apology! We’re now under attack by the demon tribe and the light sphere is about to shatter, so there’s no time to waste! This Lieutenant wishes to discuss something with the both of you...”","“Hoho...” The human man sneered and revealed a mocking expression. Huang Yueli asked coldly, “What is it about?”","Empyrean Fox clan’s Elder said, “The demon tribe’s attack is so strong. If we fight against them, we are absolutely not their match. Hence, if we wish to arrive at Blessed City’s human gathering point, the only way is to increase the advancing speed of the light sphere. We have to make sure that we pass through the void space boundary before the light sphere shatters completely and reach Blessed City’s teleportation array’s connection point...”","Speaking to this point, the Elder paused and his gaze swept past Huang Yueli and the other human practitioner. He was anticipating to pique their curiosity, hoping that they would continue to ask.","Whoever knew, the both of them just looked at him coldly without saying a word.","Hence he could only cough and overcome the awkwardness, then continue to talk on his","own.","“You’re not an array master, so you probably don’t know the principle of the teleportation array. This teleportation array speed is related to the number of people inside the light sphere. Although six people isn’t a lot, it would still affect the speed. If there are only four people left, the speed would instantly be raised by 50%! By then, there would be sufficient time to pass through the void space boundary!”","The Empyrean Fox clan’s Elder was so thick-skinned that he voiced out his shameless plan.","At the same time, he looked at Huang Yueli and the others with great expectation and chuckled. “Both of you, do you think... this idea is doable?”","Huang Yueli smiled. “Are you done?”","“Cough cough, I’m done! Both...”","The Empyrean Fox Clan’s elderly words were interrupted by the human man’s sneer.","“Divine Lieutenant, your idea is really ‘great’! I just want to ask, if we take away two people, are these two people going to jump out from the light sphere themselves? The demon tribe is outside right now. If they jump out, will they still be able to survive?” “Ughh... this... about this...”","The Empyrean Fox Clan Elder didn’t think that he would be so direct. So for a moment in time, he had nothing to say to it.","There was no way that he didn’t know that those two people would be attacked by the demon tribe if they were to jump out. Moreover, they could possibly die immediately.","But to him, his clansmen and his own lives were apparently much more valuable than Huang Yueli and the other man.","He totally didn’t care about other people’s life or death at all.","But the human man said it so frankly that it made him feel awkward."]},{"number":2999,"title":"Chapter 2999 - Shameless Plan (3)","paragraphs":["Just as the Elder kept silent, Huang Yueli’s lips curled and suddenly gave a soft laugh.","“Young buddy, we don’t need to worry if the person who jumps out will be able to survive or not! Since Divine Lieutenant has decided to jump down, he would definitely have a plan to save his skin! I didn’t expect there to be such noble people in this world. He’s willing to sacrifice himself to save other people’s lives!”","Saying that, she showed a touched look at the Empyrean Fox Clan’s Elder.","“Divine Lieutenant, today you’re offered to jump out of the light sphere to save our lives. We will never forget your kindness! When we reach Blessed City, we will definitely spread the word about you and Empyrean Fox Clan’s merits to all of God Realm’s practitioners, about your noble sentiments of thinking primarily about others!”","Hearing what Huang Yueli said, the human practitioner next to her couldn’t keep it in, and burst out in laughter! “Cough cough, that’s right, that’s right! All of you are indeed from the ancient god clans. No wonder your moral characters are so noble. We, humans, are indeed humbled. Thank you all of you, we’re really very grateful to you!” He also played dumb.","The human man’s gaze landed on Huang Yueli, as his interest in her grew deeper.","Originally, his instincts had already told him that this fellow human wasn’t as ordinary as he looked. From this incident, he was indeed much more interesting than what he had imagined.","When the Empyrean Fox Clan’s Elder heard that, he almost spat out a mouthful of blood!","Empyrean Fox Clan’s practitioners had obviously hinted Huang Yueli and the man to sacrifice themselves. However they were too embarrassed to say it outright, hence they didn’t manage to tell them immediately. Huang Yueli intentionally twisted the understanding of their meaning, claiming that they were prepared to sacrifice themselves and jump out!","This indebted look was so sincere and her acting skills had simply reached perfection.","She had just passed the buck back to them so it was not impossible for Empyrean Fox Clan’s practitioners to hint them to jump down!","Huang Yueli and the man had already made it clear that they were waiting for them to jump!","The scene had turned extremely awkward.","Empyrean Fox Clan’s practitioner’s face was flushed and he was extremely furious, but he couldn’t think of a way to continue with this topic.","He couldn’t pull down his face due to his seniority but the younger Empyrean Fox Clan’s practitioners didn’t have that many misgivings.","The young practitioners beside him wanted to berate these two lowly humans earlier but he was stopped by the Elder.","Now, he could no longer keep his anger in and stepped forward, staring fiercely at Huang Yueli and the human Spiritual Alchemist. “Enough, stop this gibberish! Why are you two human trash putting up an act? You want us to jump down? We are from the noble ancient god clan, why should we jump? If someone is to jump, it should naturally be you two humans!”","Huang Yueli’s smile instantly vanished.","Crossing her arms, she said coldly, “We’re not idiots, so why would we dig our own graves? Then why don’t you jump down yourself? You’re having such a beautiful dream, does your mother know about it?”","“You—!!”","She talked back at the Empyrean Fox Clan practitioner and the expression on his face turned ghastly!","“You humans have low abilities and are protected by the god clans, which is why you can survive the demon tribe’s attacks! Now, we’re just asking you to make a little bit of sacrifice, and you’re giving so many excuses! Simply ungrateful!”","The other Empyrean Fox Clan’s practitioner walked up and bragged unblushingly."]},{"number":3000,"title":"Chapter 3000 - Shameless Plan (4)","paragraphs":["The coldness in Huang Yueli’s eyes grew deeper. “What’s wrong with the human clan? Didn’t the humans fight against the demon tribe, or didn’t they bleed or sacrifice themselves? God clan enjoys countless resources which are the fruits of the humans’ hard work! If it wasn’t for the humans who are feeding you in the lands that you rule, do you think you can concentrate on cultivating? You’re hoping to have countless resources to be supplied so that you can easily advance?”","Huang Yueli’s anger suddenly arose when she heard that shameless speech!","Ever since she arrived at God Realm, she realized that God Realm’s ancient god clans are indeed as powerful as what the legends claimed. But they were also as conceited as they could be!","Although she was also a part of the ancient god clan, she totally could not stand the way they talked or showed contempt towards the humans.","The human man was standing next to her and kept nodding his head, as his eyes were filled with admiration towards Huang Yueli.","But to the Empyrean Fox Clan’s practitioners, it was extremely ear-piercing!","They were used to acting high and mighty, assuming that their lives were much nobler than humans.","Now that they were in danger, they felt that it was these two humans’ glory to sacrifice themselves for them!","Whoever knew that these two punks actually pointed at their noses and were unwilling to coordinate with them!","Thinking of this, the Empyrean Fox Clan’s practitioners tore away their remaining hypocrisy.","The Elder said gloomily, “Don’t bother to haggle with them! The light sphere can’t take it any longer! Humans, today, you have no other choice... but to jump! If you are willing to jump, This Lieutenant can note down your name and give you a title for sacrificing yourselves which would benefit your family. Otherwise, This Lieutenant can only do you a favor and send you off!”","Saying that, he waved his right hand. The remaining three Empyrean Fox Clan’s practitioners swarmed up and unleashed the Profound Energy within them, with a threatening posture.","It was apparent that if Huang Yueli and the man dared to say “no”, they intended to use brute force to coerce the two of them to comply.","Huang Yueli squinted her eyes and stood rooted to the ground. There weren’t any flustered emotions within her at all.","From the moment that Elder opened his mouth, she had already sensed that there would be no way to avoid today’s battle!","Under a life-threatening situation, Empyrean Fox Clan’s practitioners would absolutely shred all pretenses of cordiality.","But facing these four practitioners, combining herself and the human Spiritual Alchemist beside her, the former’s total combat power was much higher than theirs.","The Elder was in the Heart Profound Realm end-phase and the three younger practitioners were in the Dream Profound Realm mid-phase.","Based on cultivation alone, none of them were weaker than Huang Yueli.","Whereas on Huang Yueli’s side...","She subconsciously swept a glance at that human Spiritual Alchemist.","This person seemed as though he was only in the tenth stage realm, or at most, he was in the Dream Profound Realm early-phase.","Combining their powers, they were totally not the four Empyrean Fox Clan’s practitioners match!","Just at this moment, the light sphere started vibrating once again. Moreover, the tremors grew stronger, simply no different from an earthquake.","The demon tribe had evidently realized that the light sphere was on the brink of collapse, so their attacks became even more rampant.","Bursts of demonic power crashed against the light sphere continuously.","The small light sphere was like a small boat in a rampant thunderstorm, which might face the danger of capsizing at any moment.","There were six people in the light sphere, and they were caught off-guard. All of them lost their balance and rolled onto the ground. Even the Heart Profound Realm elderly man wasn’t spared.","Moreover, as the ground kept swaying, they weren’t able to climb up after they fell."]}]);
